hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15001","14962 - Narrated to us Humayd ibn Abi Makhlad al-Wasiti, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarai narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Safwan showed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, that Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam sought permission to see al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf, but the gatekeepers disavowed him and did not permit him; then Anbasah ibn Sa'id came and sought permission for him from al-Hajjaj, so he permitted him. So he entered and greeted, and he ordered two men beside the couch to make room for him, so they made room for him and he sat. Al-Hajjaj said to him: May Allah bless your father, do you know a hadith which your father narrated to Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan from your grandfather Abd Allah ibn Salam? He said: And which hadith, may Allah have mercy on you? For many a hadith. He said: The hadith of the Egyptians when they came upon Uthman. He said: I know that hadith. Abd Allah ibn Salam came while Uthman was besieged. He said: So he went and entered upon him, and they made room for him until he entered. So he said: Peace be upon you, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: And upon you peace; what brings you, O Abd Allah ibn Salam? He said: I came to stand firm until he is martyred or Allah gives you victory, and I see these people only as your killers; if they kill you, that is better for you and worse for them. So Uthman said to him: I ask you by the right I have upon you to go out to them with good which Allah brings through you, or evil which Allah repels through you. So he heard and obeyed, and went out to them; when they saw him they gathered, thinking he had brought them something they would rejoice at. So he stood as a preacher, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed, Allah sent Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a bearer of glad tidings and a warner, giving tidings of Paradise to whoever obeys him, and warning of Hell for whoever disobeys him, and made those who follow him prevail over all religion though the associators dislike it. Then He chose dwellings for him and chose Madinah for him, making it the abode of emigration and the abode of faith. By Allah, the angels have not ceased surrounding this Madinah since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to it, and the sword of Allah has not ceased sheathed from you since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to it until today. Then he said: Allah sent Muhammad with the truth; whoever is guided is guided only by Allah's guidance, and whoever strays strays only after clarity and proof. And no prophet of the past was killed but seventy thousand fighters were killed for him, all killed for him; and no caliph was ever killed but thirty-five thousand fighters were killed for him, all killed for him. So do not hasten to kill this old man; by Allah, none of you will kill him but he will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection with his hand cut off, paralyzed. Know that a father has no right over a child but this old man has the like of it over you. He said: So they stood and said: The Jews have lied! The Jews have lied. He said: You have lied, by Allah, and you are sinful; I am no Jew, I am one of the Muslims; Allah knows it, His Messenger, and the believers. And the Qur'an was revealed about me, so he recited this verse: {Say: Allah suffices as witness between me and you, and whoever has knowledge of the Book}; and Allah revealed the other verse: {Say: Have you considered, if it is from Allah and you disbelieve in it, while a witness of the Children of Israel bore witness to the like of it and believed, and you were arrogant}. He said: So they stood and entered upon Uthman and slaughtered him as a lamb is slaughtered. Shu'ayb said: So I said to Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr: What is hullan? He said: A lamb. He said: And Uthman had said before that to Kathir ibn al-Salt: O Kathir, by Allah I shall be killed tomorrow. He said: Rather Allah will raise your station and abase your enemy. He said: Then he repeated it a third time, and he said the like to him. He said: On what do you say that, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with him Abu Bakr and Umar, and he said to me: O Uthman, you are with us tomorrow, and you shall be killed tomorrow; so by Allah, I shall be killed. He said: So he was killed. He said: Then Abd Allah ibn Salam went out to the people before they dispersed, they being in the mosque, and stood on his feet and said: O people of Egypt, O killers of Uthman, you killed the Commander of the Faithful; by Allah, there shall ever be a broken covenant, shed blood, and divided wealth, undivided."
"15002","14963 - Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, from Riyah ibn Abidah, he said: Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam narrated to me, from his father, he said: People will remain after the Antichrist forty years; markets will flourish and date-palms will be planted."
"15003","14964 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam from his father: Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, he said: Raja' ibn Salamah ibn Raja' narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us; and narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, he said: Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Raja' narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, he said: Sayyar Abu al-Hakam narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: My father said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and said: Allah Almighty has praised you well for purification, O people of Quba; will you not inform me? So we said: O Messenger of Allah, upon us in the Torah is washing with water."
"15004","14965 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, he said: Abd Allah ibn Hammad al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Unaysah, from Sayyar Abu al-Hakam, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the mosque founded upon piety, the mosque of Quba, and stood at its gate and said: Allah has praised you well for purification; what is your purification? We said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people of the Book, and we find washing with water incumbent upon us, and we do it today. So he said: Allah has praised you well for purification. So he said: {In it are men who love to purify themselves, and Allah loves those who purify themselves}."
"15005","14966 - Narrated to us Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us; and narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi, he said: my father narrated to us, they said: Harmalah ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Rabi' ibn Sabrah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hakam ibn Yusuf and others of the people of Dhu al-Marwah and its elders narrated to me, from a son of Abd Allah ibn Salam, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he passed al-Hulayhah on his journey to Tabuk, his Companions said to him: The stopping place, O Messenger of Allah; shade and water; and in it were lote trees and water. So he said: It is a land of crops and cattle; leave it, for it is commanded - meaning his she-camel. So it came until it alighted under the lote tree that was in the mosque of Dhu al-Marwah."
"15006","14967 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Tirmidhi, he said: Bakr ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Dahhak, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: Jesus, peace be upon him, shall be buried with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his two Companions, so his grave will be the fourth."
"15007","14968 - Zurarah ibn Awfa from Abd Allah ibn Salam: Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, he said: Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us; and narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, he said: Mu'adh ibn Awdh Allah al-Qurashi narrated to us, they said: Awf narrated to us, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, the people hastened toward him, and I was among those who went out. When I saw his face I knew it was not the face of a liar. The first I heard him say was: Feed food, spread peace, and pray while people sleep; you will enter Paradise in peace."
"15008","14969 - Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah from Abd Allah ibn Salam: Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, he said: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Zurayk ibn Abi Zurayk narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Abd Allah ibn Salam: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of women delights you when you look, obeys you when you command, and guards your absence in herself and your property."
"15009","14970 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani, he said: Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Zurayk ibn Abi Zurayk narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between the two door-leaves of Paradise is a distance of forty years, and there shall come upon it a day when it is crowded as thirsty camels returning after five days crowd."
"15010","14971 - Qays ibn Ubad from Abd Allah ibn Salam: Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Jabalah narrated to us, he said: Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, from Qurrah ibn Khalid, from Ibn Sirin, he said: Qays ibn Ubad said: I was in a circle in which were Sa'd ibn Malik and Ibn Umar, when Abd Allah ibn Salam passed by, and they said: This is a man of the people of Paradise. So I followed him and said to him: They said such-and-such. He said: Glory be to Allah! It is not fitting for them to say what they have no knowledge of; I only saw as if a pillar was placed in a green garden and erected in it, and in its middle a handhold, and at its bottom a servant - and al-minsaf is the attendant - so it was said to me: Climb it. So I climbed it, then I seized the handhold. So I narrated it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abd Allah ibn Salam shall die holding to the firmest handhold."
"15011","14972 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, he said: Abd Allah ibn Hammad al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us; and narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, they said: Azhar narrated to us, both from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Qays ibn Ubad, he said: I entered the mosque of Madinah, and a man came and prayed two rak'ahs, shortening them, with a trace of humility upon him. So a man said: Whoever is pleased to look at a man of the people of Paradise, let him look at this. So I followed him and informed him. So he said: Glory be to Allah; it is not fitting for anyone to say what he does not know. And shall I narrate to you why that is? I saw a dream and narrated it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I saw as if I were in a garden - and he mentioned its vastness, beauty, and greenness - and in its middle an iron pillar, its bottom in the earth and its top in the sky, at its head a handhold. So it was said to me: Climb. So I said: I cannot. Then a servant came to me and lifted my clothes from behind me, and I came to be at its top. So he said: Hold fast. So I awoke, and it was in my hand. So I narrated it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The garden is Islam, the pillar is the pillar of Islam, and the handhold is the firmest; so you are upon Islam. And behold, he was Abd Allah ibn Salam."
"15012","14973 - Rib'i ibn Hirash from Abd Allah ibn Salam: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Fa'id, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: I narrate to you only from a revealed book or a sent prophet: there is no soul that repents before its illness in which it dies by a day except Allah accepts its repentance, until the sun rises from its setting place."
"15013","14974 - Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa from Abd Allah ibn Salam: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Abdan ibn Ahmad, they said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Burayd narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, he said: I came to Madinah, and Abd Allah ibn Salam met me and said: Come with me to the house; you will pray in a mosque in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and drink from a cup from which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank. So I went with him to his house, and I prayed in his mosque, and he fed me dates and gave me sawiq to drink."
"15014","14975 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, from Abu Burdah, he said: I came to Madinah and sat with Abd Allah ibn Salam, and he said: Will you not come to the house, and pray in a mosque in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and drink from a cup from which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank? So I went with him. Then he said: You are in a land in which usury is widespread, and among usury is that a man makes an advance payment and is given a gift, and he accepts it."
"15015","14976 - Kharashah ibn al-Hurr from Abd Allah ibn Salam: Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, he said: I came to Madinah and sat with elders in the mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when an old man came leaning upon a staff of his. Some of the people said to him: This is a man of the people of Paradise. So he stood behind a pillar and prayed two rak'ahs. So I stood to him and said: Some of the people claimed you are a man of the people of Paradise? So he said: Paradise belongs to Allah; He admits whom He wills. And I saw a dream in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I saw as if a man came to me and said to me: Go. So he took me and led me by a great path; then a road appeared to me on my left and I wanted to take it, so he said: You are not of its people. Then another road appeared to me on my right, so I took it until I ended at a slippery mountain; so he took my hand and propelled me, and behold I was upon its peak, and I could neither settle nor steady myself; and behold a pillar, at its top a handhold of gold. So he took my hand and propelled me until I seized the handhold. So I narrated it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: You saw good. As for the great path, it is the gathering place; as for the road that appeared on your left, it is the road of the people of Hell, and you are not of its people; as for the road that appeared to you on your right, it is the road of the people of Paradise; as for the slippery mountain, it is the station of the martyrs; as for the handhold you held to, it is the handhold of Islam, and you hold to it, Allah willing, until you die. And I hope to be of the people of Paradise. And he is Abd Allah ibn Salam."
"15016","14977 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, they said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sulayman ibn Mushir, from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, he said: I was sitting in a circle in the mosque of Madinah in which was an old man of fine appearance - and he was Abd Allah ibn Salam - and he would narrate to them a fine hadith. When he stood, the people said: Whoever is pleased to look at a man of the people of Paradise, let him look at this. I said: By Allah, I shall follow him and learn the place of his house. He said: So I followed him until he nearly left Madinah, then he entered his house; so I asked permission and he permitted me. So he said: What is your need, O son of my brother? I said to him: I heard the people say to you when you stood: Whoever is pleased to look at a man of the people of Paradise, let him look at this; and I liked to be with you. He said: Allah knows best the people of Paradise; and shall I narrate to you why they said that? While I was asleep, one came to me and said: Stand. So he took my hand and I went with him; and behold, paths on my left, so I went to take them, and he said to me: Do not take them, for they are the paths of the companions of the left. And behold, paths on my right, so he said to me: Take here. So we came to a mountain, and he said: Climb above this. So whenever I wanted to climb I fell upon my buttocks; I did that repeatedly. Then he took me until he brought me to a pillar, its head in the sky and its bottom in the earth, at its top a ring. So he said to me: Climb above this. I said: How shall I climb above this, its head being in the sky? So he took my hand and propelled me, and behold I was clinging to the ring. Then the pillar was turned away and fell, and I remained clinging to the ring until morning. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him; I narrated it to him. He said: The paths you saw on your left are the paths of the companions of the left; as for the paths you saw on your right, they are the paths of the companions of the right; as for the mountain, it is the station of the martyrs, and you shall not attain it; as for the pillar, it is the pillar of Islam; as for the handhold, it is the handhold of Islam, and you shall ever hold to it until you die. Then he said to me: Do you know how Allah created creation? I said: No. He said: Allah created Adam and said: So-and-so shall beget, and so-and-so shall beget so-and-so, and so-and-so shall beget so-and-so, and so-and-so shall beget so-and-so; his term is such, his deed is such-and-such, his provision is such-and-such; then He breathes the spirit into him."
"15017","14978 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, they said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Ala' ibn al-Musayyab, from Salih ibn Khabbab, from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: I narrate to you only from a sent prophet or a revealed book: if a servant committed every sin then repented to Allah a day before his death, it would be accepted from him."
"15018","14979 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, he said: I came to Madinah and met Abd Allah ibn Salam, and he said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith that is in the Book of Allah? And he mentioned people coming out of Hell; Ibrahim says: O Lord, Thou hast burned my sons; and they come out of it."
"15019","14980 - Ata' ibn Yasar from Abd Allah ibn Salam: Narrated to us Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Hilal ibn Usamah, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: We find the description of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We have sent you as a witness, a bearer of glad tidings, a warner, and a refuge for the unlettered; you are My servant and My Messenger; I have named you the Trusting; he is not harsh, nor coarse, nor clamorous in the markets, nor does he repay evil with its like, but he pardons, overlooks, and passes over; and I shall not take him until I straighten the crooked creed by testifying that there is no god but Allah; through it He opens blind eyes, deaf ears, and veiled hearts. Ata' ibn Yasar said: And Abu Waqid al-Laythi informed me that he heard Ka'b al-Ahbar say the like of what Ibn Salam said."
"15020","14981 - The nephew of Abd Allah ibn Salam from Abd Allah: Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, and Abdan ibn Ahmad, they said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ya'la al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from the nephew of Abd Allah ibn Salam, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: My name in the pre-Islamic age was so-and-so, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named me Abd Allah."
"15021","14982 - Bishr ibn Shaghaf from Abd Allah ibn Salam: Narrated to us Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi and Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi, they said: Amr ibn Uthman al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Ma'mar ibn Rashid, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Ya'qub, from Bishr ibn Shaghaf, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection, without boast; the first for whom the earth splits, without boast; the first intercessor and the first whose intercession is accepted; the banner of praise is in my hand on the Day of Resurrection; beneath me Adam and those below him."
"15022","14983 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, he said: Yahya ibn Talhah al-Yarbu'i narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Wasil, freedman of Abu Uyaynah, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Ya'qub, from Bishr ibn Shaghaf, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salam said: The noblest of Allah's creation to Allah is Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15023","14984 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani, he said: Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Mahdi ibn Maymun, from Muhammad ibn Abi Abd Allah ibn Abi Ya'qub, from Bishr ibn Shaghaf, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salam said: The noblest of creation to Allah on the Day of Resurrection is Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15024","14985 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from a man, from Ibn Shaghaf, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, the nearest of people on the Day of Resurrection is Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), seated to its right upon the Chair."
"15025","14986 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from Abd Allah ibn Salam: Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith showed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Musa ibn Sa'd, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say upon the pulpit: It is no harm upon you - if you find - to take two garments for Friday besides the two garments of work."
"15026","14987 - Ubayd ibn Umayr al-Laythi from Abd Allah ibn Salam: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, he said: Dirar ibn Surad Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn al-Walid al-Wassafi, from Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salam was sitting and spoke a word, and a man heard him who would not have liked to hear him; so he turned to Abu al-Darda' and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever narrates a report he would not like to be spread from him, it is a trust, even if its owner did not ask him to conceal it."
"15027","14988 - Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abd Allah ibn Salam: Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi narrated to us; and narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, he said: Duhaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, all from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Abu al-Nadr, from Abu Salamah, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: I said while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting: We find in the Book of Allah: on Friday there is an hour which no believing servant coincides with, praying, asking Allah for something, except He fulfills his need. Abd Allah said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to me, saying: Part of an hour. So I said: You spoke truly, part of an hour. I said: Which hour is it? He said: The last hours of the day. I said: It is not a time of prayer? He said: Yes; when the believing servant prays then sits, and nothing keeps him but prayer, he is in prayer."
"15028","14989 - Narrated to us Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi, he said: Abu Mushir narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us; and narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, they said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: I sat among a group of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they said: Which of you will come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him: Which deeds are most beloved to Allah? Then was revealed: {O you who believe, why do you say what you do not do}. Abu Salamah said: So Abd Allah ibn Salam recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then he wept. Yahya said: So Abu Salamah recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then he wept. Al-Awza'i said: So Yahya recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then he wept. Al-Walid said: So al-Awza'i recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then he wept. Duhaym said: So al-Walid recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then he wept. Ibrahim said: So my father recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then he wept. And Ibrahim recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then he wept."
"15029","14990 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, he said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to me, he said: Ata' ibn Yasar - or Abu Salamah - narrated to me: that Abd Allah ibn Salam narrated to him, he said: We discussed among ourselves, and we said: Which of us will come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him: Which deeds are most beloved to Allah? But we feared that any of us should stand; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man to us, and we began gesturing to one another; then he recited to us: {Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth glorifies Allah} from its beginning to its end. Hilal said: So Ata' ibn Yasar recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Yahya said: So Hilal recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Al-Awza'i said: So Yahya recited it to us from its beginning to its end."
"15030","14991 - Abd Allah ibn Hubaysh from Abd Allah ibn Salam: Narrated to us Yusuf al-Qadi, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us; and narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, he said: Shabab al-Usfuri narrated to me, they said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya al-Aslami narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: What is between Ayr and Uhud is sanctuary; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made it sanctuary. I would neither cut a tree from it nor hunt a bird."
"15031","14992 - Ubadah ibn Nusayy from Abd Allah ibn Salam: Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Munir ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I heard Ubadah ibn Nusayy narrate from Abd Allah ibn Salam, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, we find you in the Book of Allah: a nation of much praise; the birthplace of their prophet is Makkah, his emigration is Taybah, their striving is in Syria; they gird their waist-wrappers upon their halves, purify their limbs; they have a humming at night in the mosques like the humming of bees in their hives; they come on the Day of Resurrection with bright faces, hands, and feet."
"15032","14993 - Disconnected reports from Abd Allah ibn Salam: Narrated to us Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi, he said: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever prays a prayer then awaits the next is in prayer until he finishes it."
"15033","14994 - Narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, he said: Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu Isa al-Khurasani Sulayman ibn Kaysan, from Ata' al-Khurasani, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A dirham a man acquires from usury is greater with Allah than thirty-three adulteries he commits in Islam."
"15034","And from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The doors of usury are seventy-two sins, the least of them like one who approaches his mother in Islam."
"15035","14995 - Abd Allah ibn Rawahah al-Ansari, and he is Abd Allah ibn Rawahah ibn Imri' al-Qays ibn Tha'labah ibn Abd Amr ibn Imri' al-Qays ibn Malik ibn Ka'b ibn al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj; of Aqabah and Badr; martyred on the day of Mu'tah. Of his reports: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah: regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, of Banu Imri' al-Qays ibn Tha'labah ibn Ka'b ibn al-Khazraj ibn al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Abd Allah ibn Rawahah ibn Imri' al-Qays."
"15036","14956 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab: regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr, of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Abd Allah ibn Rawahah ibn Imri' al-Qays."
"15037","14957 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated, he said: Ma'mar narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered in the compensatory Umrah, with Abd Allah ibn Rawahah before him, saying: [poetry omitted in print]"
"15038","14958 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated, he said: Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated, from Thabit, from Anas: that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah, Abd Allah ibn Rawahah walked before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: [rajaz verse] Umar said: O Ibn Rawahah, before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and in the sanctuary of Allah you speak poetry? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him alone, O Umar; by the One in whose hand is my soul, this is harder upon them than the striking of swords."
"15039","14959 - Abu Shu'ayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah in that Umrah, he entered it with Abd Allah ibn Rawahah al-Ansari holding the halter of his camel, saying: [rajaz verse]"
"15040","14960 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded his Companions in the compensatory Umrah, he said: Uncover your shoulders and hasten in the circumambulation, to show the associators their endurance and strength; and he strove against them with all he could. So the people of Makkah turned - the men, women, and children among them - looking at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions while they circumambulated the House, with Abd Allah ibn Rawahah reciting rajaz before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his sword slung over him, saying: [rajaz verse] And men of the nobles of the associators absented themselves, disliking to look at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) out of rage, spite, envy, and jealousy; they went out to the outskirts of Makkah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) completed his rites and stayed three days."
"15041","15001 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, he said: al-Mu'afa ibn Imran narrated, he said: Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Miqsam Abu al-Qasim, from Ibn Abbas: that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar, he stipulated for himself the land and every yellow and white thing; meaning gold and silver. So the people of Khaybar said to him: We know the land best; so give it to us that we work it, with half the fruit for us and half for you. So he mentioned that he gave it to them on that basis; and when the time came to cut the date-palms, he sent Ibn Rawahah to them, and he estimated the date-palms - what the people of Madinah call khars - and said: In this is such-and-such. So they said: You have overestimated against us, O Ibn Rawahah. He said: Then to me belongs the estimation of the date-palms, and I shall give you half of what I said. They said: This is the truth; by it the heavens and the earth stand. We agree to take by what you said."
"15042","15002 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from A'ishah, that she said - while mentioning the affair of Khaybar -: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send Ibn Rawahah to the Jews, and the date-palms would be estimated when the first of the fruit ripened, before any of it was eaten. Then the Jews would be given the choice of taking it at that estimate, or handing it over to them at that. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only commanded estimation that zakah might be reckoned before the fruits were eaten and dispersed."
"15043","15003 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr showed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: Ibn Rawahah estimated it at forty thousand wasqs; and he claimed that when Ibn Rawahah gave the Jews the choice, they took the dates, with twenty thousand wasqs upon them."
"15044","15004 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amir ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nistas showed me, regarding Khaybar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered it, and it belonged wholly to him: its tillage and its date-palms; and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions had no slaves, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made peace with the Jews on condition they suffice us the work, with half the dates for them, on condition: I keep you as long as it appears fit to Allah and His Messenger. That is when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ibn Rawahah to estimate against them; and when he gave them the choice, the Jews took the fruit. And Khaybar remained in the hands of the Jews upon the peace of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until Umar, who expelled them. So the Jews said: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not make peace with us upon such-and-such? He said: Yes, on condition he keeps you as long as it appears fit to Allah and His Messenger; and this is when it appears fit to me to expel you. So he expelled them, then divided it among the Muslims who had conquered it with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), giving none of it to one who had not attended its conquest. He said: So its people today are the Muslims; there are no Jews in it. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only commanded estimation that zakah be reckoned before the fruits were eaten and dispersed; and they remained upon that."
"15045","15005 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr showed me, regarding the settlement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the Jews of Khaybar, on: that for us is half the fruit and for you half, and they suffice us the work. When their fruit ripened, they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Our fruit has ripened, so send an estimator to estimate between us and you. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abd Allah ibn Rawahah; and when he walked among their date-palms and looked at them, he said: By Allah, I know none of Allah's creation who fabricates a greater lie against Allah and is more hostile to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than you; by Allah, Allah has created none more hateful to me than you; yet by Allah, that does not carry me to wrong you by the weight of an atom, and I know it. He said: Then he estimated it all together, theirs and the Jews', at eighty thousand wasqs. So the Jews said: You have warred against us. So Ibn Rawahah said: If you wish, give us forty thousand wasqs and depart from us. So some of them looked at others, then they said: By this the heavens and the earth stand, and by this you overcome them."
"15046","15006 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar, he sent Abd Allah ibn Rawahah to divide with the Jews. When he came to them and they began gifting him food, he disliked taking anything from them, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only sent me as a just arbiter between him and you; I have no interest in your gifts. So he estimated the date-palms; and when he established the estimate, Abd Allah gave them the choice, saying: If you wish, I shall guarantee your share and take charge of it; and if you wish, you shall guarantee our share and take charge of it. So they chose to guarantee and take charge of it, and said: O Ibn Rawahah, this you offer us and act upon, by which the heavens and the earth stand; and they only stand by truth. And Khaybar belonged to those who witnessed Hudaybiyah; none shared it with them, none of them stayed back from it, none other than them witnessed it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted none who had stayed back from his expedition to Hudaybiyah to witness Khaybar."
"15047","15007 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the conquest of Khaybar, he said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abd Allah ibn Rawahah to divide the fruit with the Jews. When he came to them, they began gifting him food and speaking to him, and they gathered for him jewelry of their women's jewelry, saying: This is for you; lighten upon us and overlook. So Ibn Rawahah said: O company of Jews, by Allah you are the most hateful of people to me; yet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only sent me as a just arbiter between you and him. I have no interest in your world, and I shall not wrong you; and what you offered me is bribery, and we do not consume it. So he estimated the date-palms; and when he established the estimate, he gave them the choice, saying: If you wish, I shall guarantee your share; and if you wish, you shall guarantee our share and take charge of it. So they chose to guarantee and take charge of it. And they said: O Ibn Rawahah, this you act upon; by it the heaven and the earth stand; and they only stand by truth."
"15048","15008 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata': This estimation of theirs in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he informed me regarding Ibn Rawahah: that he estimated between the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Jews, saying: If you wish, then ours; and if you wish, then yours. They said: By this the heavens and the earth stand."
"15049","15009 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: When Ibn Rawahah came to them, they gathered for him jewelry of their women's jewelry and gifted it to him. So he said: O company of Jews, you are the most hateful of Allah's creation to me, yet that shall not carry me to wrong you. As for this bribery you offered us, it is illicit gain, and we do not consume it. Then he estimated against them, then gave them the choice of taking it or his taking it. They said: By this the heavens and the earth stand; so they took it at that estimate."
"15050","15010 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had no workers to work the date-palms of Khaybar and its crops, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the Jews of Khaybar and handed Khaybar to them to work it for half, paying it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: I keep you in it as long as Allah keeps you. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send Abd Allah ibn Rawahah to them, who estimated the date-palms when the first of the fruit ripened, before any of it was eaten. Then he gave the Jews the choice of taking it at that estimate, or handing it over to them at that estimate."
"15051","15011 - Abu Shu'ayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition to Mu'tah in Jumada al-Ula of the year eight, and appointed over them Zayd ibn Harithah. He said to them: If Zayd is struck, then Ja'far ibn Abi Talib is over the people; and if Ja'far is struck, then Abd Allah ibn Rawahah is over the people. So the people equipped themselves and prepared to depart, they being three thousand. When their departure came, the people bade farewell to the commanders of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted them; and when Abd Allah was bidden farewell among those bidden farewell, he wept. So it was said to him: What makes you weep, O Ibn Rawahah? He said: By Allah, it is not love of the world and attachment; but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite a verse of the Book of Allah mentioning Hell: {There is none of you but shall come to it; it is with your Lord an ordained decree}. And I do not know how the return after the coming shall be? So the Muslims said to them: May Allah accompany you and defend you, and return you to us righteous. So Abd Allah ibn Rawahah said: [poetry] Then the people prepared to depart, and Abd Allah ibn Rawahah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to bid him farewell, and said: [poetry] Then the people departed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out escorting them; and when he had bidden them farewell and turned from them, Abd Allah ibn Rawahah said: [poetry] Then they went until they alighted at Ma'an of the land of Syria. And it reached the people that Heraclius had alighted at Ma'ab of the land of Balqa' with a hundred thousand Romans, joined by the Arabized tribes of Lakhm, Judham, Balqayn, Bahra', and Bali, a hundred thousand of them, over them a man of Bali holding their banner, called Malik ibn Zanah. When that reached the Muslims, they stayed at Ma'an two nights considering their affair, and said: We shall write to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and inform him of our enemy's number; either he reinforces us with men, or he commands us his command and we proceed with it. So Abd Allah ibn Rawahah encouraged the people, saying: O people, by Allah, what you dislike is what you went out seeking: martyrdom. And we do not fight people with numbers, strength, or multitude; we fight them only with this religion with which Allah honored us. So go forth, for it is but one of the two good ends: either victory or martyrdom. And Abd Allah ibn Rawahah said in that station of theirs: [poetry]"
"15052","15012 - Abu Shu'ayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, that he narrated from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: I was an orphan of Abd Allah ibn Rawahah in his care, and he went out in that journey of his with me riding behind him on his saddle bag. By Allah, as we traveled one night, I heard him recite his verse: [poetry] When I heard it from him I wept, so he struck me with the stick and said: What is it to you - O rogue - if Allah grants me martyrdom and you return between the two sides of the saddle? Then the people went until, at the borders of Balqa', the hosts of Heraclius of Romans and Arabs met them at a village of the villages of Balqa' called Masharif. Then the associators drew near, and the Muslims withdrew to a village called Mu'tah. The people met there, and the Muslims arrayed for them, placing on their right a man of Banu Udhrah called Qutbah ibn Qatadah, and on their left a man of the Ansar called Abayah ibn Malik. Then the people met and fought; and Zayd ibn Harithah fought with the banner of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he fell amid the spears of the people. Then Ja'far took it and fought with it until, when fighting pressed him, he dismounted from a sorrel horse of his and hamstrung it; then he fought the people until he was killed. And Ja'far was the first man of the Muslims to hamstring in Islam."
"15053","15013 - Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Yahya ibn Abbad narrated to me, from his father Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: My foster father narrated to me - and he was one of Banu Murrah ibn Awf, and was in that expedition, the expedition of Mu'tah - he said: By Allah, it is as if I look at Ja'far when he dismounted from a sorrel horse of his, then hamstrung it, then fought the people until he was killed. When Ja'far was killed, Abd Allah ibn Rawahah took the banner and advanced with it, he upon his horse; and he began bringing himself down, hesitating somewhat. Then he said: [rajaz verses] And Abd Allah ibn Rawahah said: [verse] meaning his two companions Zayd and Ja'far. Then he dismounted; and when he dismounted, a cousin of his came to him with a bone of meat, saying: Strengthen your back with this, for you have met these days of yours what you have met! So he took it from his hand and took a bite of it, then he heard the crashing in the direction of the people, and said: And you still in the world? Then he cast it from his hand, took his sword, advanced, and fought until he was killed. Then Thabit ibn Aqram, one of Bal'ajlan, took the banner and said: O people, agree upon a man among you. They said: You. He said: I shall not do it. So the people agreed upon Khalid ibn al-Walid; and when he took the banner he held off the people, then withdrew until he departed with the people. And when they were struck, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zayd ibn Harithah took the banner and fought with it until he was killed a martyr; then Ja'far took it and fought with it until he was killed a martyr. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent until the faces of the Ansar changed, thinking there was about Abd Allah ibn Rawahah something they disliked. He said: Then Abd Allah ibn Rawahah took it and fought with it until he was killed a martyr. Then he said: They were raised to me in Paradise, as the sleeper sees, upon couches of gold; and I saw in the couch of Abd Allah ibn Rawahah a turning away from the couch of his two companions. So I said: For what is this? So it was said to me: They went forth, while Abd Allah ibn Rawahah hesitated somewhat, then went forth."
"15054","15014 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, he said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an army to Mu'tah and appointed over them Zayd ibn Harithah; and if Zayd is struck, their commander is Ja'far; and if Ja'far is struck, Abd Allah ibn Rawahah al-Ansari is their commander. So they went out toward Syria, toward Mu'tah; and their commanders whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had appointed were struck. So Khalid ibn al-Walid took the banner, and the Muslims agreed upon him; and Allah routed the enemy."
"15055","15015 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Jud'an, from Ibn al-Musayyab, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They were shown to me in Paradise in a tent of pearl, each of them upon a couch; and I saw Zayd and Ibn Rawahah with their necks turned aside, while Ja'far was straight, with no turning in him. He said: So I asked - or it was said to me -: when death came upon them, it was as if they turned away - or as if they turned their faces aside - while Ja'far did not do so. Ibn Uyaynah said: That is when Ibn Rawahah says: [verse]"
"15056","15016 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an army to Mu'tah and appointed over them Zayd ibn Harithah; and if he is struck, Ja'far ibn Abi Talib is their commander; and if Ja'far is struck, Abd Allah ibn Rawahah is their commander. So they went until they met Ibn Abi Sabrah al-Ghassani at Mu'tah, with hosts of Arab Christians and Romans there, Tanukh and Bahra' among them. So Ibn Abi Sabrah closed the fortress against the Muslims three days, then they came out and met upon green crops, and fought a fierce battle. And Zayd ibn Harithah took the banner and was killed; then Ja'far took it and was killed; then Ibn Rawahah took it and was killed. Then the Muslims after the commanders of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) agreed upon Khalid ibn al-Walid; so Allah routed the enemy and made the Muslims prevail. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them in Jumada al-Ula."
"15057","15017 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala' ibn Zibriq narrated to us, he said: my father narrated; and Umarah ibn Wathimah al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith al-Himsi narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Salim, from al-Zubaydi, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri showed me, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab and Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj: that Abu Hurayrah used to say in his stories: Your brother used to say poetry - or speech - not of obscenity, and he is Abd Allah ibn Rawahah: [verse fragment]"
"15058","15018 - Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn Musa and Suwayd ibn Nasr narrated, they said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from al-Haytham ibn Abi Sinan: that Abu Hurayrah used to say: A brother of yours would not speak obscenity, meaning Abd Allah ibn Rawahah, and said: [verse fragment]"
"15059","15019 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Ayli narrated, he said: Salamah ibn Rawh narrated, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, he said: al-Haytham ibn Abi Sinan narrated to me, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying in his stories, while mentioning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Your brother would not speak obscenity - meaning Abd Allah ibn Rawahah: [verse fragment]"
"15060","15020 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say in his stories: Your brother would not speak obscenity, meaning Abd Allah ibn Rawahah."
"15061","15021 - What Abd Allah ibn Rawahah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated: 15021 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Marwan al-Kufi narrated, he said: Umar ibn Abi Za'idah narrated, he said: I heard Mudrik ibn Umarah, narrating to al-Sha'bi from Abd Allah ibn Rawahah, he said: While I was passing through the mosque, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being among some of his Companions, the people said: O Abd Allah ibn Rawahah, O Abd Allah ibn Rawahah; so I thought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me, and I came. So he said: Sit, O Abd Allah ibn Rawahah; how do you speak poetry when you wish to speak? I said: I consider then I speak. He said: Then against the associators; and I had prepared nothing, so I said: [verse] So I saw dislike in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that I made his people the price of a cloak; so I considered then I said: [verse] He said: And you, may Allah make you firm, O Ibn Rawahah."
"15062","15022 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated; and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid al-Raqqi narrated, they said: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Humayd al-A'raj, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abd Allah ibn Rawahah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to come to his family by night."
"15063","15023 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Abu Mus'ab narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated, from his father, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abd Allah ibn Rawahah and Usamah ibn Zayd: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over the two leather socks."
"15064","15024 - Abd Allah ibn Zam'ah ibn al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Qusayy; his mother Quraybah bint Abi Umayyah ibn al-Mughirah, and her mother Atikah bint Abd al-Muttalib. 15024 - Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: al-Qa'nabi narrated, he said: my father Maslamah ibn Qa'nab narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Zam'ah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say in his sermon - mentioning the she-camel and the one who hamstrung it -: {When the most wretched of them was sent forth}; there rose for it a mighty, protected man among his clan, like Abu Zam'ah. Then he mentioned women, saying: For what does one of you go to his wife and flog her as a slave is flogged, then perhaps he embraces her at the end of his day? Then I heard him admonish them about their laughing at flatulence, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For what does one of you laugh at what he does?"
"15065","15025 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: I read to Anas ibn Iyad, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Zam'ah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"15066","15026 - Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that Abd Allah ibn Zam'ah informed him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day in his sermon mention the she-camel and the one who hamstrung it, saying: {When the most wretched of them was sent forth}; there rose for it a mighty, defiant, protected man among his people, like Abu Zam'ah. Then he mentioned women, saying: For what does one of you go to his wife and flog her as a slave is flogged, though perhaps he embraces her at the end of his day?! Then he admonished them about their laughing at flatulence, saying: For what does one of you laugh at what he does?"
"15067","15027 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Zam'ah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you flogs his wife as a slave is flogged, then has intercourse with her at the end of the day?"
"15068","15028 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: al-Humaydi narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated; and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah and Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Zam'ah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"15069","15029 - Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated, he said: my father narrated, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Sawdah bint Zam'ah; so her brother Abd ibn Zam'ah came from the pilgrimage and began throwing dust upon his head. When he accepted Islam, he said: I was foolish on the day I threw dust upon my head that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Sawdah!"
"15070","15030 - Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham narrated to me, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Zam'ah ibn al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib ibn Asad, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was overcome by illness, I being with him among a group of Muslims, Bilal called to prayer. So he said: Command who shall pray with the people. So I went out, and behold Umar among the people, Abu Bakr being absent. So I said: O Umar, stand and pray with the people. So he stood; and when he uttered the takbir, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard his voice, Umar being a loud-voiced man. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then where is Abu Bakr? Allah and the Muslims refuse that. So he sent to Abu Bakr, and he came after Umar had prayed that prayer, and prayed with the people. Abd Allah ibn Zam'ah said: So Umar said to me: Woe to you! What did you do to me, O Ibn Zam'ah? By Allah, when you commanded me I thought only that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had commanded you that; and were it not that, I would not have prayed with the people. I said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not command me; but when I did not see Abu Bakr, I saw you the worthiest of those present to pray with the people."
"15071","15031 - Tahir ibn Isa al-Muqri al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, he said: Rushdin ibn Sa'd narrated, he said: Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Zam'ah ibn al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib, he said: When the illness of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grew severe, I being with him among a group of Muslims, Bilal called to prayer. So he said: Command him to command the people to pray. So he went out and came to Umar, Abu Bakr being absent, and said: O Umar, stand and pray with the people. So he stood; and when he uttered the takbir, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard his voice, Umar being loud-voiced. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where is Abu Bakr? Allah and the Muslims refuse that. He repeated that several times. So he sent to Abu Bakr, and he came after Umar had prayed that prayer, and Abu Bakr prayed with the people. Abd Allah ibn Zam'ah said: Umar said to me: What did you do to me, O Ibn Zam'ah? By Allah, when you commanded me to pray with the people I thought only that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had commanded you that; and were it not that, I would not have prayed with the people! So I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not command me; but when I did not see Abu Bakr, I saw you the best of those present."
"15072","15032 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, nephew of al-Zuhri - I think - from his uncle, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Zam'ah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"15073","15033 - Abd Allah ibn Abi Habibah al-Ashhali: 15033 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated; and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: al-Qa'nabi narrated, they said: Mujammi' ibn Ya'qub al-Ansari narrated, from Muhammad ibn Isma'il, he said: It was said to Abd Allah ibn Abi Habibah: What did you attain of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us in the mosque of Quba'; so I came, a young boy, until I sat at his right, and Abu Bakr sat at his left. He said: Then he called for a drink and drank, and handed to me at his right."
"15074","15034 - Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated; and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: al-Qa'nabi narrated, they said: Mujammi' ibn Ya'qub al-Ansari narrated, from Muhammad ibn Isma'il, he said: It was said to Abd Allah ibn Abi Habibah: What did you attain of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: He stood praying, and I saw him praying in his sandals."
"15075","15035 - Abd Allah ibn Arqam al-Zuhri, and he is Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam ibn Abd Yaghuth ibn Wahb ibn Abd Manaf ibn Zuhrah; his mother Amrah bint al-Arqam ibn Hashim ibn Abd Manaf. He had gone blind before his death, and was a scribe for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them. 15035 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to me, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi Awn, he said: A letter of a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said to Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam: Answer on my behalf. So he wrote its answer, then read it to him. So he said: You hit right and did well; O Allah, grant him success. And when Umar took charge, he used to consult him."
"15076","15036 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam, he said: We were with him on a journey, and he would lead them; and when prayer came he said to us: Let one of you lead you, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When prayer comes and one of you has a need, let him begin with the need."
"15077","15037 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When prayer is established and one of you has excrement, let him begin with excrement."
"15078","15038 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When prayer is established and one of you intends excrement, let him begin with excrement."
"15079","15039 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, he said: Shu'bah informed me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"15080","15040 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Zuhayr narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Arqam, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you intends to go to the privy and prayer is established, let him begin with the privy."
"15081","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, (ha). And Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, they both said: Malik narrated to us. And Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Arqam, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you feels the need to defecate, let him begin with it before the prayer."
"15082","And Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us. And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us. And Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Arqam, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the need for the privy comes upon one of you and the prayer is established, let him begin with the privy."
"15083","And Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Arqam, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you intends to go to the privy and the prayer is established, let him begin with the privy."
"15084","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, he said: Murajja ibn Raja narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Arqam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you has the need for the privy and the prayer arrives, let him begin with the privy."
"15085","al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Arqam al-Zuhri, he said: He went out to Makkah, and he was their imam, so he put forward a man to lead them in prayer, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the prayer is established and one of you needs to defecate, let him begin with it."
"15086","al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi al-Samman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the prayer is established and one of you needs the privy, let him begin with the privy."
"15087","al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Arqam, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the prayer is established and one of you feels the need for the privy, let him begin with the privy."
"15088","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: al-Hasan ibn Qazaah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Arqam, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you feels the need for the privy and the prayer has been established, let him begin with the privy."
"15089","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bukayr al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the like of it."
"15090","al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, that he heard Urwah say: We were on a journey with Abdullah ibn al-Arqam al-Zuhri, and the prayer arrived, and he used to go ahead of us and he called the adhan for us, then he went out to relieve himself, so it was said to him: If only you had prayed and then gone out! So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the prayer arrives and one of you needs to defecate, let him begin with it, then let him pray afterwards, and let him not come to the prayer while he is holding it back."
"15091","Abdullah ibn Aqram al-Khuzai: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: al-Qanabi narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us. And Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Dawud ibn Qays, he said: I heard Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Aqram narrating from his father: That he was with his father at al-Qaa of Namirah, and a caravan passed by us and they made their camels kneel at the side of the road, so he said to me: O my son, stay with our sheep until I go near these riders. He said: So he went near them and I went with him, and the prayer was established, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among them, and I used to look at the whiteness of the armpits of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) every time he prostrated."
"15092","Abdullah ibn Jabir al-Abdi: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me. Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us. And Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Abd al-Mumin al-Muqri narrated to us, they both said: al-Harith ibn Murrah al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: A shaykh from the people of Basrah called Nufays narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Jabir al-Abdi, he said: I was among the delegation who came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Abd al-Qays, but I was not with them; I only came with my father, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them from drinking from the vessels you have heard of: the gourd, the green jar, the hollowed stump, and the tar-coated vessel."
"15093","Abdullah al-Muzani Abu Alqamah: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fada narrated to us, from his father, from Alqamah ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade breaking the current coinage of the Muslims circulating among them except in case of defect; that the dirham be broken to be made into silver, or the dinar be broken to be made into gold."
"15094","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Atiyyah ibn Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, from Mutamir ibn Sulayman, from Muhammad ibn Fada, from his father, from Alqamah ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade breaking the current coinage of the Muslims circulating among them except in case of defect."
"15095","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Mutamir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Fada, from his father, from Alqamah ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"15096","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fada narrated to us, from his father, from Alqamah ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you buys meat, let him increase its broth, for if one of you does not get meat he will get broth, and it is one of the two meats."
"15097","Mahmud ibn al-Faraj al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fada narrated to us, from his father, from Alqamah ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are among reeds or snow or muddy ground, and the prayer arrives, then gesture with gestures."
"15098","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Shabab al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Fada, from his father, from Alqamah ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may free from his slave whatever he wishes, if he wishes a third, and if he wishes a fourth."
"15099","Abdullah Abu Yazid al-Muzani: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas al-Misri narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, (ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, they both said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith showed me, from Ayyub ibn Musa, that Yazid ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to him, from his father: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Regarding camels there is a fara, and regarding sheep there is a fara, and the aqiqah is offered for the boy, and his head is not to be touched with blood."
"15100","Amr al-Ansari then al-Ajlani: Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us: My father narrated to us, (ha), and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi al-Tahhan and Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf, the two Egyptians, narrated to us, they both said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to me, from his father, that Abdullah ibn Amr al-Ajlani narrated to Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade facing anything of the two qiblahs during defecation and urination."
"15101","Amr ibn Awf ibn Milhah al-Muzani: Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Awf ibn Zayd ibn Milhah al-Muzani narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting with them, then he entered his house and said: Come in to me, and none shall come in to me except a Qurashi, so I slipped in and entered. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of Quraysh, is there among you anyone who is not of you? They said: We inform you, O Messenger of Allah, by our fathers, you and our mothers, with us are the son of the sister and the freed slave. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The ally of the people is of them, and the freed slave of the people is of them, and the son of the sister of the people is of them. O company of Quraysh, you are the rulers after me over this affair, so do not die except as believers, and hold fast to the rope of Allah all together and do not divide, and do not be like those who divided and differed after the clear proofs came to them, and they were not commanded except to worship Allah sincerely devoting religion to Him as upright, and to establish the prayer, and to give the zakat, and that is the upright religion. O company of Quraysh, preserve me regarding my Companions and their sons and the sons of their sons. May Allah have mercy on the Ansar and the sons of the Ansar."
"15102","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: We were sitting around the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his mosque in Madinah, when Jibril (peace be upon him) came to him with the revelation, so he covered himself with his cloak, and he remained long until it was lifted from him and he uncovered his cloak, and he was sweating profusely, and he was holding something. Then he said: Which of you knows what comes out of the palm tree? Then the Ansar said: We do, O Messenger of Allah, by our father, you and our mother, there is nothing that comes out of the palm tree except we know it; we are people of palm trees. Then he opened his hand and in it were date stones. He said: What is this? They said: This, O Messenger of Allah, is date stones. He said: Stones of what? They said: Stones of a year. He said: You have spoken the truth. Jibril (peace be upon him) has come to you to look after your religion. You will surely follow the ways of those before you exactly as one sandal matches the other, and you will surely take after them: if a span, then a span, and if a cubit, then a cubit, and if a fathom, then a fathom, until if they entered the hole of a lizard you would enter it. Indeed the Children of Israel split over Musa into seventy sects, all of them astray except one sect: Islam and its community. Then they split over Isa son of Maryam into seventy-one sects, all of them astray except one: Islam and its community. Then you will be upon seventy-two sects, all of them in the Fire except one: Islam and its community."
"15103","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us: al-Qanabi narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah narrated to us, (ha), and Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever revives dead land that is not within the right of a Muslim, it is his, and there is no right for an unjust root."
"15104","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Ubayd ibn Yaish narrated to us: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Yazid ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever revives a dead land, it is his, and there is no right for an unjust root."
"15105","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The well is of no liability, and the wound of the dumb animal is of no liability, and the mine is of no liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"15106","Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On Friday there is an hour of the day in which no servant asks for anything except his request is given. So it was said: Which hour is it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: When the sun stands high until part of it has passed."
"15107","Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Awf narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say the takbir in the two Eids: in the first rakah seven takbirs, and in the second rakah five takbirs before the recitation."
"15108","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us: al-Qanabi narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to us, (ha), and Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The world will not end until there is a garrison of the Muslims at Bawlan. O Ali - meaning Ali ibn Abi Talib - he said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You will surely fight the Banu al-Asfar, and those after you among the believers will fight them. Then there will come out to them the elite of the Muslims, the people of the Hijaz, who strive in the cause of Allah and are not deterred in Allah by the blame of a blamer, until Allah grants them victory over Constantinople and Rome through glorification and takbir. Then Allah will demolish its fortress, and they will obtain great wealth the like of which they never obtained, until they divide it with shields. Then a crier will cry: O people of Islam, the false Messiah, the Dajjal, has emerged in your lands. So the people will withdraw from the wealth; among them the taker, and among them the leaver, and the taker is regretful, and the leaver is regretful. Then they will say: Who is this crier? And they will not know who he is. Then they will say: Send a scout to Ludd; if the Messiah has emerged, he will bring you news of him. So they will come and look and see nothing, and they will see the people silent. Then they will say: The crier only cried out to us, so resolve, then be guided, and we shall go out all together to Ludd. If the false Messiah, the Dajjal, is there, we shall fight him until Allah judges between us and him, and He is the best of judges; and if it is the other, then these are your lands and your kinsfolk and your armies to which you have returned."
"15109","Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever revives a sunnah of mine that has died after me, then for him is the like of the reward of whoever acts upon it among the people, without that decreasing anything from the rewards of the people. And whoever innovates an innovation which Allah and His Messenger do not approve, then upon him is the like of the sin of whoever acts upon it among the people, without that decreasing anything from the sins of the people."
"15110","Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the religion will retreat to the Hijaz just as the snake retreats to its hole, and the religion will surely cling from the Hijaz to the refuge of the mountain goat on the mountain top. Indeed the religion began as strange and will return as strange, so glad tidings to the strangers who rectify what the people have corrupted after me of my sunnah."
"15111","Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: We went out on campaign with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the first campaign he undertook, al-Abwa, until when we were at al-Rawha he alighted at Irq al-Zabyah and prayed, then he said: Do you know what the name of this mountain is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: This is a mountain of the mountains of Paradise. O Allah, bless it and bless its people in it. And he said of al-Rawha: This is Sajasij, a valley of the valleys of Paradise. Seventy prophets prayed in this mosque before me, and Musa passed by it wearing two Qatawani cloaks upon a reddish she-camel among seventy thousand of the Children of Israel, performing pilgrimage to the Ancient House. And the Hour will not come until Isa son of Maryam, the servant of Allah and His Messenger, passes by it performing pilgrimage or umrah, or Allah combines that for him."
"15112","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ruwayn al-Basri narrated to us: al-Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"15113","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to me, (ha), and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us: al-Qanabi narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed I fear for my ummah after me three deeds. They said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The slip of the scholar, or an unjust ruling, or a followed desire."
"15114","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no jalab, nor janab, nor itirad, and no townsman shall sell for a Bedouin."
"15115","Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abdullah, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no sulul nor ghulul, and whoever misappropriates will bring what he misappropriated on the Day of Resurrection."
"15116","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he came to Madinah, praying toward Bayt al-Maqdis for seventeen months."
"15117","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted cutting the mishadd and the two supports and what is taken as the staff of the mount."
"15118","Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four mountains are of the mountains of Paradise, and four rivers are of the rivers of Paradise, and four battles are of the battles of Paradise. It was said: What are the mountains? He said: Uhud loves us and we love it, a mountain of the mountains of Paradise; and al-Tur is a mountain of the mountains of Paradise; and Lubnan is a mountain of the mountains of Paradise. And the four rivers: the Nile, the Euphrates, Sayhan and Jayhan. And the battles: Badr, Uhud, al-Khandaq, and Hunayn."
"15119","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us: al-Qanabi narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three matters of Jahiliyyah the people will not leave: reviling lineages, wailing, and their saying: We were given rain by such-and-such star."
"15120","Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us: Iyad ibn Abi Shamlah narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed part of poetry is wisdom."
"15121","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Anbar al-Basri narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us: Iyad ibn Abdullah Abu al-Jad al-Aslami narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses are exchanged on the day of their watering."
"15122","Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar and Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali al-Madani narrated to us, they both said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah, from Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man say: Here it is, green, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O, at your service, we have taken your good omen from your mouth; go out with us to Khadirah. So they went out to it, and no sword was drawn therein."
"15123","al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ali al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the takbir over al-Najashi five times."
"15124","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib al-Taraifi al-Raqqi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salim al-Musabbihi narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Husayni narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abdullah, from his father, from his grandfather, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not stung from one hole twice."
"15125","Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali al-Madani narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Man ibn Isa al-Qazzaz narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared Madinah a sanctuary for a barid in every direction."
"15126","Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: We went out on campaign with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of the Conquest, and we were a thousand and odd, and Allah granted us the conquest of Makkah and Hunayn. Then when we were between Hunayn and al-Taif, he saw a tree upon which weapons were hung, and it was called Dhat Anw at, and it was worshipped besides Allah. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw it, he turned away from it on a hot day to a shade nearer than it. Then a man said: O Messenger of Allah, make for us a Dhat Anw at just as they have a Dhat Anw at. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: These are the established ways; you have said, by the One in Whose Hand is Muhammad's soul, just as the Children of Israel said to Musa: Make for us a god just as they have gods. Then he said: Should I seek for you a god other than Allah while He has favored you over the worlds."
"15127","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abdullah ibn Amr, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali ibn Abi Talib: You will fight the Banu al-Asfar among a band of the Muslims who are not deterred in Allah by the blame of a blamer, until you conquer Constantinople with takbir and glorification."
"15128","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: al-Qanabi narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will surely fight the Banu al-Asfar, and you will kill them, and those after you among the believers will fight them. The believers who strive in the cause of Allah, whom no blame of a blamer deters in Allah, will go out to them, until Allah grants them victory over Constantinople and Rome through glorification and takbir. Then its fortress will be demolished, and they will obtain therein great wealth, until they divide the wealth with shields, and a crier will cry: O people of Islam, the false Messiah, the Dajjal, has emerged in your lands and your offspring. Then they will say: Who is this crier? And they will not know who he is. Then they will say: Look and be guided, and send a scout to Ludd; if the Messiah has emerged, he will bring you knowledge of him. So they will send the scout to Ludd, then they will say: We shall march to them; if it is he, we shall fight him until Allah judges between us, and He is the best of judges; and if it is the other, then these are your lands and your kinsfolk to which you have returned."
"15129","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Awf al-Muzani, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Muslims are bound by their conditions, except a condition that forbids what is lawful or permits what is unlawful. And settlement is permissible among people, except a settlement that permits what is unlawful or forbids what is lawful."
"15130","Ahmad ibn Hamdun al-Mawsili and al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya al-Mutarriz narrated to us, they both said: Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us: al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us, (ha), and Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Ali ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the charity of the Muslim increases lifespan, and prevents an evil death, and Allah removes thereby arrogance and pride."
"15131","Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twelve foundations of the religion."
"15132","And with its chain, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever changes the landmarks of the land, upon him is the curse of Allah and His anger on the Day of Resurrection; Allah will not accept from him any obligatory nor supererogatory deed."
"15133","Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Awf, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no seizing by force nor plundering."
"15134","Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Awf, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes allegiance to other than his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah and His anger on the Day of Resurrection; Allah will not accept from him any obligatory nor supererogatory deed. And whoever kills other than his killer, upon him is the curse of Allah and His anger on the Day of Resurrection; Allah will not accept from him any obligatory nor supererogatory deed. And whoever innovates an innovation or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah and His anger on the Day of Resurrection; Allah will not accept from him any obligatory nor supererogatory deed."
"15135","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, they both said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Awf, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No stray without support is left in Islam - Ibn Numayr added in his narration - until he is joined to a tribe."
"15136","Amr ibn Awf, freed slave of Suhayl ibn Amr, and it is said: ally of Banu Amir ibn Luayy, a Badri: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr: Amr ibn Awf, freed slave of Suhayl ibn Amr."
"15137","Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar al-Madani narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, that he informed him that Amr ibn Awf, and he is the ally of Banu Amir, and he had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah to al-Bahrayn, and he brought its jizyah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the one who had made peace with al-Bahrayn and appointed over them al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami. Then Abu Ubaydah arrived with wealth from al-Bahrayn, and the Ansar heard of his arrival, so they attended the Fajr prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he prayed, he turned away, and they presented themselves to him. He smiled when he saw them and said: I think you have heard of the arrival of Abu Ubaydah and that he has brought something? They said: Yes. He said: Then receive glad tidings and hope for what delights you. By Allah, it is not poverty I fear for you, but I fear that the world will be spread out for you just as it was spread out for those before you, and you will compete for it just as they competed for it, and it will distract you just as it distracted them."
"15138","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us: al-Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to us, and Muawiyah ibn Yahya narrated to me: al-Zuhri narrated to me: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah informed him that Amr ibn Awf al-Ansari, and he is the ally of Banu Amir ibn Luayy, and he had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah to al-Bahrayn, and he brought its jizyah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the one who had made peace with the people of al-Bahrayn and appointed over them al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami. Then Abu Ubaydah arrived with wealth from al-Bahrayn, and the Ansar heard of the arrival of Abu Ubaydah, so they attended the Fajr prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them, they turned away and presented themselves to him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled when he saw them, then he said: I think you have heard that Abu Ubaydah has brought something? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then receive glad tidings and hope for what delights you. By Allah, it is not poverty I fear for you, but I fear that the world will be spread out for you just as it was spread out for those before you; and you will compete for it just as they competed for it; and it will destroy you just as it destroyed them."
"15139","Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to me, from Yunus, (ha), and Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah informed him that Amr ibn Awf, and he is the ally of Banu Amir ibn Luayy, and he had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah to al-Bahrayn, and he brought its jizyah. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the one who had made peace with the people of al-Bahrayn and appointed over them al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami. Then Abu Ubaydah arrived with wealth from al-Bahrayn, and the Ansar heard of the arrival of Abu Ubaydah, so they attended the Fajr prayer with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, he turned away, and they presented themselves to him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled when he saw them, then he said: I think you have heard that Abu Ubaydah has come with something from al-Bahrayn? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then receive glad tidings of what delights you. By Allah, it is not poverty I fear for you, but I fear for you that the world will be spread out for you just as it was spread out for those before you, and you will compete for it just as they competed for it, and it will destroy you just as it destroyed them."
"15140","Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Uzayz narrated to us: Salamah ibn Rawh narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah informed him that Amr ibn Awf informed him - and he had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah to al-Bahrayn, and he brought its jizyah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the one who had made peace with the people of al-Bahrayn and appointed over them al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami. Then Abu Ubaydah arrived with wealth from al-Bahrayn, and the Ansar heard of the arrival of Abu Ubaydah, so they attended the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Fajr prayer. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, he turned away, and they presented themselves to him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled when he saw them, then he said: I think you have heard that Abu Ubaydah has come with something? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then receive glad tidings and hope for what delights you. By Allah, it is not poverty I fear for you, but I fear for you that the world will be spread out for you just as it was spread out for those before you, and you will compete therein just as they competed, and it will destroy you just as it destroyed them."
"15141","Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi narrated to us: Suwayd ibn Nasr and Hibban ibn Musa narrated to us, they both said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar and Yunus, from al-Zuhri: Urwah informed me, that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah informed him that Amr ibn Awf, and he is an ally of Banu Amir ibn Luayy, and he had witnessed Badr with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, and he mentioned the like of it."
"15142","Amr ibn Akhtab Abu Zayd al-Ansari: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Anas ibn Sirin narrated to us, that Abu Zayd ibn Akhtab said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me: May Allah beautify you. So he became a handsome old man."
"15143","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh al-Wasiti narrated to us: Salih ibn Umar al-Wasiti narrated to us: Azrah ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Ilba ibn Ahmad, from Abu Zayd, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Come near and wipe my back. So I came near and wiped his back, and I placed the Seal of Prophethood between my fingers. I said: What is the Seal of Prophethood? He said: Hair between his shoulders."
"15144","al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us: Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Azrah ibn Thabit narrated to us: Ilba ibn Ahmad narrated to me: Abu Zayd narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped my face and supplicated for me for beauty. Azrah said: Some of my family informed me that he reached a hundred and seven years, and there was in his head and beard only a few white hairs."
"15145","al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us: Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Azrah ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Ilba ibn Ahmad: Abu Zayd narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Fajr prayer, then he ascended the pulpit and addressed us until Zuhr arrived. Then he descended and prayed, then he ascended the pulpit and addressed us until Asr arrived. Then he descended and prayed Asr, then he ascended the pulpit and addressed us until the sun set. Then he informed us of what is to come; the most knowledgeable of us is the most retentive of us."
"15146","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (ha), and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, they both said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us: Abu Nuhayk narrated to me, he said: I heard Amr ibn Akhtab Abu Zayd al-Ansari say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked for water, so I brought him a cup in which there was a hair, so I took it. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, beautify him. He said: I saw him reach sixty years with not a white hair in his head and beard."
"15147","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us: Abu Nuhayk narrated to me, he said: I heard Amr ibn Akhtab Abu Zayd al-Ansari say: I saw the Seal upon the back of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) like this, showing it as though sealing."
"15148","Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal narrated to us: Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abu Zayd al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They call to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, yet they have nothing to do with Allah. Whoever fights them is more deserving of Allah than they - meaning the Khawarij."
"15149","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Ali ibn Uthman al-Lahiqi narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Harrani narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Abu Zayd al-Ansari, that he went on nine campaigns with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15150","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us: Khalid informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Amr ibn Salamah, or from Abu al-Muhallab, from Abu Zayd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once passed among the dwellings of the Ansar and found the smell of cooking meat. Then he said: Who slaughtered before we slaughter? Then a man came out and said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah; this is a day in which food is disliked. He said: Then repeat. He said: By Allah, besides Whom there is no god, I have only a jadha of sheep or a lamb. He said: Then slaughter it, but no jadha will suffice for anyone after you."
"15151","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us: Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Amr ibn Bujdan, from Abu Zayd al-Ansari, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed among our dwellings and found the smell of cooking meat. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is it that slaughtered? Then a man of us came out and said: O Messenger of Allah, it was a day in which food was disliked, so I slaughtered to eat and feed my neighbors. He said: Then repeat the slaughter. He said: No, by Allah, besides Whom there is no god, I have only a jadha of sheep or a lamb. He said it three times. He said: Then slaughter it, but no jadha will suffice for anyone after you; and he had slaughtered before the prayer."
"15152","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Khalid informed us, from Abu Qilabah, from a man of his people - I think him to be Amr ibn Bujdan - from Abu Zayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came until when he was among the dwellings of the Ansar, he found the smell of cooking meat. Then he said: Who is it that slaughtered? Then a man came out and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a day in which food is disliked. He said: Then repeat. He said: By Allah, I have only a jadha or a lamb of sheep. He said: Repeat, three times. Then he said: Then slaughter it, but it will not suffice for anyone after you."
"15153","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it, and he did not mention Amr ibn Bujdan."
"15154","Amr ibn Salamah al-Jarmi: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: Zayd ibn Akhram narrated to us: Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Rabah narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Salamah say: I went with my father to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the Islam of his people, and among what he enjoined upon us was: Let the one who leads you be the most versed of you in the Quran. So I was the most versed of them in the Quran, so they put me forward."
"15155","Amr ibn Ghaylan al-Thaqafi: Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, and Musa ibn Sahl Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, they said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us: Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Yazid ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydullah, from Amr ibn Ghaylan al-Thaqafi, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Allah, whoever believes in me and affirms me and knows that what I have brought is the truth from You, then lessen his wealth and children, and make meeting You beloved to him, and hasten his appointed end. And whoever does not believe in me and does not affirm me and does not know that what I have brought is the truth from You, then increase his wealth and lengthen his life."
"15156","Amr ibn Sufyan al-Muharibi: Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri narrated to us: al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us: Yazid ibn al-Fadl ibn Amr ibn Sufyan al-Muharibi narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Forbid your people from the nabidh of jars; for it is forbidden by Allah and His Messenger."
"15157","Amr ibn al-Ahwas Abu Sulayman al-Tamimi: al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, (ha), and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, (ha), and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us: Shabib ibn Gharqadah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage say: Is not which day the most sacred? So they said: The day of the Greater Pilgrimage. He said: Indeed your blood, your wealth, and your honors are sacred among you like the sanctity of this day of yours in this land of yours in this month of yours. Indeed no offender offends except against himself. Indeed no father offends against his son, nor a son against his father. Indeed Satan has despaired of being worshipped in this land of yours ever, but he will have obedience in some of what you deem insignificant of your deeds, and he will be content with it. Indeed all blood of Jahiliyyah is laid down, and the first I lay down thereof is the blood of al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib; he was being suckled among Banu Layth, and Hudhayl killed him. Then he said: O my community, have I conveyed? Three times. Then he said: O Allah, bear witness. Three times."
"15158","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us: Zaidah informed us, from Shabib ibn Gharqadah, from Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas: My father narrated to me that he witnessed the Farewell Pilgrimage with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: No offender offends except against himself, nor a father against his son, nor a son against his father."
"15159","Amr ibn Kharijah al-Asadi, and it is said: Kharijah ibn Amr, and the correct is: Amr ibn Kharijah, ally of Abu Sufyan ibn Harb ibn Umayyah ibn Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Amr ibn Kharijah, he said: I was beneath the she-camel of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while it was chewing its cud, and its saliva was between my shoulders. Then I heard him say: Indeed Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has given every possessor of a right his right, and no bequest is permissible for an heir. And the child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. And whoever claims to other than his father or affiliates to other than his masters out of dislike for them, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither obligatory nor supererogatory deed is accepted from him."
"15160","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us: Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, (ha), and Abu Khalifah narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, they both said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Amr ibn Kharijah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us while upon his slit-eared she-camel, and I was holding its neck rope while it was chewing its cud. Then he said: Indeed Allah has given every possessor of a right his right; there is no bequest for an heir. And the child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Whoever claims to other than his father and affiliates to other than his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither obligatory nor supererogatory deed is accepted from him."
"15161","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn Isa al-Tai narrated to us: Talhah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Amr ibn Kharijah, he said: I witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) his pilgrimage, and I was between the neck of the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while it was chewing its cud and its saliva flowed between my shoulders. Then I heard him say: Indeed Allah has given every possessor of a right his right. Indeed no bequest is permissible for an heir. The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. And whoever claims to other than his father or affiliates to other than his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither obligatory nor supererogatory deed is accepted from him."
"15162","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from Talhah Abu Muhammad, freed slave of Bahilah, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Amr ibn Kharijah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"15163","Ishaq ibn Khalawayh al-Wasiti narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Amr ibn Kharijah, he said: I was holding the bridle of the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while it was chewing its cud and its saliva flowed between my shoulders. Then I heard him say: Indeed Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has given every possessor of a right his right. Indeed no bequest is permissible for an heir. And the child belongs to the bed. And whoever claims to other than his father and affiliates to other than his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither obligatory nor supererogatory deed is accepted from him."
"15164","Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Said ibn Abi Arubah informed us, (ha), and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Amr ibn Kharijah, he said: I witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was addressing upon his mount at Mina, holding its bridle while it was chewing its cud, and its saliva flowed between my shoulders. Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, indeed Allah has apportioned to every person his share of inheritance, and no bequest is permissible for an heir. Indeed the child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Whoever claims to other than his father or takes allegiance to other than his masters out of dislike for them, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"15165","al-Sari ibn Sahl al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Rashid narrated to us: Mujjaah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Amr ibn Kharijah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"15166","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Amr ibn Kharijah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say in his sermon, while he was beneath the neck of his she-camel, and he mentioned the like of it, and he did not mention Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm."
"15167","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qatadah, from Amr ibn Kharijah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah has given every possessor of a right his right; no bequest is permissible for an heir. The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. And whoever claims to other than his father or affiliates to other than his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah; and he did not mention Shahr nor Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm."
"15168","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Amr ibn Kharijah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No bequest for an heir."
"15169","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us: Hafs narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Amr ibn Kharijah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"15170","Muhammad ibn Hammuyah al-Jawhari narrated to us: Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us: Amir ibn Mudrik narrated to us: al-Sari ibn Ismail narrated to us: Amir narrated to us, from Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us on the day of the Conquest until those far gathered to him, and he called out with a voice that made them hear. Then he said: O people, indeed Allah has done good to you and restored to every possessor of a right his right. Indeed there is no bequest for an heir after this station of mine. The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Whoever claims to other than his father or takes allegiance to other than his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people on the Day of Resurrection; neither obligatory nor supererogatory deed is accepted from him. Then he departed and the people departed."
"15171","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab: Kharijah ibn Amr narrated to me - and he was an ally of Abu Sufyan in Jahiliyyah - from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: O people, nothing of the spoils of the Muslims is lawful for me nor for anyone, weighing as much as this hair; and he took a hair from the hump of his she-camel, besides what Allah has ordained for me."
"15172","Amr ibn al-Faghwa al-Khuzai: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, the author of al-Maghazi, narrated to me: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Isa ibn Mamar, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-Faghwa al-Khuzai, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me, intending to send me with wealth to Abu Sufyan to distribute among Quraysh in Makkah after the Conquest. Then he said: Seek a companion. Then Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri came to me and said: It has reached me that you intend to go out and seek a companion, and I am your companion. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said: When you find a companion, inform me. So I informed him, and he said: Who? I said: Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri. Then he said: When he descends upon the land of his people, beware of him, for the sayer has said: Your Bakri brother, so do not trust him. So we went out until I came to al-Abwa. He said: I have a need among my people, so wait for me. I said: Rightly. When he turned away, I remembered the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I tightened my camel, then I went out hastening it, until when I was at al-Asafir, he intercepted me with a group. He said: And I hastened, and he heard me. When he saw that I had escaped him, they turned away, and he came to me and said: I had a need among my people. I said: Yes. And we went on until we arrived at Makkah, and I delivered the wealth to Abu Sufyan."
"15173","Amr ibn Hannah al-Ansari: Amr ibn Jafar al-Sadusi narrated to us: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: A man of the Ansar called Amr ibn Hannah came, and he used to recite incantations for snakebite. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, you forbade incantations, and I recite for snakebite. He said: Then recite it to me. So I recited it to him, and he said: There is no harm in this; these are covenants. He said: And a man of the Ansar came who used to recite for scorpion sting. Then he said: Whoever is able to benefit his brother, let him do so."
"15174","Amr ibn Ghaziyyah al-Ansari, an Aqabi: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding the naming of those who witnessed al-Aqabah for the pledge to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the Ansar, then among Banu Mazin ibn al-Najjar: Amr ibn Ghaziyyah ibn Thalabah ibn Khansa ibn Mandul ibn Ghanm ibn Mazin."
"15175","Abu al-Sanabil ibn Bakak ibn al-Harith ibn Umaylah ibn al-Sabbaq ibn Abd al-Dar, of the Muallafah, and his name is Amr: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Ishaq, of his lineage and name and that he is of the Muallafah."
"15176","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abu al-Sanabil ibn Bakak, he said: Subayah gave birth after the death of her husband by twenty-three or twenty-five; and when she became free she longed to marry. Then she was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If she does, then her term has ended."
"15177","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abu al-Sanabil ibn Bakak, he said: Subayah bint al-Harith gave birth after the death of her husband by twenty-three or twenty-seven nights. When she rose from her postnatal bleeding, she longed for marriage, and that was disapproved of her. Then that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If she does, then her term has ended."
"15178","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us: Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us: Ziyad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from al-Amash and Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abu al-Sanabil ibn Bakak, he said: Subayah gave birth after the death of her husband by twenty-three nights, then she longed to marry. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached and informed, and he said: If she does, then her term has been fulfilled."
"15179","Amr ibn al-Numan ibn Muqarrin al-Muzani: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Mualla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Amr ibn al-Numan ibn Muqarrin, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a gathering of the gatherings of the Ansar, and a man among them was known for foul speech. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Reviling the Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."
"15180","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from al-Numan ibn Amr ibn Muqarrin, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, supports the religion with the wicked man."
"15181","Amr ibn Sharahil: Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Mudrik narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah al-Qurashi narrated to us: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Ghaffar, from Amr ibn Sharahil, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, support Ali; O Allah, honor whoever honors Ali; O Allah, forsake whoever forsakes Ali - may Allah be pleased with him."
"15182","Amr ibn Uqaysh al-Ansari: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that Amr ibn Qays had usury in Jahiliyyah, and that usury prevented him from Islam until he would take it and then become Muslim. Then one day he came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at Uhud. Then he said to his people: Where is Sad ibn Muadh? They said: He is at Uhud. He said: Where is so-and-so? They said: At Uhud. Then he asked about his people? They said: They are at Uhud. So he took his sword and spear and wore his armor, then he came to Uhud. When the Muslims saw him, they said: Away from us, O Amr. He said: I have believed. Then he charged and fought until he was killed, and he was carried to his family wounded. Then Sad ibn Muadh entered upon him and said to his brother: Call him: Did you come in anger for Allah and His Messenger? He said: Yes. So he died and entered Paradise, and he never prayed at all."
"15183","Amr ibn Thalabah al-Juhani: Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abbadah al-Wasiti narrated to us, (ha), and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni al-Tustari narrated to us: al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, they both said: Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us: Wahb ibn Ata ibn Yazid narrated to us: al-Waddah ibn Salamah narrated to us, from his father, from Amr ibn Thalabah al-Juhani, he said: I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Sayyalah and became Muslim, and he wiped over my head. He said: A hundred years passed over Amr ibn Thalabah, and the place of the hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon his head never turned gray."
"15184","Amr ibn Atiyyah, not attributed: Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us: Shuayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Lahiah, from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amr ibn Atiyyah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed the land will be opened for you and you will be spared provision, so let none of you fail to play with his arrows."
"15185","Amr ibn Aws al-Thaqafi: Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Anbasah narrated to us: Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Amr ibn Dinar and Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from Amr ibn Aws al-Thaqafi, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever cuts the lote tree except from cultivation, Allah will build for him a house in the Fire."
"15186","Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti narrated to us: Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yala al-Taifi narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Aws, from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the delegation of Thaqif, and he used to come out to us at night and narrate to us. Then one night he was late for us, then he came out to us, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, you have been late for us tonight. Then he said: My portion of the Quran came upon me, and I disliked cutting it off until I finished it. When morning came, we asked the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) how they portioned the Quran? They said: Three, five, seven, nine, eleven, thirteen, and from Qaf and the Glorious Quran to the end of al-Mufassal is a good portion. Thus al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated it, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taifi, from Uthman ibn Amr ibn Aws, from his father, while Waki, Qurran ibn Tamam and others opposed him and narrated it from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Aws, from his grandfather Aws ibn Hudhayfah."
"15187","Amr al-Yamani: Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Muammal ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Sharik, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Amr al-Yamani, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent with me a voluntary sacrificial animal, and said: If any of it becomes incapacitated, then slaughter it, then dye its sandal in its blood and strike it upon its side, and leave it between the people and it."
"15188","Amr ibn Sawaa: Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us: Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Ayyash ibn Abbas al-Itbani, from Abu Mashar al-Himyari, from Amr ibn Sawaa al-Yafii, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seven I have cursed, and every prophet whose supplication is answered: The adder to the Book of Allah, the denier of the decree of Allah, the violator of the sanctity of Allah, the violator from my progeny of what Allah has forbidden, the abandoner of my sunnah, the monopolizer of the fay, and the tyrant with his authority to honor whom Allah has humiliated and humiliate whom Allah has honored."
"15189","Amr al-Bikali, and his companionship has been differed over: Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sulayman al-Dabbas narrated to us: Mujjaah ibn al-Zubayr al-Ataki narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, from Amr al-Bikali, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When you have rulers who command you with prayer, zakat, and jihad, then Allah has forbidden you from reviling them, and prayer behind them has become lawful for you."
"15190","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jami al-Attar narrated to us: Harun ibn Waqid al-Absi narrated to us: al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Tamimah, he said: I came to Sham seeking the obligatory duty, and there I was with a man around whom the people gathered. So I said: Who is this? They said: Amr al-Bikali; his hand was struck on the day of Yarmuk, the day the Romans were expelled from Sham. Then I heard him say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you have rulers who command you with prayer, zakat, and jihad in the cause of Allah, prayer behind them becomes lawful for you and reviling them is forbidden for you."
"15191","Amr ibn al-Harith al-Khuzai: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Ruhaym narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, the son-in-law of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the brother of his wife Juwayriyah bint al-Harith, he said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not leave at his death a dirham nor a dinar, nor a male nor female slave, nor anything except his white mule, his weapon, and land he left as charity."
"15192","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Yahya, from Amr ibn al-Harith, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left nothing except his weapon, his white mule, and land he made as charity."
"15193","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Musa narrated to us: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn al-Harith al-Khuzai, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not leave on the day he died except his weapon, his white mule, and land he made as charity."
"15194","Amr al-Jinni: Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Amr al-Jinni narrated to me, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he recited Surat al-Najm and prostrated, so I prostrated with him."
"15195","Amr ibn Madi Karib al-Zubaydi, kunyah Abu Thawr: Abu Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Jumahi said: Amr ibn Madi Karib ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Asim ibn Amr ibn Zayd, and he is Munabbih. And of the reports of Amr ibn Madi Karib."
"15196","Abu Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sallam said: Amr ibn Madi Karib had exploits in Jahiliyyah, and he reached Islam; he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Umar ibn al-Khattab directed him to Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with them both, to al-Qadisiyyah, and he had fine valor there. Umar wrote to Sad ibn Abi Waqqas of two thousand men: Amr ibn Madi Karib, and Talhah ibn Khuwaylid, and he is Talhah al-Asadi; so consult them in war but do not appoint them over anything."
"15197","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us: Said ibn Mansur narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: I saw Amr ibn Madi Karib on the day of al-Qadisiyyah urging the people to fight, and he was saying: O people, be fierce lions, strong and hostile; the Persian is but a goat when he casts his yoke. He said: While he was thus, a horseman of the horsemen of Persia aimed at him with his arrows. So it was said to him: O Abu Thawr, this horseman has aimed his arrows at you. He said: So he shot him and struck the curve of Amr's bow and broke it. Then Amr charged him and stabbed him, breaking his spine. Then he alighted to him and took two bracelets of gold upon him and a garment of brocade. He said: So that was handed over to him."
"15198","Abu Khalifah narrated to us, he said: He said: Muhammad ibn Sallam: One of our companions narrated to me, he said: Salman ibn Rabiah urged the horses, and Amr ibn Madi Karib passed upon a horse of his. Then Salman said to him: This is a crossbreed. Then Amr said: A purebred. He said: So he ordered it and it was made thirsty, then he called for a tub of water and called the noble horses, and they drank. Then the horse of Amr came and folded its forelegs and drank, and this is the doing of the crossbreed. He said: So he said to him: Do you not see? He said: Yes; the crossbreed knows the crossbreed. Then it reached Umar, and he wrote to him: It has reached me what you said to your commander, and it has reached me that you have a sword you call al-Simsamah, and I have a decisive sword. By Allah, if I placed it upon your head, I would not lift it until I reach something of its inside. So if you wish to know whether what I say is true, then repeat."
"15199","What Amr ibn Madi Karib narrated: Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from Amr ibn Samar, from Abu Tawq Sharahil ibn al-Qaqa, he said: I heard Amr ibn Madi Karib report, saying: Praise be to Allah that we, not long ago when we performed pilgrimage, used to say a rough uneven cry; and today we say as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us: At Your service, O Allah, at Your service; at Your service, no partner have You; at Your service, indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; no partner have You. And we used to prevent the people from standing at Arafat in Jahiliyyah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to come between them and the interior of Uranah, for their station was at the interior of Muhassir on the evening of Arafah, fearing the jinn would snatch them. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: They are but your brothers when they become Muslim."
"15200","Those named Umayr: Umayr ibn Qatadah al-Laythi Abu Ubayd, and he is Umayr ibn Qatadah ibn Said ibn Amir ibn Juda ibn Layth ibn Bakr ibn Abd Manah ibn Kinanah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Mudrikah ibn Ilyas ibn Mudar ibn Nizar ibn Mad ibn Adnan: Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us: al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Azraq narrated to us: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Sinan, that Ubayd ibn Umayr al-Laythi narrated to him, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the Farewell Pilgrimage: Indeed the allies of Allah are those who pray and who establish the five prayers which Allah has ordained upon His servants, and fast Ramadan seeking reward for its fast, and give zakat with a content soul seeking reward for it, and avoid the major sins which Allah has forbidden. Then a man of his Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, how many are the major sins? He said: They are nine, the greatest of them: associating with Allah, killing the believing soul without right, fleeing on the day of battle, slandering the chaste woman, sorcery, devouring the wealth of the orphan, devouring usury, disobedience to the two Muslim parents, and violating the Sacred House, your qiblah, living and dead. No man dies who has not done these major sins, and establishes the prayer, and gives the zakat, except he will accompany Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the midst of a Paradise whose gates are leaves of gold."
"15201","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us: Isa ibn Khalid al-Yamami narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The major sins are seven: associating with Allah, killing the believing soul, fleeing from battle, devouring usury, devouring the wealth of the orphan, disobedience to parents, and deviation in the Sacred House."
"15202","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Hawtharah ibn Ashras narrated to us: Suwayd Abu Hatim, the food merchant, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, from his grandfather, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, which prayer is most excellent? He said: Lengthy standing. He said: Which charity is most excellent? He said: The effort of the poor. He said: Which of the believers is most complete? He said: The best of them in character."
"15203","Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us: Rifdah ibn Qudaah al-Awzai narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands with every takbir in the obligatory prayer."
"15204","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Khunays, from Abu Badr, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: There was a question in my mind that had grieved me; I had not asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it, nor heard anyone ask him about it. So I used to watch for him, and one day I entered while he was performing ablution, and I found him in two states I loved to find him in: I found him free and in good spirits. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to ask you. He said: Yes, ask whatever comes to you. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is faith? He said: Generosity and patience. I said: Which of the believers are best in faith? He said: The best of them in character. I said: Which of the Muslims are best in Islam? He said: The one from whose hand and tongue the Muslims are safe. I said: Which jihad is most excellent? Then he lowered his head and remained silent long, until I feared I had burdened him, and I wished I had not asked him, though I had heard him say yesterday: Indeed the greatest of people in crime among the Muslims is he who asks about something not forbidden upon them, and it becomes forbidden because of his question. So I said: I seek refuge in Allah from the anger of Allah and the anger of His Messenger. Then he raised his head and said: How did you say? I said: Which jihad is most excellent? He said: A word of justice before an unjust ruler."
"15205","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Attar al-Hamdani narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us: Shihab ibn Khirash al-Hawshabi narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Mujahid, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them and said: May Allah brighten a man who hears my saying and retains it; for many a bearer of understanding has no understanding, and many a bearer of understanding conveys it to one more understanding than he."
"15206","Umayr Dhu Marran al-Hamdani: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Safati narrated to us: Hamid ibn Yahya narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mujalid ibn Said ibn Umayr Dhi Marran, from his father, from his grandfather Umayr, he said: The letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Merciful, from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Umayr Dhu Marran, and whoever of Hamdan has become Muslim: Peace be upon you, for I praise to you Allah besides Whom there is no god. To proceed: It has reached us of your Islam since our coming from the land of Rome, so receive glad tidings, for Allah has guided you with His guidance. And when you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and establish the prayer, and give the zakat, then for you is the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger over your blood and your wealth and over the land of Alyun upon which you became Muslim, its plain and its mountain, its springs and its pasture, without being wronged nor restricted. For charity is not lawful for Muhammad nor for his household. And Malik ibn Murarah al-Rahawi has guarded the unseen, fulfilled the trust, and conveyed the message. So I enjoin upon you good regarding him, O Dhu Marran, for he is regarded among his people; and may your Lord love you."
"15207","Umayr ibn Habib ibn Khumashah al-Ansari then al-Khatmi: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Dabbi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Jafar al-Khatmi, that his grandfather Umayr ibn Habib ibn Khumashah had companionship; he pledged to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at puberty, and he enjoined his son, saying: Beware of sitting with fools, for sitting with them is a disease. Whoever forbears toward the fool rejoices in his forbearance, and whoever loves him regrets. And whoever is not content with the little the fool brings will be content with the much. And whoever is patient over what he dislikes attains what he loves. And when one of you intends to enjoin good or forbid evil, let him prepare himself with patience over harm, and let him trust in reward from Allah, the Mighty and Majestic; for whoever trusts in reward from Allah will not feel the touch of harm."
"15208","Umayr ibn Sad al-Ansari, reports of Umayr ibn Sad: Muhammad ibn al-Rubal al-Adami al-Shirazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Hakim al-Shirazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Hakim al-Razi narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Harun ibn Antarah narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from Umayr ibn Sad, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, sent Umayr ibn Sad as governor over Hims, and he remained a year with no news reaching him. Then Umar said to his scribe: Write to Umayr; by Allah, I see him only as having betrayed us. When this letter of mine reaches you, come, and come with what you have collected of the Muslims when you look into this letter of mine. He said: So Umayr took his sack and placed therein his provision and his bowl, and hung his water skin, and took his staff. Then he came walking from Hims until he entered Madinah. He said: He arrived with his color pale, his face dusty, and his hair long. Then he entered upon Umar and said: Peace be upon you, O Commander of the Believers, and the mercy of Allah. Then Umar said: What is your affair? Then Umayr said: What do you see of my affair? Do you not see me sound of body, pure of blood, with the world dragging it by its horn? He said: And what is with you? And Umar thought he had brought wealth. Then he said: With me is my sack in which I place my provision, and my bowl in which I eat, and wash therein my head and my clothes; and my water skin in which I carry my ablution water and my drink; and my staff upon which I lean and strive thereby against an enemy if he confronts me. By Allah, the world is but a follower of my belongings. Umar said: So you came walking? He said: Yes. Umar said: Had you none to volunteer for you a mount to ride? He said: They did not, nor did I ask them that. He said: Evil are the Muslims you left. Then Umayr said to him: Fear Allah, O Umar, for Allah has forbidden you backbiting; I saw them praying the dawn prayer. He said: Then where is your share, and what did you do? Then he said: What is your question, O Commander of the Believers? Then Umar said: Glory be to Allah. Then Umayr said: Were I not afraid to grieve you, I would not inform you. You sent me until I reached the land, and I gathered the righteous of its people and entrusted them with collecting their fay. Then when they collected of them, I placed it in its places. And had any of it reached you, I would have brought it to you. He said: So you brought us nothing? He said: No. He said: Renew a covenant for Umayr. He said: That is something; I shall not work for you nor for anyone after you. By Allah, I was not safe; indeed I was not safe. Had I said to a Christian: May Allah disgrace you, this is what exposed me, O Umar. And my most wretched days are the day I allied with you, O Umar. Then he sought his permission, and he permitted him, and he returned to his house. He said: And between him and Madinah were miles. Then Umar said when Umayr departed: I see him only as having betrayed us. Then he sent a man called al-Harith, and gave him a hundred dinars, and said to him: Go until you alight with him as a guest; if you see trace of anything, come back, and if you see severe hardship, give him these hundred dinars. So al-Harith went, and there was Umayr sitting boiling his shirt beside the wall. Then the man greeted him, and Umayr said to him: Alight, may Allah have mercy on you. So he alighted, then he asked him and said: From where have you come? He said: From Madinah. He said: How did you leave the Commander of the Believers? He said: Well. He said: How did you leave the Muslims? He said: Well. He said: How did you leave the Commander of the Believers? He said: Well. He said: Does he not establish the prescribed punishments? He said: Yes; he struck a son of his who committed indecency, and he died of his beating. Then Umayr said: O Allah, aid Umar, for I know him only as intense in his love for You. He said: So he stayed three days, and they had only a loaf of barley which they singled him out with, going hungry, until hardship befell them. Then Umayr said to him: O man, you have made us hungry; if you see fit to move from us, do so. He said: Then he brought out the dinars and gave them to him. Then he said: The Commander of the Believers sent them to you, so seek help thereby. He said: Then he cried out and said: I have no need of them; return them. Then his wife said to him: If you need them, else place them in their places. Then Umayr said: By Allah, I have nothing to place them in. So his wife tore the lower part of her garment and gave him a rag, and he placed them therein. Then he went out and distributed them among the sons of martyrs and the poor. Then he returned, while the messenger thought he would give him something thereof. Then Umayr said to him: Convey from me greetings to the Commander of the Believers. Then al-Harith returned to Umar. Then he said: What did you see? He said: I saw, O Commander of the Believers, severe hardship. He said: Then what did he do with the dinars? He said: I do not know. He said: And Umar wrote to him: When this letter of mine reaches you, do not put it from your hand until you come. So he came to Umar and entered upon him. Then Umar said to him: What did you do with the dinars? He said: I did what I did; what is your question about them? He said: I adjure you to inform me what you did with them? He said: I sent them ahead for myself. He said: May Allah have mercy on you. Then he ordered a wasq of food and two garments. Then he said: As for the food, I have no need of it; I have left in the house two sa of barley; until I eat that, Allah will bring provision. And he did not take the food. And as for the two garments, he said: The wife of so-and-so is bare, so he took them and returned to his house. Then he did not remain but died, may Allah have mercy on him. Then that reached Umar, and it grieved him, and he asked mercy for him. Then he went out walking, with walkers with him, to Baqi al-Gharqad. Then he said to his companions: Let every man of you wish a wish. Then a man said: I wish, O Commander of the Believers, that I had wealth and would free so-and-so for the sake of Allah. And another said: I wish that I had wealth and would spend in the cause of Allah. And another said: I wish that I had strength and would draw with a bucket from Zamzam for the pilgrims of the House of Allah. Then Umar said: I wish that I had a man like Umayr to seek help with in the affairs of the Muslims."
"15209","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr: I heard Abdullah ibn Yazid, or Zayd, narrating from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, that Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to Umayr ibn Sad al-Ansari, while he was over Hims, forbidding the people to pray two rakahs after Asr. Then Abu al-Darda said: As for me, I shall not leave them; whoever wishes to submit, let him submit."
"15210","What Umayr ibn Sad narrated: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Rabiah Fahd ibn Awf narrated to us, (ha), and Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Salih al-Marwazi narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, they both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Abu Talhah al-Khawlani, he said: We entered upon Umayr ibn Sad at the discharge of the people of Palestine, and contagion was mentioned before him. Then he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no contagion, nor omen, nor hamah."
"15211","Umayr ibn Amir Abu Dawud al-Mazini, a Badri: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then among Banu Mazin ibn al-Najjar, then among Banu Khansa ibn Mabdhul ibn Amr ibn Ghanm ibn Mazin: Umayr, and his kunyah Abu Dawud ibn Amir ibn Malik ibn Khansa ibn Mabdhul."
"15212","What Abu Dawud al-Mazini narrated: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they both said: Abu Bakr al-Ayan Muhammad ibn Abi Attab narrated to us: Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Musa Abu Ghaziyyah al-Ansari narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Said ibn Jubayr, from Jafar ibn Hamzah ibn Abi Dawud al-Mazini, from his father, from Abu Dawud al-Mazini - and Abu Dawud was of the people of Badr - he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he entered the mosque of Dhu al-Hulayfah and prayed therein four rakahs. Then he entered ihram in the mosque, and those in the mosque heard him and said: He entered ihram from the mosque. Then he entered ihram when he mounted his mount, and he who was at the mosque said: He entered ihram when his mount stood straight with him. Then when he stood upon al-Bayda, he entered ihram, and those upon al-Bayda heard him, and they said: He entered ihram from al-Bayda. And all of them spoke the truth."
"15213","Umayr ibn Abi Waqqas al-Zuhri, brother of Sad, of the first Emigrants, martyred on the day of Badr: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, regarding the naming of those martyred on the day of Badr among the Muslims, of Quraysh, then of Banu Zuhrah: Umayr ibn Abi Waqqas."
"15214","Abu Shuayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, regarding the naming of those martyred on the day of Badr among the Muslims, then of Quraysh, then of Banu Zuhrah ibn Kilab: Umayr ibn Abi Waqqas ibn Uhayb ibn Abd Manaf ibn Zuhrah."
"15215","al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those martyred with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the Muslims, then of Quraysh, then of Banu Zuhrah: Umayr ibn Abi Waqqas."
"15216","Umayr ibn Wahb al-Jumahi: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, he said: When the idolaters returned to Makkah from Badr, and Allah, the Exalted, had killed whom He killed of them, Umayr ibn Wahb came until he reached Safwan ibn Umayyah in al-Hijr. Then Safwan said: May Allah make life ugly after the slain of Badr. Then Umayr said: Yes; by Allah, there is no good in life after. Were it not for a debt upon me for which I find no payment, and my dependents behind me for whom I find nothing, I would enter upon Muhammad and kill him if I filled my eyes of him; for I have with them a pretext, saying: I came for this captive son of mine. Then Safwan rejoiced at his saying and said: Your debt is upon me, and your dependents are like my dependents in maintenance, if anything suffices me and we are unable for them. So Safwan carried him and equipped him with the sword of Safwan, and it was polished and poisoned. And Umayr said to Safwan: Conceal me for nights. Then Umayr came until he arrived at Madinah, and alighted at the door of the mosque, and hobbled his mount, and took the sword toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Umar ibn al-Khattab looked at him while he was among a group of the Ansar talking about the Battle of Badr and thanking Allah's blessing. When Umar saw Umayr ibn Wahb with the sword, he was alarmed by him and said: With you is the dog, this enemy of Allah who incited between us and estimated us for the people. Then Umar stood and entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This is Umayr ibn Wahb; he has entered the mosque with weapons, and he is the wicked traitor, O Messenger of Allah; do not trust him. He said: Bring him in to me. Then Umar and Umayr entered, and he ordered his Companions to enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and then guard against Umayr when he entered upon them. Then Umar ibn al-Khattab and Umayr ibn Wahb came and entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with Umar having his sword. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umar: Step back from him. When he drew near him, Umayr greeted him: Good morning - and it is the greeting of the people of Jahiliyyah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has honored us above your greeting and made our greeting al-Salam, and it is the greeting of the people of Paradise. Then Umayr said: Your covenant with it is recent. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has replaced it for us with better than it. What has brought you, O Umayr? He said: I came regarding my captive with you, so treat me leniently regarding my captive, for you are the kin and family. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then what of the sword upon your neck? Then Umayr said: May Allah make swords ugly; did they avail us of anything? I forgot it while it was upon my neck when I alighted; and by my life, I have other concern. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tell me the truth, what has brought you? He said: I came only regarding my captive. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then what did you stipulate to Safwan ibn Umayyah al-Jumahi in al-Hijr? Then Umayr was alarmed and said: What did I stipulate to him? He said: You undertook for him to kill me, upon his maintaining your sons and paying your debt, and Allah stands between you and that. Then Umayr said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah, and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. We used, O Messenger of Allah, to deny you the revelation and what comes to you from heaven. And this talk between me and Safwan in al-Hijr, as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, none witnessed it but I and he. Then Allah informed you of it. So I believe in Allah and His Messenger, and praise be to Allah Who brought me to this station. Then the Muslims rejoiced when Allah guided him. And Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: A pig was more beloved to me than he when he appeared, and today he is more beloved to me than some of my sons. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sit, we shall console you. And he said: Teach your brother the Quran, and release to him his captive. And he said: O Messenger of Allah, I strove as I could to extinguish the light of Allah, so praise be to Allah Who brought me this path. So permit me to join Quraysh and call them to Islam, that Allah may guide them and rescue them from destruction. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him, and he joined Makkah. And Safwan would say to Quraysh in their gatherings: Receive glad tidings of a victory that will make you forget the Battle of Badr. And he would ask every rider arriving from Madinah whether there was any event therein. And he hoped for what Umayr ibn Wahb had said, until a man of the people of Madinah arrived. Then Safwan asked of him, and he said: He has become Muslim. Then the idolaters met him and said: He has apostatized. And Safwan said: It is upon me never to benefit him with maintenance nor ever speak to him a word. And Umayr came to them and called them to Islam and advised them, and many people became Muslim."
"15217","Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, he said: Umayr ibn Wahb al-Jumahi sat with Safwan ibn Umayyah after the calamity of the people of Badr of Quraysh in al-Hijr shortly, and he was of those who harmed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions, and they met from him hardship while they were in Makkah. And his son Wahb ibn Umayr was among the captives of the companions of Badr. He said: Then they mentioned the companions of the well by their calamities. Then Safwan said: By Allah, there is no life after them. And Umayr ibn Wahb said: You have spoken the truth. By Allah, were it not for a debt upon me for which I have no payment, and dependents I fear destitution for after me, I would ride to Muhammad until I killed him; for I have regarding them a pretext: my son with them is a captive in their hands. Then Safwan seized it and said: Your debt is upon me; I shall pay it from you, and your dependents are with my dependents, their like as long as they remain; nothing suffices me while we are unable for them. Umayr said: Conceal my affair and yours. He said: I shall. He said: Then Umayr ordered his sword, and it was sharpened and poisoned. Then he set out to Madinah. While Umar ibn al-Khattab was in Madinah among a group of the Muslims recalling the day of Badr, and what Allah honored them with, and what He showed them of their enemy, he looked at Umayr ibn Wahb alighting at the door of the mosque girt with the sword. Then he said: This dog, the enemy of Allah, Umayr ibn Wahb, has come only for evil; this is he who incited between us and estimated us for the people on the day of Badr. Then Umar entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this enemy of Allah, Umayr ibn Wahb, has come girt with the sword. He said: Then bring him in. Then Umar came until he took the sword's baldric upon his neck and seized him thereby. And Umar said to men of those with him of the Ansar: Enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sit with him, and beware this dog against him, for he is not to be trusted. Then he entered with him upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with Umar holding his sword's baldric. Then he said: Release him, O Umar; come near, O Umayr. Then he drew near and said: Good morning - and it was the greeting of the people of Jahiliyyah among them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has honored us with a greeting better than your greeting, O Umayr: al-Salam, the greeting of the people of Paradise. Then he said: By Allah, O Muhammad, your covenant with it is recent. He said: Then what has brought you? He said: I came for this captive in your hands, so do good to him. He said: Then what of the sword upon your neck? He said: May Allah make swords ugly; did they avail anything? He said: Tell me the truth, what have you come for? He said: I came only for this. He said: Rather you sat, you and Safwan ibn Umayyah, in al-Hijr, and you recalled the companions of the well of Quraysh. Then you said: Were it not for a debt upon me and my dependents, I would go out until I killed Muhammad. Then Safwan undertook for you your debt and your dependents upon your killing me, and Allah stands between you and that. Umayr said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah. We used, O Messenger of Allah, to deny you what you brought us of heaven's news and what descends upon you of revelation. And this affair none witnessed but I and Safwan. By Allah, I know none informed you of it but Allah. So praise be to Allah Who guided me to Islam and brought me this path. Then he bore witness to the testimony of truth. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Instruct your brother in his religion, and teach him the Quran, and release to him his captive. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, I strove to extinguish the light of Allah, severe in harm to whoever was upon Allah's religion. And I love that you permit me to proceed to Makkah and call them to Allah and to Islam, that Allah may guide them; else I shall harm them as I used to harm your Companions in their religion. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him, and he joined Makkah. And Safwan, when Umayr ibn Wahb departed, said to Quraysh: Receive glad tidings of an event coming to you now that will make you forget the Battle of Badr. And Safwan would ask the riders about him, until a rider arrived and informed him of his Islam. Then he swore never to speak to him nor ever benefit him. Then when Umayr arrived at Makkah, he dwelt therein calling to Islam and harming whoever opposed him severely. And many people became Muslim at his hands."
"15218","al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, he said: When the idolaters returned to Makkah, and Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, had killed whom He killed of them, Umayr ibn Wahb al-Jumahi came until he sat with Safwan ibn Umayyah in al-Hijr. Then he said: May Allah make life ugly after the slain of Badr. He said: Yes; by Allah, there is no good in life after them. Were it not for a debt upon me for which I find no payment, and dependents for whom I leave nothing, I would travel to Muhammad and kill him if I filled my eye of him; for I have with him a pretext to plead to him, saying: I came for this captive son of mine. Then Safwan rejoiced at his saying and said: Your debt is upon me, and your dependents are like my dependents in maintenance; nothing suffices me while I am unable for them. So Safwan carried him and equipped him, and ordered Umayr's sword to be polished and poisoned. And Umayr said to Safwan: Conceal me days. Then Umayr came until he arrived at Madinah, and alighted at the door of the mosque, and hobbled his mount, and took the sword. Then he headed for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, looked at him while he was among a group of the Ansar talking about the Battle of Badr and mentioning Allah's blessing therein. When Umar saw him with the sword, he was alarmed, and Umar said: This dog, this enemy of Allah who incited between us on the day of Badr and estimated us for the people. Then Umar stood and entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This is Umayr ibn Wahb; he has entered the mosque girt with his sword, and he is the traitor, the wicked, O Prophet of Allah; do not trust him. He said: Bring him in. Then Umar went out and ordered his Companions to enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and then guard against Umayr when he entered upon them. Then Umar and Umayr entered until they entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with Umayr having his sword. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umar: Step back from him. When Umayr drew near him, he said: Good morning - and it is the greeting of the people of Jahiliyyah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has honored us above your greeting and made our greeting the greeting of the people of Paradise, and it is al-Salam. Then Umayr said: Your covenant with it is recent. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has replaced for us better than it. What has brought you, O Umayr? He said: I came regarding our captives, for you are the kin and family. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then what of the sword upon your neck? Umayr said: May Allah make swords ugly; did they avail us of anything? I only forgot it upon my neck when I alighted; and by my life, I have thereby a lesson. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tell me the truth, what has brought you? He said: I came only regarding my captive. He said: Then what did you stipulate to Safwan ibn Umayyah in al-Hijr? Then Umayr was alarmed and said: What did I stipulate to him? He said: You undertook for him to kill me, upon his maintaining your sons and paying your debt, and Allah stands between you and that. Umayr said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah, and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. We used, O Messenger of Allah, to deny you the revelation and what comes to you from heaven. And this talk was between me and Safwan in al-Hijr, as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said; none witnessed it but he and I. Then Allah informed you of it. So I believe in Allah and His Messenger, and praise be to Allah Who brought me to this path. Then the Muslims rejoiced with him when Allah guided him. And Umar said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the pig was more beloved to me than Umayr when he appeared, and he is more beloved to me than some of my sons. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sit, O Umayr, we shall console you. And he said to his Companions: Teach your brother the Quran and release to him his captive. Then Umayr said: O Messenger of Allah, I strove with what I could to extinguish the light of Allah, so praise be to Allah Who brought me and guided me. So permit me to join Quraysh and call them to Allah and to Islam, that Allah may guide them and rescue them from destruction. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him, and he joined Makkah. And Safwan ibn Umayyah would say to Quraysh in their gatherings: Receive glad tidings of a victory that will make you forget the Battle of Badr. And he would ask every rider arriving from Madinah whether there was any event therein. And he hoped for what he had said, until a man of Madinah arrived. Then Safwan ibn Umayyah asked of him, and he said: He has become Muslim. Then the idolaters cursed him and said: He has apostatized. And Safwan said: It is upon me to Allah never to benefit him with maintenance, nor ever speak to him a word from my head. And Umayr came to them and called them to Islam and advised them to his utmost, and many people became Muslim."
"15219","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Askar narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman informed us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, I know him only from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Wahb ibn Umayr witnessed Uhud as a disbeliever, and he was struck by a wound, and he was among the slain. Then a man of the Ansar passed by him and recognized him, and placed his sword in his belly until it emerged from his back, then left him. When night entered and cold befell him, he joined Makkah and recovered. Then he and Safwan ibn Umayyah gathered in al-Hijr, and Wahb said: Were it not for my dependents and a debt upon me, I would love to be the one to kill Muhammad. Then Safwan said to him: Then how would you do? He said: I am a swift runner none catches; I shall come to him and deceive him, then strike him with the sword, then join the horses, and none will catch me. Then Safwan said to him: Your dependents are with my dependents, and your debt is upon me. So he went out sharpening his sword and poisoning it. Then he went out to Madinah intending only to kill the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he arrived at Madinah, Umar ibn al-Khattab saw him, and that distressed him and grieved him. Then he said to the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I have seen Wahb, and his coming suspicions me; and he is a traitorous man, so surround your Prophet. Then the Muslims surrounded the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Wahb came and stood upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Good morning, O Muhammad. He said: Allah has replaced for us better than it. He said: My covenant with you is that you speak of it admiringly. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What has brought you? He said: I came to ransom your captives. He said: What of the sword? He said: We carried them on the day of Badr, but we neither prospered nor succeeded. He said: Then what is the thing you said to Safwan in al-Hijr: Were it not for my dependents and a debt upon me, I would be the one to kill Muhammad myself? Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed him of his affair. Then Wahb said: Hah, how did you say? Then he repeated upon him. Wahb said: You used to inform us news of the people of earth, and we denied you; I see you inform news of the people of heaven. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah. He said: O Messenger of Allah, give me your turban. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him his turban. Then he went out to Makkah. Then Umar said: He arrived while he was more hateful to me than the pig, then he returned while he is more beloved to me than some of my children."
"15220","Umayr ibn Salamah al-Damri, and he is Umayr ibn Salamah ibn Muntab ibn Talhah ibn Judayy ibn Damrah ibn Bakr ibn Abd Manah ibn Kinanah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Mudrikah ibn Ilyas ibn Mudar ibn Nizar ibn Mad ibn Adnan: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us with this lineage: Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Ziyad al-Bakkai, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Yasar."
"15221","Umayr al-Abdi Abu al-Ashath: Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Ashath ibn Umayr al-Abdi, from his father, he said: The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When they intended to depart, they said: You have retained from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) all you heard, so ask him about nabidh. Then they came to him? Then they said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in an unhealthy land; nothing suits us therein except drink. He said: And what is your drink? They said: Nabidh. He said: And in what do you drink it? They said: In the hollowed stump. Then he said: Do not drink in the hollowed stump. Then they said: By Allah, our people will not agree with us upon this. Then they returned and asked him, and he said to them the like of that. Then they returned, and he said: Do not drink in the hollowed stump, lest a man of you be struck a blow from which he remains lame until the Day of Resurrection. Then they laughed. Then he said: And what do you laugh at? They said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One Who sent you with truth, we drank in a hollowed stump of ours, and some of us rose against others, and this one was struck a blow from which he remains lame until the Day of Resurrection."
"15222","Umayr father of Abu Bakr: Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, they both said: Abu Hafs ibn Ali narrated to us: Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu Bakr ibn Umayr, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, the Exalted, has promised me to admit of my ummah three hundred thousand to Paradise. Then Umayr said: O Prophet of Allah, increase us. Then Umar said: Enough, O Umayr. Then he said: What have we to do with you, O son of al-Khattab? What is it to you that Allah admit us to Paradise? Then Umar said: Indeed Allah, Majestic and Mighty, if He wills, admits the people to Paradise with one handful or one scoop. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umar has spoken the truth."
"15223","Umayr ibn Umayyah: Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us: Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Ayyub, that Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to him, that al-Salm ibn Yazid and Yazid ibn Ishaq narrated to him, from Umayr ibn Umayyah, that he had a sister, and when he went out to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she harmed him regarding him and reviled the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she was an idolater. Then one day he wrapped a sword for her, then came to her and placed it upon her and killed her. Then her sons stood and cried out and said: We know who killed her; shall our mother be killed? And these are a people who have idolatrous fathers and mothers. When Umayr feared they would kill other than her killer, he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. Then he said: Did you kill your sister? He said: Yes. He said: And why? He said: She used to harm me regarding you. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to her sons and asked them, and they named other than her killer. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed them of him and declared her blood void. They said: Hearing and obeying."
"15224","Umayr, freed slave of Abi al-Lahm al-Ghifari, and the name of Abi al-Lahm is Abdullah ibn Abd ibn Malik ibn Abdullah ibn Affan; and Abi al-Lahm was a poet, and Umayr witnessed the conquest of Khaybar; and he was only called Abi al-Lahm because he abstained from eating meat. al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, (ha), and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: al-Qanabi narrated to us, they both said: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd, he said: I heard Umayr, freed slave of Abi al-Lahm, say: My master ordered me to dry meat in strips, and a poor man came to me, and I fed him of it. Then he knew and beat me. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. Then he called him and said: Why did you beat him? He said: He feeds food without my ordering him. He said: The reward is between you both."
"15225","al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhajir ibn Qunfudh, from Umayr, freed slave of Abi al-Lahm, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the stones of oil, praying for rain, raising the insides of his palms."
"15226","127 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from his father Ishaq ibn al-Harith, from his uncle Ishaq ibn Abd Allah, and from Abu Bakr ibn Zayd, from Umayr, the freed slave of Abi al-Lahm, he said: I came with my masters to Madinah intending emigration, until when we drew near Madinah they left me behind with their baggage and departed, and severe hunger befell me. Then one of those who had come out of Madinah passed by me and said: If you entered one of the walled orchards of Madinah you would get some of its fruit. Umayr said: So I entered a walled orchard among the orchards of Madinah and cut two clusters from its date-palms. Then the owner of the orchard came to me and took me out until he brought me to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He asked me about my affair and I informed him. Then he said to me: Which of the two is better So I pointed to one of them, then he ordered me and I took it, and he ordered the owner of the orchard and he took the other, and he let me go free."
"15227","128 - Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated, Ribi ibn Ibrahim narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, my father narrated to me, from his uncle, and from Abu Bakr ibn Zayd, that they both heard Umayr, the freed slave of Abi al-Lahm, saying: I came with my masters intending emigration until we drew near Madinah, then he mentioned something like it."
"15228","129 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from his father, from his uncle, and from a man of Quraysh called Abu Bakr ibn Zayd, from Umayr, the freed slave of Abi al-Lahm, he said: I came with my masters intending emigration, then he mentioned something like it."
"15229","130 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, (ha) and Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated, both said: Ibn Lahiah narrated, Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh narrated, from Umayr, the freed slave of Abi al-Lahm, he said: I used to graze livestock at Dhat al-Jaysh and neediness befell me, so I mentioned that to one of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he directed me to a walled orchard belonging to one of the Ansar. So I cut some clusters from it, then they seized me and took me to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I informed him of my need, so he gave me one cluster and returned the rest to its people."
"15230","131 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Hisham ibn Sad narrated, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Umayr, the freed slave of Abi al-Lahm, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of Khaybar while I was an owned slave, and I said: Give me. So he gave me a sword and said: Gird yourself with it. So I took it and girded myself with it and it fell to the ground. Then he gave me from the lowly household goods."
"15231","132 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Muhajir ibn Qunfudh narrated, from Umayr, the freed slave of Abi al-Lahm, he said: I raided with my master at Khaybar and witnessed its conquest, so I asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to allot a share to me, so he gave me from the lowly goods and did not allot a share to me."
"15232","133 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Umayr, the freed slave of Abi al-Lahm, he said: I witnessed Khaybar with my masters, then the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered me and I girded myself with a sword, and I was dragging it. He was informed that I am an owned slave, so he ordered for me something from the lowly goods."
"15233","134 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, Nasr, meaning Ibn Tarif, narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Umayr, the freed slave of Abi al-Lahm, he said: I presented to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a ruqyah I used to recite for madness, and he kept saying: Take such-and-such from it and add such-and-such to it."
"15234","135 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Umayr, the freed slave of Abi al-Lahm, he said: I presented to him, meaning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a ruqyah I used to recite for the insane in the pre-Islamic period, and he said: Drop such-and-such from it and drop such-and-such from it, and recite with such-and-such from it."
"15235","Those named Adi. Adi ibn Hatim al-Tai, kunya Abu Tarif, he used to live in Kufah. Mention of his lineage. 136 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Abu Ubayd al-Qasim ibn Sallam, he said: Hatim of Tayy is ibn Abd Allah ibn Sad ibn al-Hashraj ibn Imri al-Qays ibn Adi ibn Akhram."
"15236","137 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad al-Yazidi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sad narrated, from al-Waqidi, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died while Adi ibn Hatim was over the charities of his people, meaning an agent of the Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"15237","Mention of his Islam. 138 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi narrated to us, Salih ibn Malik al-Khuwarizmi narrated, Abd al-Ala ibn Abi al-Musawir narrated, Amir al-Shabi informed me, he said: Adi ibn Hatim al-Tai came to Kufah, so I came to him with some of the people of Kufah and we said to him: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was sent with prophethood, and I do not know anyone among the Arabs who was more hateful toward him or more averse to him than me, until I joined the Romans and became Christian among them. Then when there reached me what he calls to of good character and what had gathered to him of people, I set out until I came to him. I stood before him, and with him were Suhayb, Bilal and Salman. He said: O Adi ibn Hatim, accept Islam and you will be safe. I said: Akh akh. Then I knelt and sat and joined my knee to his knee, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam He said: You believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, and you believe in the decree, its good and its evil, its sweet and its bitter. O Adi ibn Hatim, the Hour will not come until the treasures of Khosrau and Caesar are opened. O Adi ibn Hatim, the Hour will not come until the lone woman rider comes from al-Harrah, and there was no Kufah that day, until she circumambulates this Kabah without a guard. O Adi ibn Hatim, the Hour will not come until the bag of wealth goes around and is carried around and finds no one to accept it, so he strikes it against the ground and says: Would that you had never been, would that you were dust."
"15238","And from his reports. 139 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, that Adi ibn Hatim said: A man said when Uthman was killed: Two goats will not butt heads over it. So I said: Yes indeed, and many eyes will be gouged out over it."
"15239","Mention of his death. 140 - Musa ibn Harun ibn Abd Allah al-Hammal narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying: Adi ibn Hatim al-Tai, kunya Abu Tarif, died in Kufah in the time of al-Mukhtar, in the year sixty-eight."
"15240","What Adi ibn Hatim transmitted. Amir al-Shabi from Adi ibn Hatim. 141 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, (ha) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, both said: Shubah narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Safar, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the mirad He said: If it hits with its edge then eat, and if it hits with its side and kills, then it is beaten to death so do not eat. I said: I send my dog and it eats. He said: If you send your dog and mention the name of Allah then eat. I said: But if it eats He said: Then do not eat, for it only kept for itself and did not keep for you. I said: I send my dog and find another dog with it. He said: Do not eat, for you only named over your dog and did not name over the other. And the wording is that of the hadith of Sulayman ibn Harb."
"15241","142 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr narrated to us, Adam narrated, Shubah narrated, Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Safar narrated, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I send my dog and name Allah, and I find another dog with it and I do not know which of them took it. He said: Do not eat, for you only named over your dog and did not name over another."
"15242","143 - Abu Yusuf al-Qadi and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, both said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shubah informed us, from Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, that he said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I send my dog and find another dog with it and I do not know which of them killed it He said: Do not eat, for you only named over your dog and did not name over another."
"15243","144 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about hunting with the mirad He said: What hits with its edge then eat it, and what hits with its side then it is beaten to death. He said: And I asked him about hunting with a dog He said: What it holds for you then eat, for the taking of the dog is its slaughter. But if you find another dog with your dog and you think it may have taken it with it and killed it, then do not eat, for you only mentioned the name of Allah over your dog and did not mention over another."
"15244","145 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, Amir narrated, he said: I heard Adi ibn Hatim saying: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about hunting with the mirad So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What you hit with its edge then eat, and what you hit with its side then it is beaten to death. And I asked him about hunting with a dog He said: What it holds for you and does not eat from it then eat it, for its taking is its slaughter. But if you find another dog with your dog and you think it may have taken it with it and killed it, then do not eat it, for you only mentioned the name of Allah over your dog and did not mention over another."
"15245","146 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham and Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated, both said: Abu Shihab al-Hannat narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we have dogs with which we hunt. He said: Look at these trained beasts of prey, teach them from what Allah has taught you, and eat from what they hold for you. If it kills and does not eat then eat it, but if it eats then do not eat it. I said: What if my dogs mix with other dogs, do you think I may eat from it So he forbade us from that. And the wording is that of the hadith of Dawud."
"15246","147 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated, Musa ibn Ayan narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we have dogs with which we hunt, and he mentioned something like it."
"15247","148 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a people who hunt with these dogs and birds, so what is lawful for us from them He said: Trained beasts of prey, teaching them from what Allah has taught you, to the end of the verse. I said: O Messenger of Allah, even if it kills He said: Even if it kills. I said: O Messenger of Allah, even if other dogs mix with it He said: Do not eat except what the name of Allah has been mentioned over. I said: O Messenger of Allah, we shoot arrows He said: Eat what pierces and you mention the name of Allah over it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the mirad He said: Do not eat from the mirad except what you slaughter."
"15248","149 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated, Shubah narrated, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about hunting with a dog He said: If you send your dog and name Allah and it takes and kills then eat, but if it eats from it then do not eat, for it only held for itself."
"15249","150 - Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala narrated, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated, he said: I read to al-Fudayl ibn Maysarah, from Abu Jarir, that Amir al-Shabi said: We went to Adi ibn Hatim to ask him about hunting, and among us was Muhammad ibn Sirin. So I said to him: You are people of hunting, so narrate to us about hunting. Adi said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I said: We are people of two mountains and most of our food is game. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: With what do you hunt it I said: With dogs and arrows. He said: If your dogs hold then name Allah, so what they hold then eat. But if another trained dog enters among them, then do not eat until you slaughter it. And if you take it out of water then do not eat it until you slaughter it, for it is beaten to death."
"15250","151 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shubah informed us, from Said ibn Masruq, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I said: I send my dog and take another dog with my dog and I do not know which of them took it He said: Do not eat, for you only named over your dog and did not name over another."
"15251","152 - Abu Zurah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam narrated, Shubah narrated, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about hunting I said: I send my dog and name Allah, then I find another dog with my dog and I do not know which of them took it He said: Do not eat, for you only named over your dog and did not name over another."
"15252","153 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, from Bayan, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I said: We are a people who hunt with these dogs He said: If you send your trained dogs and mention the name of Allah over them then eat what they hold for you, even if they kill, except that the dog eats. But if it eats then do not eat, for I fear it only held for itself. And if other dogs mix with them then do not eat."
"15253","154 - Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Nasr and Hibban ibn Musa narrated, both said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, that he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about hunting He said: If you send your dog then name Allah. If you reach it while it has killed and not eaten then eat, for it only held for you. And he mentioned the hadith like the hadith of Amir al-Shabi from Adi ibn Hatim."
"15254","155 - Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Nasr and Hibban ibn Musa narrated, both said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, that he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about hunting He said: If you send your dog then name Allah. If you reach it while it has killed and not eaten then eat, for it only held for you. But if you reach it while it has killed and eaten from it then do not eat anything from it, for it only held it for itself. And if your dog mixes with another dog and it kills and does not eat from it then do not eat anything from it, for you only named over your dog and did not name over another. And if you shoot your arrow then mention the name of Allah. If you find it fallen in water and dead then do not eat it, for you do not know whether the water killed it or your arrow. And if you find it after a night or two nights and see in it no trace other than your arrow, then if you wish to eat, eat."
"15255","156 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: If you send your dog then mention the name of Allah. If it holds for you and you reach it alive then slaughter it. But if you reach it while it has killed and not eaten then eat. But if you find other dogs with it then do not eat, for you do not know which of them killed it. And if you shoot your arrow then mention the name of Allah over it. If it holds for you then eat. But if you find it after it was hidden from you for a day and you find in it nothing but the trace of your arrow then eat if you wish. But if you find it drowned in water then do not eat."
"15256","157 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my land is a land of game. He said: If you send your trained dog and name Allah then eat what the dog holds for you. But if it kills and eats from it then do not eat, for it only held for itself. And if you send your dog and name Allah and dogs over which you did not name mix with it then do not eat, for you do not know which of them killed it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot game and it disappears from me for the night. He said: If you find your arrow in it and find nothing else in it then eat it."
"15257","158 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated, Yusuf ibn Yazid Abu Mashar al-Barra narrated, Umar ibn Bashir narrated, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: When I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about hunting with dogs, he did not know what to say to me until there was revealed: And what you have taught of the trained beasts of prey, teaching them from what Allah has taught you."
"15258","159 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated, Shubah narrated, Ibn Abi al-Safar informed me, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: We asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I said: I send my dog and take another dog with me, and I do not know which of them took it He said: Do not eat, for you only named over your dog and did not name over another."
"15259","160 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, al-Mutamir narrated, he said: I heard Isa ibn al-Musayyab narrating from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of game and we go out with arrows, then he mentioned the throwing sticks. The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you shoot with the mirad and name Allah and it pierces then eat it, for that is its slaughter. But if it hits sideways then do not eat it unless you slaughter it. And if you find nothing but a smooth stone, then it suffices for you."
"15260","161 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam narrated, Shubah narrated, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about hunting with the mirad He said: If you hit with its edge then eat, and if you hit with its side then do not eat, for it is beaten to death."
"15261","162 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about hunting with the mirad He said: Do not eat from it except what you slaughter."
"15262","163 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Husayn ibn Numayr narrated, Husayn narrated, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the mirad He said: If it hits with its edge and pierces then eat, and if it hits with its side then do not eat."
"15263","164 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated, Ubaydah narrated, from Salim, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the mirad He said: If it pierces then eat, and if it hits with its side then do not eat."
"15264","165 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam informed us, Shubah narrated, Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Safar narrated, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about hunting with the mirad He said: If you hit with its edge then eat, and if you hit with its side and it kills then it is beaten to death so do not eat."
"15265","166 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (ha) and Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated, both said: Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, Asim ibn Sulayman informed me, from Amir, from Adi ibn Hatim, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If your shot falls in water and drowns then do not eat it."
"15266","167 - Abd Allah ibn al-Abbas al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Amir al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot game and find it after three days He said: Eat whatever you find the trace of your arrow on, so long as you do not find a beast of prey in it or find it drowned."
"15267","168 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Isa ibn Yunus and Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, (ha) and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated, Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about hunting with a falcon, and he said: What it holds for you then eat."
"15268","Chapter. 169 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati and Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, both said: Hamid ibn Yahya narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Adi ibn Hatim, how will you be when the lone woman rider comes out from the palaces of Yemen until she reaches al-Hirah, fearing nothing but Allah and the wolf for her sheep I said: But Tayy is mine with its battalions and its men. He said: Then Allah will suffice for her besides them."
"15269","170 - Abu al-Fadl al-Saqati and Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, both said: Hamid ibn Yahya narrated, Sufyan narrated, Bayan ibn Bishr narrated, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with something like it. He said: The woman has indeed ridden out from Yemen to al-Hirah, fearing nothing but Allah."
"15270","Chapter. 171 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Ruasi narrated, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: When Ramadan comes then fast thirty days unless you see the crescent before that."
"15271","172 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya narrated, from Mujalid, Amir narrated to me, Adi ibn Hatim narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught me prayer and fasting, and he said: Pray so and pray so, and fast so. When the sun sets then eat and drink until there becomes clear to you the white thread from the black thread of dawn. And fast thirty days unless you see the crescent before that. So I took two threads of black and white hair and I kept looking at them and it did not become clear to me. So I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he laughed and said: O son of Hatim, that is only the whiteness of day from the blackness of night."
"15272","173 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, something like it."
"15273","174 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Muhammad ibn Fudayl and Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, something like it."
"15274","175 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated, Musa narrated, Musa ibn Ayan narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Mujalid, from Amir, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have memorized everything you enjoined upon me except the white thread from the black thread. I slept last night with two threads with me, looking at this one time and at this one time. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, smiled and said: The white thread from the black thread is only that which is in the horizon of the sky."
"15275","176 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Husayn ibn Numayr narrated, Husayn narrated, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: When this verse was revealed: Until there becomes clear to you the white thread from the black thread of dawn, I took a black cord and a white cord and placed them under my pillow and looked, but it did not become clear. So I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he laughed and said: Your pillow is then indeed broad and long. That is only the night and the day."
"15276","177 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated, Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated, from Mutarrif, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about His saying: The white thread from the black thread, are they the two threads So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, smiled and said: No, but it is the whiteness of day and the blackness of night."
"15277","178 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa narrated, Jarir narrated, from Mutarrif, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the white thread from the black thread, are they the two threads He said: You are indeed wide of the nape if you can see the two threads. Then he said: No, but it is the blackness of night and the whiteness of day."
"15278","179 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Yazid al-Sudai narrated, my father narrated, Abu Yusuf narrated, from Simak, from Amir, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: When this verse was revealed: And eat and drink until there becomes clear to you the white thread from the black thread of dawn, I took two cords, one black and the other white, and placed them under my pillow. I lifted them in the night and could not distinguish the white from the black. So I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: O son of Hatim, your pillow is then indeed broad. He only said: Eat and drink until there becomes clear to you the whiteness of day from the blackness of night."
"15279","Chapter. 180 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr al-Kirmani narrated, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated, from Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him as a collector of charity to his people. When he had taken their charities, the death of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, coincided with that."
"15280","181 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, both said: Sulayman ibn Yazid Abu Dawud, freed slave of Banu Hashim, narrated, Ali ibn Yazid al-Sudai narrated, from Abu Hani, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A woman shall not travel more than three days except with a mahram."
"15281","Chapter. 182 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated, al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated, Abd al-Ala ibn Abi al-Musawir narrated, from Amir al-Shabi, he said: Adi ibn Hatim came to Kufah, so I came to him with some of the scholars of Kufah and the scribes, and we said: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Yes. I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: O Adi ibn Hatim, accept Islam and you will be safe. I said: And what is Islam He said: You testify that there is no god but Allah, and you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah, and you believe in all the decrees, their good and their evil, their sweet and their bitter."
"15282","Qays ibn Abi Hazim from Adi ibn Hatim. 183 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki, Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, all said: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated, Sufyan narrated, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated, from Qays ibn Abi Hatim, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Al-Hirah was shown to me as fangs of dogs, and you will conquer it. Then a man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, grant me the daughter of Buqaylah. He said: She is yours, so give her to him. Then her brother came and said: Will you sell her He said: Yes. He said: Then decide whatever you wish. He said: For a thousand dirhams. He said: I have taken her for a thousand. They said: If only you had said thirty thousand He said: And is there a number greater than a thousand"
"15283","Khaythamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Adi ibn Hatim. 184 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, (ha) and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, both said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is none among you but Allah, mighty and majestic, will speak to him with no interpreter between Him and him. He looks to his right and sees nothing but what he sent forth of his deeds, and he looks to his left and sees nothing but what he sent forth of his deeds, and he looks before him and sees nothing but the Fire facing him. So protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date."
"15284","185 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, al-Amash narrated, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is none among you but Allah will speak to him with no interpreter between Him and him. He looks to his right and sees nothing but his deeds, and he looks to his left and sees nothing but his deeds, then he looks before him and sees the Fire. So whoever among you is able to shield his face from the Fire, even with half a date."
"15285","186 - Shuayb ibn Imran al-Askari narrated to us, Abdan ibn Muhammad narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Ziyadah narrated, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, something like it."
"15286","187 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Yahya ibn Isa narrated, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is none among you but Allah, mighty and majestic, will speak to him on the Day of Resurrection with no interpreter between Him and him. He looks to his right and sees nothing but what he sent forth, and he looks to his left and sees nothing but what he sent forth, and he looks before him and sees the Fire. So whoever is able to shield his face from the Fire, let him do so, even with half a date."
"15287","188 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abu Husayn narrated to us, both said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Sharik narrated, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is none among you but Allah will speak to him on the Day of Resurrection with no interpreter between Him and him. He looks to his right and sees nothing but something he sent forth, then he looks facing him and the Fire meets him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: So whoever among you is able to shield his face from the Fire, let him do so, even with half a date."
"15288","189 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ubayd al-Qasim ibn Sallam informed us, Abu Muawiyah narrated, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, something like it."
"15289","190 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, something like it."
"15290","191 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Jarir narrated, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and said: Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date, and if you do not find then with a good word. Jarir, Fudayl ibn Iyad, Asbat ibn Muhammad and Abu Muawiyah added in this hadith between al-Amash and Khaythamah: Amr ibn Murrah."
"15291","192 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Shafii narrated to us, my uncle Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Protect yourselves from the Fire, then he turned aside and averted until we thought he was looking at it. Then he said: Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date, and even with a good word."
"15292","193 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned the Fire, then he mentioned something like it."
"15293","194 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, (ha) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, all said: Shubah narrated, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date, and if you do not find then with a good word."
"15294","195 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Hawadi narrated, Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated, Shubah narrated, from Mansur, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned the Fire, then he averted his face and sought refuge from it three times. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date, and if you do not find then with a good word."
"15295","196 - Muhammad ibn Husayn al-Anmati and Abd al-Salam ibn Sahl al-Sukkari narrated to us, both said: Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated, Ata ibn Muslim narrated, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I never entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, but he made room for me, or he said: he moved for me. One day I entered upon him while he was in a house full of his Companions, and when he saw me he made room for me until I sat beside him."
"15296","197 - Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khali al-Himsi narrated, my father narrated to me, Salamah al-Awdi narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd al-Riqashi, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people of hunting, what do you think about the mirad He said: What pierces from it then eat. And I asked him about dogs He said: If you send your dogs, then what they take then eat, unless another dog from outside enters among them."
"15297","198 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim narrated, he said: My father narrated to me, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The most fortunate and most unfortunate part of a man is what is between his jaws."
"15298","199 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hashim ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Khuthaym al-Hilali narrated, Abu Junadah, who lived among Banu Salul, narrated, al-Amash narrated, from Khaythamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: On the Day of Resurrection people will be ordered toward Paradise. When they draw near it and smell its fragrance and look at its palaces and what Allah has prepared in it for its people, they will be called: Turn them away from it, they have no share in it. They will return with a regret like none the first ones returned with. They will say: Our Lord, if You had entered us into the Fire before showing us Your reward and what You prepared in it for Your allies, it would have been easier for us. He said: That is what I intended for you. When you were alone you openly defied Me with grave sins, and when you met people you met them humbly, showing people contrary to what you give Me from your hearts. You feared people and did not fear Me, and you honored people and did not honor Me, and you left for people and did not leave for Me. Today I shall make you taste painful punishment along with what I have deprived you of reward."
"15299","200 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ukashah al-Kirmani narrated, Amr ibn Zurarah narrated, Abu Junadah narrated, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: People from among the people will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, then he mentioned something like it."
"15300","201 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated, Said ibn Uthman al-Qurashi narrated, Husayn al-Saluli narrated, al-Amash narrated, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he came from Badr, and a man of the Ansar said: Did we meet but feeble old women like guarded treasure so we slaughtered them Then the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, changed until I saw it as if pomegranate seeds had burst in it. Then he said: O son of my brother, do not say that. Those were the great chiefs of Quraysh. Had you seen them in their gatherings in Makkah you would have feared them. By Allah, I came to Makkah and saw them sitting in the mosque, and I could not greet them out of awe of them. Then I remembered the saying of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: O people, love Quraysh, for whoever loves Quraysh has loved me, and whoever hates Quraysh has hated me. Allah has made my people beloved to me, so I do not hasten punishment for them nor deem blessing for them too much. O Allah, You made the first of Quraysh taste chastisement, so make the last of them taste favor. But Allah knew what is in my heart of love for my people, so He delighted me concerning them. Allah, mighty and majestic, said: And warn your nearest kin, and lower your wing to those who follow you of the believers, meaning my people. Praise be to Allah who made the truthful one from my people, and the martyr from my people, and the leaders from my people. Allah turned people back to front, and the best of the Arabs were Quraysh, and it is the tree about which Allah said: The example of a good word is like a good tree, meaning by it Quraysh. Its root is firm, he says: its root is nobility. And its branch in the sky, he says: The honor with which Allah honored them by Islam by which He guided them and made them its people. Then He sent down concerning them a firm chapter from the Book of Allah: For the accustomed favor of Quraysh, their accustomed journey of winter and summer, so let them worship the Lord of this House, who fed them from hunger and secured them from fear. Al-Amash said: Khaythamah said: Adi ibn Hatim said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when Quraysh was mentioned to him with good but it delighted him until that delight was visible in his face. And he used to recite this verse: And indeed it is a remembrance for you and your people, and you will be questioned."
"15301","Hammam ibn al-Harith from Adi ibn Hatim. 202 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we send trained dogs of ours. He said: What they hold for you then eat. I said: Even if they kill He said: Even if they kill, so long as no dog from outside them joins them."
"15302","203 - Musa ibn Harun and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated, (ha) and Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zanbur narrated, both said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I send my trained dogs and they hold for me, may I eat He said: If you send your trained dogs and they hold for you then eat. I said: Even if they kill He said: Even if they kill, so long as no other dog joins them. I said: I shoot with the mirad and it pierces He said: If it pierces then eat, but if it hits with its side then do not eat."
"15303","204 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we send dogs and they hold for us. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If they are trained and you mention the name of Allah then eat. I said: O Messenger of Allah, even if they kill He said: Even if they kill, so long as no other dogs join it. I said: I find what is shot with the mirad He said: If you mention the name of Allah and it pierces then eat, but if it kills then do not eat."
"15304","205 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muammal ibn Ismail narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Amash and Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Adi, something like it."
"15305","206 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Fudayl ibn Amr, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Adi ibn Hatim, that he asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I send my dogs and name Allah, may I eat from what they hold for me He said: Yes. I said: Even if they kill He said: Even if they kill, unless another dog enters among them. I said: And the mirad, I shoot with it and name Allah He said: If it pierces then eat, but if it hits it with its side then do not eat."
"15306","Abd Allah ibn Maqil ibn Muqarrin from Adi ibn Hatim. 207 - Amr ibn Thawr al-Judhami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, (ha) and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, (ha) and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, both said: Sufyan narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Maqil, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is able to shield himself from the Fire even with half a date, let him do so."
"15307","208 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Shubah narrated, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Maqil saying: Adi ibn Hatim used to say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date."
"15308","209 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated, Israil narrated, (ha) and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated, Israil informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Maqil, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date."
"15309","210 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Awn ibn Sallam narrated, Zuhayr narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Maqil, from Adi ibn Hatim, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date."
"15310","211 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Waddah narrated, (ha) and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, both said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Maqil, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date."
"15311","212 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abu Usamah narrated, from Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah, (ha) and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, (ha) and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Faraj narrated, both said: Ishaq al-Azraq narrated, from Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Maqil, from Adi ibn Hatim, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date."
"15312","213 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Abbad narrated, Yazid narrated, from Ata, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Maqil, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date."
"15313","214 - Abd Allah ibn al-Sabbah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Luwayn Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Maqil, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date."
"15314","215 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu al-Jawwab narrated, from Ammar ibn Zurayq, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Abd Allah ibn Maqil, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date."
"15315","Said ibn Jubayr from Adi ibn Hatim. 216 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated, Shubah narrated, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, Shubah informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot game and seek it but do not find it except after a night. He said: If you see your arrow in it and no beast of prey has eaten from it then eat. Shubah said: I narrated it to Abu Bishr and he said: Said ibn Jubayr only said, from Adi ibn Hatim, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: If you recognize your arrow in it and see no other trace in it, and you know it killed it, then eat."
"15316","217 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated, Shubah narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot game then seek the trace after that. He said: If you find your arrow in it and no beast of prey has eaten from it then eat. Then I narrated it to Iyas ibn Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, and he narrated to me from Said ibn Jubayr, from Adi ibn Hatim, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: If you see your arrow in it and you know it killed it then eat."
"15317","Musab ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas from Adi ibn Hatim. 218 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail and Ibn al-Asbahani narrated, (ha) and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, all said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated, Ghutayf ibn Ayan of the people of al-Jazirah informed us, from Musab ibn Sad, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a cross of gold on my neck. He said: O Adi, cast this idol from your neck. So I cast it off. I reached him while he was reciting Surah Baraah, and he recited this verse: They took their rabbis and monks as lords besides Allah, until he finished it. I said: We do not worship them. He said: Do they not forbid what Allah made lawful so you forbid it, and permit what Allah forbade so you deem it lawful I said: Yes. He said: That is their worship."
"15318","219 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Abd al-Salam ibn Harb, from Ghutayf ibn Ayan, from Musab ibn Sad, from Adi ibn Hatim, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, something like it."
"15319","Muhill ibn Khalifah from Adi ibn Hatim. 220 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim and Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated, (ha) and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated, both said: Shubah narrated, from Muhill ibn Khalifah, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date, and if you do not find then with a good word."
"15320","221 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Sahl ibn Sinan al-Nahrutiri narrated, Ahmad ibn Abi Qadi Nahrutiri narrated, Shubah narrated, from Muhill ibn Khalifah and Muhammad ibn Khalifah, from Adi ibn Hatim, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date."
"15321","222 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, both said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, Yahya ibn al-Walid al-Musayyar al-Tai narrated, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Salih al-Narsi narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated, (ha) and Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, Mujahid ibn Musa narrated, both said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated, Yahya ibn al-Walid narrated to me, from Muhill ibn Khalifah, from Adi ibn Hatim, that he went out to their gathering and prayer was established. Their imam advanced and lengthened the prayer and the sitting. When he finished he said: Whoever leads you in prayer, let him complete bowing and prostration, for behind him are the young, the old, the sick, the traveler and the needy. When prayer came, Adi advanced and completed bowing and prostration and kept the prayer brief. When he finished he said: This is how we used to pray behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And the wording is that of the hadith of Ibn Mahdi."
"15322","223 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, both said: al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah al-Bazzar narrated, Uthman ibn Umar narrated, Israil narrated, Sad al-Tai narrated, Muhill ibn Khalifah narrated, Adi ibn Hatim narrated to me, he said: I was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a man came complaining of need, then another came complaining of highway robbery. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Adi, have you seen al-Hirah I said: No, though I have been told of it. He said: If you live long you will surely see lone women riders traveling from al-Hirah to circumambulate the Kabah in safety, fearing none but Allah. And if you live long, the treasures of Khosrau will surely be opened. I said: O Messenger of Allah, Khosrau ibn Hurmuz He said: Khosrau ibn Hurmuz. And if you live long you will surely see a man going out with his palm full of dirhams or silver seeking one to accept it. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date, and if you do not find then with a good word."
"15323","224 - al-Hasan ibn Hammad ibn Fadalah al-Sayrafi narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated, Abu Asim narrated, Sadan ibn Bishr narrated, Abu Mujahid narrated, Muhill ibn Khalifah narrated to me, that he heard Adi ibn Hatim saying: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when two men came, one complaining of poverty and the other complaining of highway robbery. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: As for highway robbery, only a little will pass over you until the caravan goes out from al-Hirah to Makkah without a guard. As for poverty, the Hour will not come until one of you goes around with his charity and finds no one to accept it. Then each of you will surely stand before Allah, mighty and majestic, with no veil between him and Him to translate, and He will surely say: Did I not give you wealth He will say: Yes. He will say: Did I not send a messenger to you He will say: Yes. Then he looks to his right and sees nothing but the Fire, then he looks to his left and sees nothing but the Fire. So let each of you protect himself from the Fire even with half a date, and if he does not find then with a good word."
"15324","225 - Shuayb ibn Imran al-Askari narrated to us, Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Askari narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, Abu Abdan Maslamah narrated, from Sad al-Tai, from Muhill ibn Khalifah, from Adi ibn Hatim, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: There is none among you but his Lord will speak to him with no interpreter to translate for him and no veil to veil him. He will say: Did I not send a messenger to you He will say: Yes. Then He will say: Did I not give you wealth and favor you He will say: Yes. So let each of you protect himself from the Fire even with half a date."
"15325","Tamim ibn Tarafah from Adi ibn Hatim. Simak ibn Harb from Tamim. 226 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Tamim, he said: I heard Adi ibn Hatim when he came to a lodging where he was staying, and a Bedouin came to him asking, and he said: I have nothing with me to give you, but I have a coat of mail in Kufah and it is yours. The Bedouin disparaged it, so he swore not to give him. Then he said: I only came asking you about a servant to help me with it. He said: I have assigned my coat of mail to you, and by Allah it is dearer to me than three slaves. The Bedouin desired it and said: I accept your kindness. Adi said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever swears an oath and sees better than it, let him do what is better, I would not have given you."
"15326","227 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Tamim, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever swears an oath and sees better than it, let him take what is better and expiate for his oath."
"15327","228 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated, Muhammad ibn Jafar Ghundar narrated, Shubah narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, he said: I heard Adi ibn Hatim when a man came to him asking him for a hundred dirhams, and he said: You ask me for a hundred dirhams while I am the son of Hatim By Allah, I will not give you. Then he said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever swears an oath and sees better than it, let him do what is better, I would not have given you."
"15328","Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay from Tamim ibn Tarafah. 229 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Shubah narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Tamim al-Tai, from Adi ibn Hatim, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever swears an oath and sees better than it, let him leave it and do what is better."
"15329","230 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, from al-Amash, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If one of you swears over something and sees better than it, let him expiate it and do what is better."
"15330","231 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated, Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated, from al-Shaybani, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever swears an oath and sees better than it, let him do what is better."
"15331","232 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, (ha) and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, both said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever swears and sees better than it, let him leave his oath and do what is better, and let him expiate for his oath."
"15332","233 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Jarir narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, he said: A beggar came to Adi ibn Hatim asking him for expenses toward the price of a servant. He said: I have nothing to give you except my coat of mail and helmet, so I shall write to my family to give them to you. He was not pleased, so Adi became angry and said: By Allah, I shall not give you anything. Then the man was pleased, so he said: By Allah, were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever swears an oath and sees what is more God-fearing, let him do it, but he has not broken his oath."
"15333","234 - Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, (ha) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated, both said: Sufyan narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: Two men came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and gave sermons. One of them said: Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger is rightly guided, and whoever disobeys them both has gone astray. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Stand, you are a bad preacher."
"15334","235 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: A man gave testimony before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger is rightly guided, and whoever disobeys them both has gone astray. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be silent, you are a bad preacher. He disliked his saying: and whoever disobeys them both."
"15335","Abbad ibn Hubaysh from Adi ibn Hatim. 236 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, Abbad ibn Hubaysh narrated to me, from Adi ibn Hatim al-Tai, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was sitting in the mosque. The people said: This is Adi ibn Hatim. I was a Christian, and I came without assurance or letter. When I was brought to him he took my hand, and before that he had said: I hope Allah will place his hand in my hand. He stood with me, and a woman met him with a boy with her, and they said: We have a need of you. He stood with her until he fulfilled her need. Then he took my hand until he came to his house. A cushion was cast for him, so he sat on it and I sat before him. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: What makes you flee but that it be said: but Allah, so do you know any god but Allah Then he spoke a while, then said: What makes you flee or harms you but that it be said: Allah is greatest, so do you know anything greater than Allah I said: No. He said: The Jews are those with anger upon them, and the Christians are astray. I said: Then I am a monotheist Muslim. I saw his face brighten with joy. Then he ordered for me and I stayed with a man of the Ansar, and I used to come to him at both ends of the day. While I was with him in the evening, people came to him in garments of wool from these striped cloaks. He prayed, then stood and urged giving for them. Then he said: With a sa or half a sa or half of it, and even with part of a handful, let each of you shield his face from the heat of Hell or the Fire, even with half a date. For each of you will meet Allah and He will say to him what I say to you: Did I not make for you hearing and sight He will say: Yes. He will say: Did I not make for you wealth and children He will say: Yes. He will say: Where is what you sent forth for yourself Then he looks before him and behind him and to his right and to his left and finds nothing to shield his face with. So let each of you shield his face from the Fire even with half a date, and if he does not find then with a good word. I do not fear poverty for you, for Allah, mighty and majestic, will help you and give you until the lone woman rider travels between Yathrib and al-Hirah, and most feared for her mount is theft. I kept saying to myself: Then where are the robbers of Tayy"
"15336","237 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated, both said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated, Shubah narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Abbad ibn Hubaysh saying: I heard Adi ibn Hatim saying: The cavalry of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or the messengers of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came with Aqrab and took my paternal aunt and some people. When they were brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, they were arrayed for him, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, the delegate is distant and the child is cut off, and I am an old woman with no capacity for service, so bestow favor upon me, may Allah, mighty and majestic, bestow upon you. He said: And who is your delegate She said: Adi ibn Hatim. He said: The one who fled from Allah and His Messenger She said: Then he bestowed favor upon me. When he returned, and a man beside him whom she thought was Ali, he said: Ask him for mounts. She said: So I asked him, and he ordered a she-ass. I said: You have done a deed your father would not do. She said: Come to him desiring or fearing, for so-and-so came to him and got from him, and so-and-so came to him and got from him. So I came to him, and with him were a woman and children or a child. He mentioned their closeness to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I knew it was not the kingship of Khosrau and Caesar. He said: O Adi, what makes you flee that it be said: There is no god but Allah, so is there any god but Allah What makes you flee that it be said: Allah is greatest, so is there anything greater than Allah So I accepted Islam and saw his face brighten. He said: The Jews are those with anger upon them and the Christians are the astray. Then people came to him and asked him. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: As for what follows, it is for you, O people, to give from surplus. Let a man give a sa, part of a sa, a handful. Shubah said: And most of my knowledge is that he said: With a date, with half a date. Each of you will meet Allah and He will say: Did I not make you hearing and seeing Did I not make for you wealth and children, so what did you send forth He looks before him and behind him and to his right and to his left, and finds nothing. He shields nothing from the Fire but his face. So protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date, and if you do not find then with a good word. I do not fear poverty for you. Allah will surely help you and surely give you, or surely open for you, until the lone woman rider travels between al-Hirah and Yathrib, most fearing for her camel-litter theft."
"15337","Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Adi ibn Hatim. 238 - Abd Allah ibn Najiyah narrated to us, al-Rabi ibn Thalab narrated, Abu Ismail al-Muaddib narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will surely come upon people a time when the lone woman rider travels from Makkah to al-Hirah with none taking the halter of her mount, and there will surely come upon people a time when a man walks with his palm full of gold giving it in charity with none accepting it from him."
"15338","239 - Abu Muhammad al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from more than one, that Adi ibn Hatim narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Only a little will pass over you until the lone woman rider travels between Makkah and al-Hirah with none taking her halter, and only a little will pass over each of you until a man walks with his palm full of gold and finds none to accept it. And there is none among you but he will surely be presented to Allah, mighty and majestic, with no interpreter between Him and him. So whoever is able to shield himself from the Fire even with half a date, let him do so."
"15339","Qays al-Kindi from Adi ibn Hatim. 240 - Abu Zurah al-Dimashqi Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr and Hafs ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, both said: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, my father narrated, from Uthman ibn Qays al-Kindi, from his father, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, we do not ask you about obeying one who is God-fearing and righteous, but about one who does and does, mentioning evil. He said: Fear Allah, and hear and obey."
"15340","Bilal ibn al-Mundhir from Adi ibn Hatim. 241 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Shaybani al-Kufi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated, Ishaq ibn Idris al-Uswari narrated, Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated, from Sadaqah ibn Said, from Bilal ibn al-Mundhir, from Adi ibn Hatim, that he led them in Zuhr prayer and recited like: When the sky splits. When he finished the prayer he said: I did not fall short for you from the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"15341","al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim from Adi ibn Hatim. 242 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated, from Abthar ibn al-Qasim, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from Khalid ibn Abi Nawf, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, there are dogs and we send them after game, and they eat what they hold for us He said: Yes. I said: Even if they kill He said: Even if they kill."
"15342","243 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated, from Khalid ibn Qusayt, from al-Dahhak, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we have dogs and we send them after game, and we eat from what they hold for us He said: Yes. Khalid ibn Qusayt is Khalid ibn Abi Nawf."
"15343","al-Mughirah ibn Sabil from Adi ibn Hatim. 244 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, Said ibn Masruq narrated, from al-Mughirah ibn Sabil, he said: Amr ibn Hurayth proposed to Adi ibn Hatim for his daughter, and he said: I shall not marry you except on my terms. He said: Your terms are yours. He said: She is not better than the daughters of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he married her to him on the obligatory dowry."
"15344","Murri ibn Qatari from Adi ibn Hatim. 245 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated, (ha) and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated, all said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Murri ibn Qatari, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if one of us gets game and has no knife with him, may he slaughter with a smooth stone or a split stick He said: Let the blood flow with whatever you wish and mention the name of Allah."
"15345","246 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam narrated, Shubah narrated, Simak ibn Harb narrated, he said: I heard Murri ibn Qatari narrating from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I slaughter with a smooth stone and a stick He said: Let the blood flow with whatever you wish, mention the name of Allah, and eat."
"15346","247 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, Shubah informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Murri ibn Qatari narrating from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I send my dog and it takes game, but I find nothing to slaughter it with except a smooth stone and a stick. He said: Let the blood flow with whatever you wish and mention the name of Allah."
"15347","248 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil, Simak ibn Harb informed me, from Murri ibn Qatari, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about game I hunt He said: Let the blood flow with whatever you wish and mention the name of Allah, the Exalted."
"15348","249 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, both said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Murri ibn Qatari, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we send trained dogs. He said: If you mention the name of Allah then eat. I said: Even if they kill He said: Even if they kill."
"15349","250 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, Shubah narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Murri ibn Qatari narrating from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father used to join kinship and do such-and-such. He said: Your father sought a matter and attained it, meaning remembrance."
"15350","251 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, Shubah narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Murri ibn Qatari narrating from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I ask you about food I leave, which I leave only out of scruple. He said: Do not leave anything in which you imitate Christianity."
"15351","Tamim ibn Abd al-Rahman from Adi ibn Hatim. 252 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, (ha) and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to me, both said: Artah ibn Husayn al-Bunani narrated, Tamim ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, Adi ibn Hatim narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Adi, do not despise my Companions. The treasures of Khosrau will surely be opened, and the lone woman rider will surely come out from al-Hirah under the protection of this House, and this wealth will surely be spread at the start of the day then cast aside at its end with none accepting it. Adi said: I have seen two, and the third will surely be."
"15352","Abu Imran, I think al-Jawni, from Adi. 253 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, (ha) and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Kathir al-Wasiti narrated, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from Abu Hashim, from Abu Imran, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about one in major impurity sleeping He said: He performs ablution as for prayer."
"15353","Thabit ibn Aslam al-Bunani from Adi. 254 - al-Abbas ibn Ahmad al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Saiqah narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated, Jubayr ibn Hujr narrated, from Thabit al-Bunani, he said: Adi ibn Hatim narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will almost come upon people a time when it is hard for a man to pay the zakah of his wealth."
"15354","al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman from Adi. 255 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Kathir ibn al-Harith, from al-Qasim, freed slave of Muawiyah, from Adi ibn Hatim, that he asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best He said: The service of a slave in the path of Allah, the shade of a tent, or a she-camel lent for milking."
"15355","Adi ibn Amirah al-Kindi. 256 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Adi ibn Amirah al-Kindi, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us and said: O people, whomever we employ among you over work and he conceals from us a needle or more, it is misappropriation he will bring on the Day of Resurrection. Then a black man of the Ansar stood, as if I look at him now, and said: O Messenger of Allah, take back your work from me. He said: And why He said: I heard you say what you just said. He said: And I say it now: Whomever we employ among you over work, let him bring its little and its much. What he is given of it he takes, and what he is forbidden he refrains from."
"15356","257 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Adi ibn Amirah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, something like it."
"15357","258 - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Adi ibn Amirah al-Kindi, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whomever we employ among you over work, let him bring its little and its much. What he is given of it he takes, and what he is forbidden he refrains from."
"15358","259 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Adi ibn Amirah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, something like it."
"15359","260 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Sufyan narrated, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Adi ibn Amirah al-Kindi, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whomever we employ among you over work and he misappropriates from us a needle or more, it is misappropriation he will bring on the Day of Resurrection. Then a black man of Azd stood before him, as if I look at him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, take back your work from me. He said: And what is with you He said: I heard you say such-and-such. He said: And I say it now: Whomever we employ among you over work, let him bring its little and its much. What he is given of it he takes, and what he is forbidden he refrains from."
"15360","261 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaim al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated, Marwan ibn Muawiyah al-Fazari narrated, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhawi narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Mismai narrated, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated, (ha) and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Ayyub Dallawayh narrated to me, Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Utbah narrated, all of them from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Adi ibn Amirah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, something like it."
"15361","262 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Assal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated, Sharik narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Adi ibn Amirah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, something like it."
"15362","263 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to me, (ha) and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, both said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated, he said: I read to al-Fadl ibn Maysarah, from Ibn Hariz, that Qays ibn Abi Hazim narrated to him that Adi ibn Amirah al-Kindi narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he prostrated would spread his arms until the whiteness of his armpits was seen."
"15363","264 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn narrated to me, from Adi ibn Adi al-Kindi, from his father Adi, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The previously married woman expresses herself, and the virgin, her consent is her silence."
"15364","265 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated, Adi ibn Adi narrated, Raja ibn Haywah and al-Urs ibn Amirah narrated, from Abu Adi, he said: There was a dispute between Imri al-Qays and someone, so they disputed to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He asked the Hadrami for proof, but he had no proof, so he judged against Imri al-Qays with an oath. The Hadrami said: O Messenger of Allah, if you enable him to swear, my land is gone by Allah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever swears a false oath will meet Allah while He is angry with him. Raja ibn Haywah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited: Those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price, the verse. Imru al-Qays said: Then what is for me if I leave it, O Messenger of Allah He said: Paradise. He said: Then I call you to witness that I have left it."
"15365","And his son Adi ibn Adi, he has Companionship. 266 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated, (ha) and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Jafar ibn Musafir narrated, Abd Allah ibn Nafi narrated, from Muhammad ibn Jafar, both from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Adi ibn Adi al-Kindi, that he informed them, he said: Two men came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, disputing over land. One of them said: It is my land, and the other said: It is my land, I plowed it and cut its reeds. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made the one in whose possession the land was swear."
"15366","267 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Adi ibn Adi al-Kindi, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever swears over the wealth of a Muslim man will meet Allah while He is angry with him. It was said: And whoever leaves it, O Messenger of Allah He said: Then Paradise is his."
"15367","Adi ibn Badda, he lived in Kufah. 268 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Salih ibn Abd Allah al-Tirmidhi narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim narrated to me, from Abd al-Malik ibn Said ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man of Banu Sahm went out with Tamim al-Dari and Adi ibn Badda. The Sahmi died, and when they came with his estate they missed a silver cup inlaid with gold. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made them both swear. Then it was found, and they said: We bought it from Adi ibn Tamim. Then two men of the guardians of the Sahmi stood and swore by Allah that our testimony is more worthy than their testimony, and that the cup belongs to your companion. Concerning them was revealed: O you who believe, testimony among you."
"15368","Adi al-Judhami. 269 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki and Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, both said: Said ibn Mansur narrated, Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Adi al-Judhami, that he met the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on one of his journeys and said: O Messenger of Allah, I had two wives and they fought, so I threw at one of them and killed her. He said: Pay her blood-money and do not inherit from her. It is as if I look at the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a red camel with cut ears, saying: O people, learn, for hands are only three: the hand of Allah is the highest, the hand of the giver is the middle, and the hand of the receiver is the lowest. So refrain from asking even by bundles of firewood. Have I conveyed Have I conveyed"
"15369","270 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to me, Wuhayb narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah narrated to me, a man of Judham narrated to me, from a man of them called Adi, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, something like it."
"15370","271 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, that he heard a man of Judham narrating from a man of them called Adi, that he threw a stone at a wife of his and she died. He followed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Tabuk and told him his affair. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: You pay her blood-money and do not inherit from her."
"15371","272 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, they said: Abda ibn Abd Allah al-Saffar narrated, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, Sulayman ibn Kinana, the freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Abi Sufyan narrated to me, from Adi ibn Zayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made a protected reserve (hima) in every direction around Madinah for a barid; its trees are not to be stripped of leaves nor cut down, except a stick to drive with."
"15372","273 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, al-Ala ibn al-Fadl ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suwiyyah al-Minqari narrated, and Abu Umayyah Salm ibn Isam al-Thaqafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Faraj al-Riyashi narrated, al-Ala ibn al-Fadl ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suwiyyah al-Minqari narrated, Abu al-Fadl ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to me, from his father Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suwiyyah, from Abi Suwiyyah, from his father Khalifah ibn Abda ibn Jarwal, he said: I asked Muhammad ibn Adi ibn Rabiah ibn Suwah ibn Jusham how his father Muhammad had named him Muhammad in the Jahiliyyah. He said: I asked my father about what you asked me, and he said: I went out as one of four men of Banu Tamim; I was one of them, along with Sufyan ibn Mujashi ibn Darim, Usamah ibn Malik ibn Jundub ibn al-Anbar, Yazid ibn Rabiah ibn Kinabiyyah ibn Hurqus ibn Mazin, and Yazid ibn Jafnah ibn Malik ibn Ghassan in Sham. When we arrived in Sham we camped at a pond with trees belonging to a Dayrani - meaning the owner of a hermitage. We said: If only we would wash from this water, oil ourselves and put on our clothes, then go to our companion. The Dayrani looked down upon us and said: This speech is not the speech of the people of this land. We said: Yes, we are a people of Mudar. He said: Which Mudar? We said: Of Khindif. He said: A prophet will soon be raised from among you, so hasten and take your share of him and you will be guided, for he is the Seal of the Prophets. We said: What is his name? He said: Muhammad. When we left Ibn Jafnah, a boy was born to each one of us and he named him Muhammad. Al-Ala said: Qays ibn Asim said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do you know who was the first of the Arabs to know of you before you were sent? He said: No. He said: Banu Tamim, and he told him this story."
"15373","274 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr: Utbah ibn Ghazwan ibn Jabir ibn Wahb ibn Qabisah ibn Malik ibn al-Harith ibn Mazin ibn Mansur ibn Ikrimah ibn Hissah ibn Qays ibn Ghaylan ibn Matar, an ally of Nawfal ibn Abd Manaf."
"15374","275 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham narrated, Abu Ubaydah Mamar ibn al-Muthanna narrated, he said: Utbah ibn Ghazwan was kunya'd Abu Abd Allah, and it was said: Abu Ghazwan. He was tall and handsome. He died in year seventeen while heading to Basrah on his second trip, and was buried at one of the watering places, at fifty-five years of age, an ally of Banu Nawfal ibn Abd Manah."
"15375","276 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, he said: Utbah ibn Ghazwan died in year seventeen on the road to Basrah as governor for Umar ibn al-Khattab, at fifty-seven years of age. It was said: He died in year twenty. He is the one who founded Basrah, laid out its dwellings and built its mosque, and he is the one who conquered Ubullah. His governorship of Basrah was six months; Umar ibn al-Khattab had appointed him over it."
"15376","277 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, Abu al-Numan Arim narrated, Jarir narrated, Humayd ibn Hilal narrated, Khalid ibn Umayr narrated to me, he said: We campaigned with Utbah ibn Ghazwan and we conquered Ubullah, and there was a basket of walnuts. We said: We have seen no stones to break them open and eat."
"15377","278 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abi Nasr, from Utbah ibn Ghazwan al-Sulami - and Umar had sent him as governor over Basrah, and he was a Badri - he stood and addressed and said: This world has announced its parting and nothing remains of it but dregs like the dregs of a vessel which its owner pours out. Beyond you lies an abode, so move to it with the best of what is at hand. By Allah, I saw myself as the seventh of seven with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and our mouths had cracked from eating trees; there is not a man among us today but he is a governor over a city of the cities. I saw myself with Sad ibn Malik racing for a cloak, so I took half of it and Sad took half. It has reached me that between the two leaves of the gates of Paradise is forty years, and a day will come upon it when it is crowded. There was never a prophethood but it was abrogated until it becomes kingship. I seek refuge with Allah from being great in myself and small in the eyes of people. You will test the governors after me."
"15378","279 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abi Nasr, he said: Utbah ibn Ghazwan addressed us and said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as the seventh of seven; we had no food but the bark of trees."
"15379","280 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, they said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Khalid ibn Umayr al-Adawi, he said: Utbah ibn Ghazwan addressed us, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed, this world has announced its parting and turned away swiftly, and nothing remains of it but dregs like the dregs of a vessel which its owner pours out. You are moving from it to an abode that does not pass away, so move with the best of what is at hand. It was mentioned to us that a stone is cast from the edge of Hell and falls for seventy years without reaching its bottom; by Allah it will surely be filled. Are you amazed? It was mentioned to us that between the two leaves of the gates of Paradise is a journey of forty years, and a day will come upon it when it is crowded with throngs. I saw myself as the seventh of seven with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); we had no food but tree leaves until our mouths cracked. I picked up a cloak and split it between me and Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, the horseman of Islam; I wrapped myself with half of it. There is not one of us alive today but he has become governor of a city of the cities. I seek refuge with Allah from being great in myself and small with Allah. No prophethood ever remained but it changed until its end becomes kingship. You will test - or you will be tested by - the governors after us."
"15380","281 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated, from Khalid ibn Umayr, and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, they said: Waki narrated, from Qurrah ibn Khalid, from Khalid ibn Umayr al-Adawi, Waki said: Abu Naamah said: I heard from Khalid ibn Umayr, he said: Utbah ibn Ghazwan addressed us and said: This world has announced its parting and turned away swiftly, and nothing remains of it but dregs like the dregs of a vessel. You are in an abode from which you will move, so move with the best of what is at hand. I saw myself as the seventh of seven with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); we had no food to eat but tree leaves until our mouths cracked. Qurrah said: I found a cloak. Abu Naamah said: I picked up a cloak and split it in two halves; I wore half and gave Sad half. There is not one of those seven today but he is over a city of the cities. The governors after me will surely be tested. By Allah, there was never a prophethood but it changed until it becomes kingship and despotism. It was mentioned to me - Qurrah said: That a stone, and Abu Naamah said: That a sheet - is cast from the edge of Hell and falls to its bottom; Qurrah said: Seventy autumns, and Abu Naamah said: Seventy autumns, and it will surely be filled. Between the two leaves of the gates of Paradise is a journey of forty days, and a day will come upon the gates of Paradise when there is no gate but it is crowded. I seek refuge with Allah from being great in myself and small with Allah."
"15381","282 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Azhar ibn Jamil narrated, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated, Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Khalid ibn Umayr, from Utbah ibn Ghazwan, and he mentioned the hadith."
"15382","283 - Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Abu Naamah al-Adawi narrated, from Khalid ibn Umayr, and Shuways ibn Kaysan, they said: Utbah ibn Ghazwan addressed and mentioned the hadith."
"15383","284 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated, Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated, from al-Hasan, from Utbah ibn Ghazwan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"15384","285 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to me, and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Jawwaz narrated, they said: Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Utbah ibn Ghazwan, he said: I saw us with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as the seventh of seven; we had no food but the leaves of the hublah, until one of us would pass stool like sheep droppings."
"15385","286 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abbad ibn Yaqub al-Asadi narrated, Amr ibn Thabit narrated, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, he said: I heard Aba al-Khalil narrating from Mujahid, Ibn al-Shikhkhir narrated to me, he said: Utbah ibn Ghazwan al-Sulami came to us and addressed us while in Basrah, saying: This world has announced its parting and turned away swiftly, and nothing remains of it but dregs like the dregs of a vessel which its owner poured out. You are moving, so move with the best of what is at hand. I saw myself as the seventh of seven with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and our mouths had cracked from eating trees."
"15386","287 - Abu Ubaydah Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim al-Askari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jami al-Attar narrated, Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Qurashi narrated, Abu Naamah al-Adawi narrated, from Khalid ibn Umayr, from Utbah ibn Ghazwan, he said: We would witness fighting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when the sun passed its zenith he would say to us: Charge, so we would charge."
"15387","288 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Jabalah narrated, Umar ibn al-Fadl al-Sulami narrated, Ghazwan ibn Utbah ibn Ghazwan narrated, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"15388","289 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Subayh narrated, Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to me, from Utbah ibn Ghazwan, brother of Banu Mazin ibn Sasah - and he was of the Companions - that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: After you are days of patience; one who holds fast in them to the like of what you are upon will have like the reward of fifty of you. They said: O Prophet of Allah, or of them? He said: Rather, of you. They said: O Prophet of Allah, or of them? He said: No, rather of you - three or four times."
"15389","290 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Sufi narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl narrated, my father narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Isa, from Zayd ibn Ali, from Utbah ibn Ghazwan, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you loses something or one of you wants help while in a land with no company, let him say: O servants of Allah, help me; O servants of Allah, help me - for Allah has servants whom we do not see, and this has been tried and found true."
"15390","291 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Bashir al-Shami narrated, Umar Abu Hafs narrated, Utbah ibn Ibrahim ibn Utbah ibn Ghazwan narrated, from his father, from Utbah ibn Ghazwan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day to Quraysh: Is there among you one who is not of you? They said: Our nephew Utbah ibn Ghazwan. He said: The sister's son of a people is of them, and the ally of a people is of them."
"15391","292 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated, and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated, they said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Utbah ibn Abd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The martyrs and those who die of plague will come, and the companions of the plague will say: We are martyrs. It will be said: Look; if their wounds are like the wounds of the martyrs, flowing blood with the scent of musk, then they are martyrs - and they will be found so."
"15392","293 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti and Abu Zayd al-Hawti narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Yaman narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, he said: Utbah ibn Abd al-Sulami said: When a man would come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a name he did not like, he would change it. We came to him - seven of Banu Sulaym, the eldest of us al-Irbad ibn Sariyah - and we pledged to him all together."
"15393","294 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, my father narrated to me, and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Utbah ibn Abd, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No Muslim loses three children who have not reached puberty but they will meet him at the eight gates of Paradise; he may enter through whichever he wishes."
"15394","295 - Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, Zurayq ibn al-Sakht narrated, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Utbah ibn Abd al-Sulami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts one day as an obligation in the path of Allah, Allah will distance Hell from him as the distance between the seven heavens and earths; and whoever fasts one day voluntarily, Allah will distance Hell from him a journey like the distance between the heaven."
"15395","296 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Tai narrated, and Ismail ibn Qirat al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman, son of the daughter of Shurahbil, narrated, and Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, they said: Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn Shabur narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Tai narrated, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Utbah ibn Abd narrating from his father, that he came among people wanting to change their names. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me, he called me - and I was a young boy - and said: What is your name? I said: Atalah ibn Abd. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather, you are Utbah ibn Abd. Show me your sword. So he unsheathed it, and when he looked at it, it was a sword with thinness and weakness. He said: Do not strike with this, but stab with it, stabbing."
"15396","297 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Tai narrated, and Ismail ibn Qirat al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman, son of the daughter of Shurahbil, narrated, and Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated, they said: Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn Shabur narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Tai narrated, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Utbah ibn Abd narrating from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Banu Qurayzah: Whoever puts an arrow in has Paradise. Utbah said: So I put in three arrows."
"15397","298 - Muhammad ibn Abi Zurah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, and Ismail ibn Qirat al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, they said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, Damdam ibn Zurah narrated, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Utbah ibn Ubayd al-Sulami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The caliphate is in Quraysh, judgment is in the Ansar, the call is in Abyssinia, and jihad and emigration are in the Muslims and the Emigrants thereafter."
"15398","299 - Ibrahim ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Utbah ibn Abd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Qurayzah and al-Nadir: Whoever puts an arrow into this fortress, Paradise is assured for him. Utbah said: So I put in three arrows."
"15399","300 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Utbah ibn Abd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me - and I was a young boy - and said: What is your name? I said: Atalah ibn Abd. He said: You are Utbah ibn Abd."
"15400","301 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Utbah ibn Abd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Show me your sword. So he unsheathed it, and he looked at it, and it had thinness and weakness. He said: Do not strike with this, but stab with it, stabbing."
"15401","302 - Yahya ibn Salih narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ramli narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Utbah ibn Abd, and Abi Umamah, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the ruler seeks out suspicion among the people, he corrupts them."
"15402","303 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Said narrated to me, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Utbah ibn Abd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man were dragged on his face from the day he was born until he dies old in seeking Allah's pleasure, he would deem it little on the Day of Resurrection."
"15403","304 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, my father narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Utbah ibn Abd, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, curse the people of Yemen, for their might is severe, their number large, their fortresses fortified. He said: No. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the two non-Arabs, Persia and Rome. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the people of Yemen pass by you driving their women and carrying their sons on their shoulders, they are of me and I am of them."
"15404","305 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hisham ibn Said Abu Ahmad al-Talqani narrated, al-Hasan ibn Ayyub al-Hadrami narrated, Abd Allah ibn Nasij al-Hadrami narrated, from Utbah ibn Abd al-Sulami, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Rise and fight. Then a man was struck with an arrow. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This one is assured."
"15405","306 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Isam ibn Khalid al-Himsi narrated, al-Hasan ibn Ayyub al-Hadrami narrated, Abd Allah ibn Nasij narrated, Utbah ibn Abd narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded his Companions to fight, and a man of his Companions was struck with an arrow. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This one is assured. And when he commanded them to fight they said: Then, O Messenger of Allah, we will not say as Banu Israil said to Musa: Go, you and your Lord, and fight - to the end of the verse - but we say: Go, you and your Lord, and fight; we are with you both among the fighters."
"15406","307 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, and Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Abd al-Samad al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Kharijah, al-Hakam ibn Musa and Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to me, they said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Aqil ibn Mudrik al-Sulami, from Luqman ibn Amir al-Awsabi, from Utbah ibn Abd al-Sulami, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for clothing, and he clothed me with two coarse garments. I saw myself wearing them, and I was among the best-clothed of his Companions."
"15407","308 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, Safwan ibn Amr narrated, from Aqil ibn Mudrik, from Utbah ibn Abd, that when he pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said to him: What is your name? He said: Nushbah. He said: You are Utbah ibn Abd."
"15408","309 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated, Hariz ibn Uthman narrated, and Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to me, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated, they said: Hariz ibn Uthman narrated, from Shurahbil ibn Shufah, he said: Utbah ibn Abd al-Sulami met me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No Muslim loses three children who have not reached puberty but they will meet him at the eight gates of Paradise; he may enter through whichever he wishes."
"15409","310 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated, Safwan ibn Amr narrated, Abu al-Muthanna al-Mulayki narrated to me, from Utbah ibn Abd, Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Slain are three: a believing man who strives with his wealth and soul in the path of Allah until, when he meets the enemy, he fights them until killed - he said: that is the boasting martyr in the tent of Allah beneath His Throne; none are preferred over them but by the merit of the degree of prophethood. And a believing man who burdened himself with sins and faults and did much, who strove with his soul and wealth in the path of Allah until, when he met the enemy, he fought them until killed - that is a rinsing that washes away his sins and faults; the sword wipes away faults, and he is admitted through whichever gate of Paradise he wishes, for it has eight gates and Hell has seven gates, some better than others. And a hypocrite man who strove with his soul and wealth in the path of Allah until, when he met the enemy, he fought them until killed - he said: that one is in the Fire; the sword does not wipe away hypocrisy."
"15410","311 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak and Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from Safwan ibn Amr, from Abi al-Muthanna al-Mulayki, from Utbah ibn Abd al-Sulami - and he was of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The slain are three men: a believer who strove with his wealth and soul in the path of Allah until, when he met the enemy, he fought them until killed - that is the boasting martyr in the tent of Allah beneath His Throne; the Prophets do not surpass him but by the degree of prophethood. And a believing man who burdened himself with sins and faults, who strove with his wealth and soul in the path of Allah until, when he met the enemy - until killed - that is a rinsing that washes away his sins and faults; the sword wipes away faults, and he is admitted through whichever gate of Paradise he wishes, for it has eight gates, some better than others, and Hell has seven gates. And a hypocrite man who strove with his soul and wealth in the path of Allah until, when he met the enemy, he fought them until killed - that one is in the Fire; the sword does not wipe away hypocrisy."
"15411","312 - Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Abu Tawbah al-Rabi ibn Nafi narrated, Muawiyah ibn Sallam narrated, from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Aba Sallam saying: Amir ibn Zayd al-Bikali narrated to me, that he heard Utbah ibn Abd al-Sulami saying: A bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What is this Hawd of yours that you speak of? He said: Like the distance between al-Bayda and Busra; Allah will extend me therein with a watering trough whose ends no created human knows. Umar ibn al-Khattab - may Allah be pleased with him - said Allahu Akbar. He said: As for the Hawd, the poor Emigrants who fight in the path of Allah will come to me at it, and I hope Allah will show me the trough so I drink from it. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Lord has promised me to admit seventy thousand of my ummah to Paradise without reckoning, then each thousand will intercede for seventy thousand, then my Lord will scoop for me with His two hands three scoops. Umar said Allahu Akbar and said: The first seventy thousand - Allah will let them intercede for their fathers and tribes, and I hope Allah will place me in one of the last scoops. The bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, is there fruit in it? He said: Yes, and in it is a tree called Tuba, matching al-Firdaws. He said: Which tree of our land does it resemble? He said: It resembles nothing of your land's trees, but have you been to Sham? He said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: It resembles a tree in Sham called the walnut, growing on a single trunk, then spreading at its top. He said: How great is its base? He said: If a young she-camel of your family's camels were to set out, it would not circle its base before its collarbone breaks from old age. He said: Is there grape in it? He said: Yes. He said: How great is its cluster? He said: A month's journey for the pied crow, without turning or tiring. He said: How great is its berry? He said: Did your father ever slaughter something great of his sheep? He said: Yes. He said: Then he skinned its hide and gave it to your mother? And said: Tan this, then make for us from it a bucket with which we water our livestock? He said: Yes. He said: Then it is like that. He said: That would suffice me and my household? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And most of your tribe."
"15412","313 - Abd Allah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated, Abd al-Razzaq narrated, Mamar narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Amr ibn Zayd al-Bikali, from Utbah ibn Abd al-Sulami, he said: A bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about Paradise and mentioned the Hawd, saying: Is there fruit in it? He said: Yes, and in it is a tree called Tuba. He said: O Messenger of Allah, which tree of our land does it resemble? He said: It resembles nothing of your land's trees. Have you been to Sham? For there is a tree there called the walnut, growing on a trunk with its top branching. He said: O Messenger of Allah, how great is its base? He said: If a young she-camel of your family's camels were to set out, you would not encompass its base before its collarbone breaks from old age. He said: Is there grape in it? He said: Yes. He said: How great is its cluster? He said: A month's journey for the pied crow, without tiring. He said: How great is its berry? He said: Your father and mother took a young she-camel, slaughtered it and skinned its hide, then said: Make for us from it a bucket. He said: O Messenger of Allah, that berry would suffice me and my family? He said: Yes, and most of your tribe."
"15413","314 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated, Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Abi Humayd al-Ruayni, Yazid Dhu Misr told me, he said: I came to Utbah ibn Abd al-Sulami, Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: O Aba al-Walid, I went out seeking sacrificial animals and found nothing but a toothless one, and I disliked it. What do you say? He said: Why did you not come to me so I could sacrifice it for you? I said: Glory be to Allah, it is not valid for you nor valid for me? He said: Yes, because you doubt and I do not doubt. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade the yellow-eyed, the one whose horn is uprooted from its base, the blind whose eye has burst, the straggler that cannot follow the flock from lameness and weakness, and the broken-boned cripple."
"15414","315 - Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Habban al-Missisi narrated, Isa ibn Yunus narrated, and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, from al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amir, from Utbah ibn Abd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to his wife, let him cover himself and not strip as the donkey strips."
"15415","316 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated, Salamah ibn Raja narrated, from al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amir, from Utbah ibn Abd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command dyeing the hair, in opposition to the non-Arabs."
"15416","317 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated, from al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, Abu Amir al-Alhani narrated to me, from Utbah ibn Abd, and Abi Umamah, and Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, Ruzayq ibn al-Sakht narrated, al-Walid ibn al-Qasim al-Alhani narrated, al-Ahwas ibn Hakim narrated, Abd Allah ibn Amir narrated to me, that Abu Umamah and Utbah ibn Abd al-Sulami narrated to him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever prays the dawn prayer in congregation, then remains in the mosque glorifying Allah the glorification of forenoon, will have like the reward of a pilgrim and one performing Umrah, complete for him his Hajj and his Umrah."
"15417","318 - Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Mushir and Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated, they said: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Habib ibn Ubayd, from Utbah ibn Abd al-Sulami, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a bedouin came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I hear you mention in Paradise a tree I know none thornier than - meaning the talh. He said: The castrated billy-goat - meaning the gelded - therein are seventy kinds of food, no kind resembling another."
"15418","319 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Sabbah al-Mismai narrated, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Nasr ibn Shafiyy, from a shaykh of Banu Sulaym, from Utbah ibn Abd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cutting horses' tails, forelocks and manes. As for their tails, they are their fly-whisks; as for their manes, they are their warmth; as for their forelocks, good is tied therein."
"15419","320 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated, Abd al-Razzaq ibn Hammam narrated, from Sufyan, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from a man called Nasr, from Utbah ibn Abd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"15420","321 - Ibrahim ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Alhani, Yazid ibn Zayd narrated to me, from Utbah ibn Abd, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No servant leaves his house for morning or evening going to the mosque but his steps are a step as expiation and a step as a good deed."
"15421","322 - Jafar ibn Ahmad al-Shami al-Kufi narrated to us, Jubarah ibn Mughallis narrated, Bishr ibn Umarah narrated, from al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, from Rashid ibn Sad, from Utbah ibn Abd, and Abi al-Darda, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take suhur at the end of the night. And he used to say: It is the blessed morning meal."
"15422","323 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated, and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh al-Himsi narrated, they said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Sulami, from Utbah ibn Abd al-Sulami, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): How was the beginning of your affair? And he mentioned the hadith."
"15423","324 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Bukayr ibn Amir narrated, from al-Sha'bi, that Utbah ibn Farqad bought land on the bank of the Euphrates and made it reeds. When Umar came, he mentioned that he had bought land, and he said to him: From whom? He said: From its owners. When evening came his companions gathered and he called him and said: From whom did you buy the land? He said: From its owners. He said: Did you sell him anything? They said: No. He said: These are its owners, so return the land to whom you bought it from and take back the price."
"15424","325 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Arfajah, he said: We were mentioning the month of Ramadan, and Utbah ibn Farqad said: What are you mentioning? We said: We mention the month of Ramadan. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: In it the gates of Paradise are opened and the gates of Fire are closed and the devils are chained, and a caller calls every night: O seeker of good, come forth, and O seeker of evil, desist."
"15425","326 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated, Abd Allah ibn Harb narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Arfajah al-Thaqafi, from Utbah ibn Farqad al-Sulami, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When the month of Ramadan comes, the gates of Paradise are opened and the gates of Fire are closed and the devils are chained, and a caller calls: O seeker of good, come forth, and O seeker of evil, desist, until the month passes."
"15426","327 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Arfajah, with its isnad the like of it."
"15427","328 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, Ali ibn Qutaybah narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Aqil ibn Talhah, from Utbah ibn Farqad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw lagging among his Companions and called among them: O companions of Surat al-Baqarah."
"15428","329 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, my father narrated, and Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from Husayn, Umm Asim, wife of Utbah ibn Farqad, told me, she said: We were with Utbah, women who perfume themselves and go out, yet he had the best scent among us though he did no more than oil himself. We said to him: What is this scent? He said: Leprosy-like rash seized me in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I complained of it to him. He commanded me to cover my garment over me - meaning covering his private part - then he spat in his hands then wiped with them my back and belly."
"15429","330 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid narrated, from Husayn, from Umm Asim, wife of Utbah ibn Farqad, she said: We were with Utbah, women, each one of us wanting to be sweeter-scented than her companion, yet Utbah was sweetest in scent. When he went out he was known by his perfume's scent. I asked him about it and he said: Rash seized him in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he complained of it to him. He commanded him and he sat before him and placed his hand over his private part, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat in his hand and wiped his back and belly."
"15430","331 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Rabiah, and he is Ibn Awf, narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Husayn, from Umm Asim, wife of Utbah ibn Farqad, she said: We were three wives of Utbah, and we would perfume ourselves, yet he was sweetest of us in scent, though he did no more than oil his head and beard. One saying to him would say: O Ibn Farqad, how sweet your scent. She said to him: We perfume ourselves and you do no more than oil your head and beard, yet you are sweetest of us in scent - how is that? He said: Rash afflicted me, and he said: Come near. So I came near, and he took my lower waist-wrapper and placed it over my private part, then stretched his hands and blew into them, wiped one over the other, wiped one over my belly and the other over my back - this scent is from that."
"15431","332 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih ibn Safwan al-Sulami narrated to us, my father narrated to me, and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated, and Abd al-Malik ibn Bukayr ibn Yahya al-Misri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, they said: Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Talut ibn Zayd, from Ullayy ibn Rabah, from Utbah ibn al-Nuddar al-Sulami, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which of the two terms did Musa fulfill? He said: The kindest and most complete of them. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Musa wanted to part from Shuayb, peace be upon him, he told his wife to ask her father to give her of his sheep what they could live by. So he gave her what his sheep produced that year of single-colored births. When the sheep came to the watering trough, Musa, peace be upon him, stood facing the trough, and nothing issued from them but he struck its side, so they conceived and all bore single-colored, with among them no fashush, no dabub, no tha'ul, no kamshah whose udder escapes the hand. He said: If you conquer Sham you will find remnants of them, so take them - they are the Samiriyyah. Ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr said: My father said: al-fashush is she whose milk spurts at milking, al-dabub she whose udder sticks to the milk at milking, and al-kamshah she that withholds at milking."
"15432","333 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Maslamah ibn Ali, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to me, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Ullayy ibn Rabah, he said: I heard Utbah ibn al-Nuddar say: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day and he recited Ta-Sin until, when he reached the story of Musa, peace be upon him, he said: Musa hired himself for eight or ten years for the chastity of his private part and the food of his belly."
"15433","334 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated, Abu Wahb Ubayd Allah ibn Ubayd al-Kalai narrated, from Makhul, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Utbah ibn al-Nuddar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When your campaigns extend far, spoils are deemed lawful, and resolutions multiply, then the best of your jihad is ribat."
"15434","335 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to me, he said: Utbah ibn Masud died in year forty-four."
"15435","336 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Sufyan narrated, he said: I heard al-Zuhri saying: Abd Allah ibn Masud was not earlier in emigration than his brother Utbah, but he died before him."
"15436","337 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated, Abu Muawiyah Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated, from al-Masudi, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Utbah ibn Masud died in the time of Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"15437","338 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated, Abu Asim narrated, Abu Madan al-Minqari narrated, Awn ibn Abd Allah narrated, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, he said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a black slave girl and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I owe a believing neck - will this suffice for me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is your Lord? She said: Allah is my Lord. He said: What is your religion? She said: Islam. He said: Who am I? She said: You are the Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? She said: Yes, I testify that you are the Messenger of Allah. He said: And do you pray the five? She said: Yes. He said: And do you fast Ramadan? She said: Yes. He said: And do you affirm what came from Allah? She said: Yes. He said: Then he struck her back and said: Free her, for she has sufficed for you."
"15438","339 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rabiah al-Kilabi narrated, Abu Umays Utbah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah narrated, from Awn ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from his father, he said: When Utbah ibn Masud died, Abd Allah ibn Masud wept. It was said to him: Do you weep? He said: My brother and my companion with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the most beloved of people to me - except for Umar ibn al-Khattab - may Allah be pleased with him."
"15439","340 - Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Ufayr narrated, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from Adi ibn Adi al-Kindi, he said: I heard al-Urs ibn Umayrah - and he was of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A man may do the deeds of the people of Fire for a time of his life, then the highway of the highways of Paradise is presented to him and he does it until he dies upon it - that is for what was written for him. And a man may do the deeds of the people of Paradise for a time of his life, then the highway of the highways of Fire is presented to him and he does it until he dies upon it - that is for what was written for him."
"15440","341 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated, he said: I heard Adi ibn Adi saying: Raja ibn Haywah and al-Urs ibn Umayrah narrated to me that a man of Hadramawt and Imru al-Qays ibn Abis - between him and another there was a dispute over land of his - came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked the Hadrami for proof, and he had no proof, so he ruled for Imru al-Qays with the oath. The Hadrami said: O Messenger of Allah, have you enabled him to take the oath? By Allah, my land is gone. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a false oath to cut off thereby the wealth of a Muslim man will meet Allah while He is angry with him. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Imru al-Qays and recited to him this verse. Imru al-Qays said: O Messenger of Allah, what is for one who leaves it? He said: Paradise. He said: Then I call you to witness that I have left it."
"15441","342 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Salih ibn Abd Allah al-Tirmidhi narrated to me, Sufyan ibn Amir narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, from Adi ibn Adi, from his father, from al-Urs ibn Umayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give women authority to marry, so the previously-married speaks for herself and the permission of the virgin is her silence. Sufyan ibn Amir added al-Urs in the isnad. And al-Layth ibn Sad narrated it from Abi Husayn and did not go beyond Adi ibn Umayrah."
"15442","343 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Salamah ibn Abi Kabshah narrated, Salim ibn Nuh narrated, Umar ibn Amir al-Sulami narrated, Khalid ibn Yazid narrated, from Adi ibn Adi ibn Umayrah al-Kindi, from al-Urs ibn Umayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not punish the common people for the deed of the elite until the elite do a deed which the common people are able to change and do not change it - that is when Allah permits the destruction of the common people and the elite."
"15443","344 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Isa narrated, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Sayf ibn Sulayman, he said: I heard Adi ibn Adi saying: A freedman of ours narrated to me that he heard my grandfather saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah does not punish the common people for the deed of the elite - and he mentioned the like of it."
"15444","345 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Yaish narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from Mughirah ibn Ziyad, from Adi ibn Adi, from al-Urs ibn Umayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a sin is committed in the land, whoever witnesses it and denies it is like one absent from it, and whoever is absent from it and approves of it is like one who witnessed it."
"15445","346 - Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Aftah narrated, Yahya ibn Zahdam narrated, my father Zahdam ibn al-Harith narrated, from al-Urs ibn Umayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"15446","347 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated, from Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Bakkai, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr of the Ansar, then of Banu Umayyah ibn Zayd: Uwaym ibn Saidah - and Ibn Ishaq did not give his lineage - saying: He is an ally of Banu Amr ibn Awf, and it is said: He is of themselves."
"15447","348 - Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated, Abu Uways narrated, from Shurahbil ibn Sad, from Uwaym ibn Saidah al-Ansari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them at Masjid Quba and said: Allah Almighty has praised you well for purification in the story of your mosque - what is the purification with which you purify? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we know nothing but that we had Jewish neighbors who would wash their backsides from stool, so we washed as they washed."
"15448","349 - Khalaf ibn Umar al-Ukbari narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uwaym ibn Saidah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah chose me and chose Companions for me, making among them ministers, helpers and in-laws for me. Whoever reviles them, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people; neither sarf nor adl will be accepted from him on the Day of Resurrection."
"15449","350 - Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uwaym ibn Saidah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Marry virgins, for they are sweetest in mouths, most fruitful in wombs, and most content with little."
"15450","351 - Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uwaym ibn Saidah narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rebuked a man with a Persian bow and said: Throw it away. Then he pointed to the Arab bow and said: With this and with the spear of the lance you will be established in lands and given victory over your enemy."
"15451","352 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul narrated, from Amr ibn Tamim ibn Uwaym, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: My sister Mulaykah and a woman of ours called Umm Afif bint Masruh were under Hamal ibn al-Nabighah. Umm Afif struck Mulaykah with her house's tent-pole while she was pregnant, killing her and what was in her belly. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled for her blood-money and for her fetus a ghurrah - a slave or slave-girl. Her brother al-Ala ibn Masruh said: O Messenger of Allah, do we pay for one who neither ate nor drank nor looked nor cried out? Is the like of this annulled? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rhyming like the rhyming of the Jahiliyyah?"
"15452","353 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Arfajah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be tribulations and tribulations; whoever comes to the ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while they are united, wanting to split them - kill him, whoever he is."
"15453","354 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Arfajah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes out against my ummah while they are united, wanting to split them - kill him, whoever he is."
"15454","355 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated, Israil narrated, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Arfajah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: After me there will be tribulations and tribulations; whoever you see wanting to split the ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while they are united - kill him, whoever he is."
"15455","356 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abu Mardaniyyah narrated, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Arfajah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be tribulations and tribulations; whoever you see splitting the ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - kill him, whoever he is."
"15456","357 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, my father narrated to me, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Arfajah al-Ashjai, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: After me there will be tribulations and tribulations - and he raised his voice with it - whoever wants to split the ummah of Muhammad, Allah's blessings be upon him, while their affair is united - kill him, whoever he is. He swore he did not except anyone of the people."
"15457","358 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Abd Allah ibn al-Mukhtar and Layth, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Arfajah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: After me there will be tribulations and tribulations; whoever you see walking to the ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), splitting its unity - kill him."
"15458","359 - Abd Allah ibn al-Sabbah al-Asbahani and Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawzi narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Abd Allah ibn al-Mukhtar, Layth ibn Abi Sulaym and al-Fadl ibn Fadalalah, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Arfajah, he raised the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There will be tribulations and tribulations; whoever you see walking to the ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while they are united, to split them - kill him, whoever he is."
"15459","360 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn narrated, Hushaym narrated, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab and Mujalid, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Arfajah, a man of his people, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever walks to my ummah while they are united, wanting to split them - kill him, whoever he is."
"15460","361 - Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Saffar narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated, Shu'bah narrated, and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Shu'bah, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Arfajah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will be tribulations and tribulations; whoever wants to split the affair of the Muslims while they are united - strike him with the sword, whoever he is."
"15461","362 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Fadl ibn Muwaffaq narrated, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarani narrated, they said: Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated, from Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Bajali, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Arfajah ibn Durayh al-Ashjai, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: After me there will be tribulations and tribulations; whoever you see leaving the community or wanting to split the ummah of Muhammad while their affair is united - kill him, whoever he is. The Hand of Allah is upon the community, and Satan is with one who leaves the community."
"15462","363 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated, Abu Asim narrated, Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn Bashir al-Aslami narrated, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Arfajah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be tribulations and tribulations; whoever wants to split the ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - kill him, whoever he is."
"15463","364 - Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Ayyub al-Sarifini narrated, Abu Usamah narrated, from Zakariyya ibn Siyah al-Thaqafi, Ziyad ibn Ilaqah narrated, from Arfajah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be tribulations and tribulations - raising his voice with it - whoever you see wanting to split the affair of my ummah while it is united - kill him, whoever he is."
"15464","365 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated, Abu Mashar al-Bara narrated, from al-Abbas ibn Awsajah, from al-Furat al-Qazzaz, from Abi Asim, from Arfajah ibn Durayh al-Ashjai, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are upon unity and one comes splitting your unity and breaking your staff - kill him, whoever he is."
"15465","366 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Yunus ibn Abi Yaqub narrated, from his father, from Arfajah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever comes to you while your affair is united upon one man, wanting to split your unity - kill him."
"15466","367 - Abu Amir Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Nahwi al-Suri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated, Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Abi Malik narrated, from his father, from Arfajah ibn Sharahil, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: After me there will be tribulations and tribulations; whoever comes to my ummah while they are united, splitting the affair of their unity - kill him."
"15467","368 - al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya and Muhammad ibn Dawud al-Tawzi narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated, Abu Muawiyah narrated, from Yazid ibn Mardaniyyah, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Arfajah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Hand of Allah is upon the community, and Satan is with one who opposes the community, running."
"15468","369 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Kaysan al-Missisi narrated to us, Khabbab ibn Hilal narrated, and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari and Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated, and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yala ibn Abbad ibn Yala narrated, and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Numan al-Jawhari narrated, and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated, and Muhammad ibn Abd Musa ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, they said: Abu al-Ashhab Jafar ibn Hayyan narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tarafah, from Arfajah ibn Asad, that his nose was cut on the day of al-Kulab in the Jahiliyyah, so he took a nose of silver which rotted upon him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to take a nose of gold."
"15469","370 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to me, Abu al-Ashhab narrated, Abd al-Rahman Turfah narrated to me, from his grandfather Arfajah ibn Asad, that his nose was cut on the day of al-Kulab in the Jahiliyyah; he took a nose of silver which rotted upon him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to take a nose of gold."
"15470","371 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated, my father narrated to me, Salm ibn Zarir narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Tarafah ibn Arfajah narrated, that Arfajah's nose was cut on the day of al-Kulab, so he took a nose of silver which rotted upon him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to take a nose of gold."
"15471","372 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Razi narrated, they said: Asim ibn Hilal narrated, Ghadairah ibn Urwah al-Fuqaymi told me, my father told me, he said: I came to Madinah and entered the mosque while people were waiting for prayer. A man came out to us with his head dripping from ablution he had performed or from a bath he had taken. He led us in prayer. When we prayed, people began standing to him saying: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of such? O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of such? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Thus, O people, Allah's religion is in ease - three times. And I went out of the door and left."
"15472","373 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, Utbah ibn Tamim Abu Saba narrated, from al-Walid ibn Amir al-Muzani, from Urwah ibn Muattib al-Ansari, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled that the owner of the mount is most entitled to its front."
"15473","374 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abi al-Aswad, he said: When people began the Hajj of year nine, Urwah ibn Masud came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a Muslim and sought permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to return to his people. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I fear they will kill you. He said: If they found me sleeping they would not wake me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him, and he returned to his people as a Muslim. He presented supper, and Thaqif came greeting him. He called them to Islam, and they accused him, angered him and let him hear what he had not expected. Then they left him, until when they entered dawn and daybreak rose, he stood on a balcony in his house, called the adhan for prayer and bore witness, and a man of Thaqif shot him with an arrow and killed him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of Urwah is like the companion of Ya-Sin: he called his people to Allah and they killed him."
"15474","375 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyabi narrated, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, he said: When Abu Bakr departed and people stayed for their Hajj, Urwah ibn Masud al-Thaqafi came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and became Muslim, then sought permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to return to his people. He said: I fear they will kill you. He said: If they found me sleeping they would not wake me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him, and he returned to Taif. He presented supper, and Thaqif came greeting him. He called them to Islam and advised them, and they accused him, disobeyed him and let him hear of harm what he had not feared from them. They left him, until when they entered dawn and daybreak rose, he stood in a balcony in his house, called the adhan for prayer and bore witness, and a man of Quraysh shot him with an arrow and killed him."
"15475","376 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jubarah ibn Mughallis narrated, Abd Allah ibn Hakim narrated, from Hajjaj, from Dawud ibn Abi Asim, from Urwah ibn Masud al-Thaqafi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had water with him; when women reached it he would dip their hands in it."
"15476","377 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, from Amir, Urwah ibn Mudarris ibn Aws ibn Harithah narrated to me, that he performed Hajj in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but did not catch the people except at night while they were at Jam; so he went to Arafat at night and poured forth from it, then returned to Jam and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I wore myself out and tired my mount - do I have Hajj? He said: Whoever prayed with us the dawn prayer at Jam and stood with us until we pour forth, having poured forth from Arafat before that by night or day, has completed and ended his tafath."
"15477","378 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Sufyan narrated, Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard Urwah ibn Mudarris ibn Harithah ibn Lam saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Muzdalifah and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come to you now from the two mountains of Tayy, having worn out my mount and tired myself - do I have Hajj? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever witnesses with us this prayer and stands with us until we pour forth, having stood at Arafah before that by night or day, his Hajj is complete and he has ended his tafath."
"15478","379 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, they said: Shu'bah ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Safar narrated, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn Mudarris, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at Jam and said: O Messenger of Allah, do I have Hajj? He said: Whoever prayed with us this prayer and stood with us at this standing-place, having poured forth from Arafat before that by night or day, his Hajj is complete and he has ended his tafath. And the wording is of the hadith of Sulayman ibn Harb."
"15479","380 - Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'bah ibn Juwan narrated, Abu Asim narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi al-Safar, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn Mudarris, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, do I have Hajj? He said: Whoever prayed with us this prayer and stood with us at these standing-places, having poured forth from Arafat before that by night or day, his Hajj is complete and he has ended his tafath."
"15480","381 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated, they said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated, from Abu Dawud ibn Yazid al-Awdi, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn Mudarris al-Tai, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Jam before he pours forth. When he looked at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: O Messenger of Allah, I crossed the two mountains and met hardship. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches our pouring forth has caught the Hajj. And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad added in his hadith, from Zahmawayh: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Calm your fear; whoever catches this pouring forth of ours has caught the Hajj."
"15481","382 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn Mudarris, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing at Muzdalifah, and he said: Whoever prayed this prayer of ours then pours forth with us, having stood before that at Arafah by night or day, his Hajj is complete."
"15482","383 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Khalid ibn Ubayd Allah narrated, and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, they said: Khalid narrated, from Mutarrif, from Amir, from Urwah ibn Mudarris, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I tired and wore out and wore thin. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches Jam with the people and the imam before they pour forth has caught the Hajj, and whoever does not catch the people and the imam at Jam before they pour forth has not caught the Hajj."
"15483","384 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Mutarrif, from Amir, Urwah ibn Mudarris narrated to me, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I wore thin and tired and did and did. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches Jam and stands with the people until they pour forth has caught the Hajj, and whoever does not catch that has no Hajj."
"15484","385 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Sufyan narrated, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard Urwah ibn Mudarris ibn Aws ibn Harithah ibn Lam al-Tai saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Muzdalifah and said: O Messenger of Allah, I came from the two mountains of Tayy; by Allah, I came only after tiring myself and wearing out my mount, and I alighted at no mountain but I stood upon it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever witnesses with us this prayer, having stood at Arafah before that by night or day, his Hajj is complete and he has ended his tafath."
"15485","386 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Sad narrated, my uncle narrated, my father narrated, from Ibn Ishaq, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to me, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn Mudarris ibn Harithah ibn Lam al-Tai, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the standing-place of Jam and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come to you from the mountain of Tayy, having worn out my mount and tired myself; by Allah, I alighted at no mountain but I stood upon it - do I have Hajj, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prayed with us the dawn prayer at Jam, having come to Arafat before that by night or day, has ended his tafath and his Hajj is complete."
"15486","387 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatawani narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated, from Amir, from Urwah ibn Mudarris al-Tai, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was standing at Jam and said: O Messenger of Allah, I came from the mountain of Tayy, having humbled my mount and tired myself; by Allah, I alighted at no mountain but I stood upon it - do I have Hajj? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches with us this prayer, having come to Arafat before that by night or day, has ended his tafath and his Hajj is complete."
"15487","388 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, Amir narrated, from Urwah ibn Mudarris al-Tai, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he mentioned the like of it."
"15488","389 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Waki narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn Mudarris, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"15489","390 - Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwab al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated, Abd Allah ibn Bazigh narrated, from Sadaqah ibn Abi Imran, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah al-Tai, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at the standing-place at Jam and said: O Messenger of Allah, I came from the two mountains of Tayy, wearing myself out and tiring my mount; by Allah, I alighted at no mountain but I stood upon it - do I have Hajj, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prayed with us this prayer, having come to Arafah by night or day, has ended his tafath and his Hajj is complete."
"15490","391 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ali ibn Muslim al-Muaddib narrated, Yahya ibn Yala narrated, my father narrated to me, from Ghaylan ibn Jami, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Urwah ibn Mudarris, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at Jam with people around him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man of Tayy of the two mountains, and I humbled my mount; by Allah, I alighted at no mountain you stood at but I stood upon it - do I have Hajj, O Messenger of Allah? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever witnesses with us this prayer, his Hajj is complete and he has ended his tafath."
"15491","392 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Tamimi narrated, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn Mudarris, with its isnad the like of it."
"15492","393 - Bakr ibn Muhammad Abu Umar al-Qazzaz al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muawiyah al-Ziyadi narrated, Sad ibn Amir narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Zayd, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn Mudarris, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Jam and said: O Messenger of Allah, do I have Hajj? He said: Whoever prayed with us this prayer in this place, having poured forth before that from Arafat by night or day, his Hajj is complete and he has ended his tafath."
"15493","394 - Abdan ibn Ahmad and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, they said: Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Dirhami narrated, Umayyah ibn Khalid narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Sayyar, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn Mudarris, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Jam and said: O Messenger of Allah, I came from the two mountains of Tayy, leaving no mountain but I stood upon it - do I have Hajj? He said: Whoever prayed this prayer with us, having poured forth from Arafah by night or day, his Hajj is complete and he has ended his tafath."
"15494","395 - Ahmad ibn Zayd ibn al-Harish al-Ahwazi narrated to us, my father narrated, and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated, Imran ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn Mudarris, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man is with whom he loves."
"15495","396 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, from al-Sha'bi, Urwah al-Bariqi narrated to me, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses - good is tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"15496","397 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Safar and Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn Abi al-Jad, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Good is tied in the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection - reward and spoils."
"15497","398 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated, they said: Khalid narrated, and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid narrated, from Husayn, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Urwah al-Bariqi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses - good is tied in their forelocks, and reward, until the Day of Resurrection."
"15498","399 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Muhammad ibn Fudayl and Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated, from Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses - good is tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is that? He said: Reward and spoils."
"15499","400 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Hasan ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated, from Zaidah, from Husayn, from Urwah al-Bariqi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Horses - good is tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"15500","401 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, they said: Zuhayr narrated, Jabir narrated, from Amir, from Urwah al-Bariqi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses - good is tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"15501","402 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Sufyan narrated, Mujalid narrated, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it, with the addition therein of reward and spoils."
"15502","403 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Amr ibn Abd Allah al-Awdi narrated, my father narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah al-Bariqi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj. Thus Amr al-Awdi narrated it from his father from Sufyan. And people narrate it from Sufyan from Jabir from al-Sha'bi from Wahb ibn Hanbash - and that is the correct."
"15503","404 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, they said: Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated, from Husayn, from Amir, from Urwah al-Bariqi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Camels are honor for their people, and sheep are blessing."
"15504","405 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated, from Abi Ishaq, he said: Urwah al-Bariqi stopped by us while we were in our gathering and narrated to us, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Horses - good is tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"15505","406 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Abu Ishaq narrated, from Urwah al-Bariqi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"15506","407 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, Israil narrated, from Abi Ishaq, from Urwah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"15507","408 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Sinan ibn Muthar narrated, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abi Jafar al-Farra, from Abi Ishaq, from Urwah al-Bariqi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses - good is tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"15508","409 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Abi Ishaq, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Urwah ibn Abi al-Jad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses - good is tied in their forelocks."
"15509","410 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated, and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith and Yahya al-Himmani narrated, they said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated, Shabib ibn Gharqadah narrated, from Urwah al-Bariqi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good is tied in the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection."
"15510","411 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Sufyan narrated, Shabib ibn Gharqadah narrated, he said: I heard Urwah ibn Abi al-Jad al-Bariqi saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Horses - good is tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"15511","412 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Sufyan narrated, Shabib ibn Gharqadah narrated, that he heard the clan narrating to him from Urwah ibn Abi al-Jad al-Bariqi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him a dinar to buy for him a sacrificial animal with it. Urwah said: So I bought for him with it two sheep, then sold one of them for a dinar and a sheep. Then he prayed for me for blessing in trade. And when he would buy dust he would profit in it."
"15512","413 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Shabib, from Urwah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"15513","414 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Harami ibn Hafs narrated, Said ibn Zayd narrated, from al-Zubayr ibn Hurayth, from Nuaym ibn Abi Hind, from Urwah al-Bariqi, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twisting the forelock of a horse between his fingers, then said: Horses - good is tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"15514","415 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from Aidh ibn Nusayb, from Urwah al-Bariqi, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come to a reddish horse in the market of Madinah with my uncles, exposing its forelock with his two fingers, saying: Horses - good is tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"15515","416 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Abi Humaydah al-Taini, from Urwah al-Bariqi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses - good is tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"15516","417 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi al-Tahhan al-Misri and al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari both said: Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh told us: Bishr ibn Bakr told us: from al-Awzai, from Abu Humaydah, from Urwah al-Bariqi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Goodness is tied in the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection."
"15517","Simak ibn Harb, from Urwah al-Bariqi. 418 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji told us: Bundar ibn Bashshar told us: Muslim ibn Qutaybah told us: from al-Masudi, from Simak ibn Harb, from Urwah al-Bariqi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly, he said: Horses have goodness tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"15518","Shurayh ibn Hani, from Urwah al-Bariqi. 419 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi told us: Abdullah ibn Raja told us: Israil told us: from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Urwah al-Bariqi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Goodness is tied in the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection."
"15519","420 - Musa ibn Harun told us: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh told us: Yahya ibn Adam told us: Israil told us: from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Urwah al-Bariqi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Goodness is tied in the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection."
"15520","Abu Labid, from Urwah al-Bariqi. 421 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim told us: Said ibn Zayd told us: al-Zubayr ibn Hurayth told us: from Abu Labid, from Urwah al-Bariqi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a caravan of goods for sale, and he gave him a dinar and said: Buy a sheep for us. So he went and bought two sheep for a dinar, then a man met him and he sold him a sheep for a dinar, then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a dinar and a sheep, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: May Allah bless for you in your hand bargain. He said: I would stand in the rubbish dump and would not return to my family until I had profited forty thousand."
"15521","Those named Uyaynah. Uyaynah ibn Badr al-Fazari. 422 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawwazi told us: Sulayman ibn Umar told us: from Khalid al-Raqqi: Marwan ibn Muawiyah al-Fazari told us: from Malik ibn Abi al-Husayn, from Uqbah, a shaykh from Fazarah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Uyaynah ibn Badr and Hisn entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while Abu Bakr and Umar were with him, all sitting together on the ground, so he called for a cushion for Uyaynah and seated him on it and said: When a noble man of a people comes to you, honor him."
"15522","Those named Attab. Attab ibn Asid ibn Abi al-Is ibn Umayyah ibn Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf, and his mother was Zaynab bint Amr ibn Umayyah ibn Abd Shams. He was a governor of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over Makkah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while he was his agent over it. What Attab ibn Asid narrated. 423 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us: Harami ibn Hafs al-Qasmali told me: Khalid ibn Abi Uthman al-Qurashi told us: from Ayyub ibn Abdullah ibn Yasar, from Amr ibn Abi Aqrab who said: I heard Attab ibn Asid, while leaning his back against the House of Allah, saying: By Allah, I did not gain in this office which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to me except two decorated garments, and I clothed Kaysan, my freed slave, with them."
"15523","424 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud told us: Khalid ibn Nizar al-Mawsili told us: Muhammad ibn Salih al-Tammar told us: from Ibn Shihab, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Attab ibn Asid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about the zakat of vineyards: They are estimated like palm trees are estimated, then their zakat is paid as raisins just as the zakat of palm trees is paid as dates."
"15524","425 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki told us: Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib told us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad told us: from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from his brother Abdullah ibn Ubaydah, from Attab ibn Asid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him when he appointed him over Makkah: Will you convey from me to your people what I command you with? Say to them: No one should combine a sale and a salam contract, no one should sell a sale involving uncertainty, and no one should sell what he does not have."
"15525","426 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi told us: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa told us: Ibn Abi al-Wazir told us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad told us: from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Ayyub ibn Khalid, from Attab ibn Asid, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A woman is not married together with her maternal aunt nor with her paternal aunt."
"15526","Attab ibn Shumayr al-Dabbi. 427 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us: Abu Nuaym told us: Abd al-Samad ibn Jabir ibn Rabiah told us: from Mujammi ibn Attab ibn Shumayr, from his father who said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I have an old shaykh and brothers, so I will go to them so that perhaps they will become Muslim and I will bring them to you. He said: If they become Muslim it is better for them, and if they remain, Islam is wide and spacious."
"15527","Those named Atiyyah. Atiyyah al-Qurazi, he used to live in Kufah. 428 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told us: from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, (Ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us: Abu Nuaym told us: Sufyan told us: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Atiyyah al-Qurazi, who said: I was among those taken on the day of Qurayzah, and they would kill whoever had grown pubic hair and leave whoever had not grown it, and I was among those left."
"15528","429 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi told us: Amr ibn Marzuq told us: Shubah told us: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr who said: Atiyyah said: I was among the captives of Banu Qurayzah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has not grown hair, leave him. So they looked and did not see anything, and they released me."
"15529","430 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani told us: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli told us: Muhammad ibn Salamah told us, (Ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, the author of al-Maghazi, told us: Ibrahim ibn Sad told us: from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj told me: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Atiyyah al-Qurazi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had ordered the killing of everyone from Banu Qurayzah who had grown hair, and I was a boy and they found me not grown, so they released me."
"15530","431 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told us: from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Atiyyah, and he mentioned something similar."
"15531","432 - Bishr ibn Musa told us: al-Humaydi told us: Sufyan told us: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr who said: I heard Atiyyah al-Qurazi saying: On the day Sad ibn Muadh gave judgment concerning Banu Qurayzah I was a boy, so they looked at my waist-wrapper and did not find me grown, and here I am among you."
"15532","433 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us: Arim Abu al-Numan told us: Abu Awanah told us: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Atiyyah al-Qurazi, who said: I was among those concerning whom Sad gave judgment. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that their fighters be killed and their offspring taken captive. He said: I was brought and I thought only that he would kill me. He said: He uncovered my pubic area and they looked at it and found it had not grown, so they placed me among the captives."
"15533","434 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani told us: My father told us: Zuhayr told us: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr told us: from Atiyyah al-Qurazi who said: I was among those against whom Sad passed judgment, and they doubted about me, whether I was among the fighters or among the offspring, so they looked at my pubic area and found it had not grown, so they cast me among the offspring."
"15534","435 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji told us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath told us: Hammad ibn Salamah told us: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr: Atiyyah al-Qurazi told me, he said: I was presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the time of Qurayzah; whoever among us had reached puberty or his pubic hair had grown was killed, so they looked at me and I had not grown pubic hair, so I was left."
"15535","436 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi told us: Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruasi told us: Yazid ibn Ata told us: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Atiyyah al-Qurazi, (Ha). And Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari and Abu Hanifah al-Wasiti told us, they said: Mamar ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi told us: Amir ibn Mudrik told us: from Ali ibn Salih, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Atiyyah al-Qurazi, who said: I was among the captives presented, among those presented from the captives at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they did not find me grown, so I was released."
"15536","437 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari told us: Yahya al-Himmani told us: Sharik told us: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Atiyyah al-Qurazi, who said: I was presented to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Qurayzah, and they did not find me grown, so they let me go."
"15537","438 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us: My father told me: Hushaym told us: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Atiyyah al-Qurazi who said: I was among those presented to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Qurayzah, and they doubted about me, so they looked at my pubic area and it had not grown, so I was released."
"15538","439 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us: Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Talqani told us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah told us: from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, who said: I heard a man in the mosque of Kufah saying: On the day Sad ibn Muadh gave judgment concerning Banu Qurayzah I was a boy, and they doubted about me, but they did not find the razor had been run over me, so I was spared."
"15539","Atiyyah ibn Sad al-Sadi, from Banu Jusham ibn Sad. 440 - Yusuf al-Qadi told us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Attab told us: Hammad ibn Salamah told us: Abu al-Miqdam Raja told us: from Ismail ibn Atiyyah - a man from Banu Jusham - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wealth of Allah is asked for and given."
"15540","441 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari told us: from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Simak ibn al-Fadl, from Urwah ibn Muhammad ibn Atiyyah, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The giving hand is better than the lower hand."
"15541","442 - Muhammad ibn Abi Zura told us: Hisham ibn Ammar told us, (Ha). And Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi told us: Sahl ibn Zanjalah al-Razi told us, they said: al-Walid ibn Muslim told us: Ibn Jabir told me: Urwah ibn Muhammad ibn Atiyyah told me: from his father, from his grandfather Atiyyah ibn Sad who said: I came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among a group from Banu Sad, and I was the youngest of them, so they left me behind with their baggage. They came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and fulfilled their needs, and he said: Is anyone left? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, a boy left behind with our baggage. So he ordered them to call me, and I came to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever Allah gives you, do not ask the people for anything, for the upper hand is the giving hand and the lower hand is the one given to, and Allah is the One asked and the Giver. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke to me in our dialect."
"15542","443 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us: My father told me, (Ha). And Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami told us: Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us: Ibrahim ibn Khalid told us: Abu Wail al-Sanani al-Muradi told me, he said: We were sitting with Urwah ibn Muhammad, he said: My father told me, from my grandfather Atiyyah, and he had companionship, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Anger is from Satan, and Satan was created from fire, and fire is only extinguished with water, so when one of you becomes angry, let him perform ablution."
"15543","444 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us: My father told me, (Ha). And Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami told us: Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us: Ibrahim ibn Khalid al-Sanani told us: Umayyah ibn Shibl told me, and others, from Urwah ibn Muhammad, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the ruler burns with rage, Satan gains mastery."
"15544","445 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara said: Ali ibn al-Madini told us: Hisham ibn Yusuf told us: from al-Numan ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from Urwah ibn Muhammad ibn Atiyyah al-Sadi, from his father, from his grandfather Atiyyah, that he was among those who spoke to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the captives of Hawazin, and the Messenger of Allah said: Your kin and your origin and all the foster mothers. And he said: For this day we kept you back, and they are your mothers and your sisters and your maternal aunts. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke to his companions, and they returned their captives to them except two men, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go and give them the choice. One of them said: I leave him, and the other said: I will not leave him. When he turned away, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He chose well for himself. He would pass by the virgin slave girl and the boy and leave him, until he passed by an old woman and said: I will take this one, for she is the mother of a clan and they will ransom her from me for whatever they can. So Atiyyah exclaimed Allahu Akbar and said: Take her, O Messenger of Allah, there is no coolness in her mouth, nor is her breast firm, nor is her comer finding anything; an old woman, O Messenger of Allah, a freed captive woman with no one. When he saw no one turning to her, he left her."
"15545","446 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam told us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah told us, (Ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq told us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah told us, they said: Hashim ibn al-Qasim told us: Abu Aqil told us: Abdullah ibn Yazid told us: Rabiah ibn Yazid told me: from Atiyyah ibn Bashir, from Atiyyah al-Sadi, and he was among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The slave does not reach being among the God-fearing until he leaves what is harmless out of caution against what is harmful."
"15546","447 - Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas told us: My father told me: Ibn Wahb told us: Asim ibn Abdullah ibn Tamim told me: from his father, from Urwah ibn Muhammad, from his father, from his grandfather, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the delegation of his people, and when they entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Has anyone come to you other than you? They said: Yes, a youth from us whom we left behind with our baggage. He said: Send for him. When I entered upon him while they were with him, he received me and said: The giving hand is the upper one, and the asking hand is the lower one, and whatever you can do without, do not ask, for the wealth of Allah is asked for and given."
"15547","Atiyyah ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi. 448 - Abu Zura Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi told us: Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi told us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq told us: from Isa ibn Abdullah ibn Malik, from Atiyyah ibn Sufyan, from Abdullah, who said: A delegation from Thaqif came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Ramadan, and he pitched a tent for them in the mosque, and when they became Muslim they fasted with him."
"15548","Those named Ata. Ata al-Shaybi al-Hajabi. 449 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami told us: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim al-Awdi told us, (Ha). And Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani told us: Jafar ibn Imran al-Thalabi told us, they said: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi told us: Fitr ibn Khalifah told us: Ata, a man from Banu Shaybah, and he was a very old shaykh, told me, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying at this Station wearing two sandals of smooth tanned leather."
"15549","Ata ibn Ibrahim. 450 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami told us: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi told us: Abu Asim told us: from Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz, from Yahya ibn Ubayd ibn Ata, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Put straps on sandals."
"15550","Those named Asim. Asim ibn Adi al-Ansari, a Badr veteran. 451 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani told us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi told us: Muhammad ibn Fulayh told us: from Musa ibn Uqbah, from al-Zuhri who said: Asim ibn Adi ibn al-Jadd ibn al-Ajlan went out to Badr, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him back and allotted him his share."
"15551","452 - Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi told us: Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi told us: Ziyad ibn Abdullah al-Bika'i told us: from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: Asim ibn Adi ibn al-Jadd ibn Ajlan ibn Dubayah, and he is from Bali, an ally of Banu Ubayd ibn Zayd ibn Malik ibn Awf ibn Amr ibn Awf ibn Malik ibn al-Aws, went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Badr, and he sent him back and allotted him his share along with the people of Badr. And it is said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left him in charge over al-Aliyah. And it is said: He lived one hundred and fifteen years."
"15552","453 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi told us: al-Qanabi told us: Malik told us, (Ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us: al-Qanabi told us: from Malik, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, from Abu al-Baddah ibn Asim ibn Adi, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the camel herders regarding staying overnight: they stone on the day of sacrifice, then they stone the next day, and the day after for two days, then they stone on the day of departure."
"15553","454 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi told us: Dawud ibn Umayyah al-Zuhri told us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah told us: from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from Abu al-Baddah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"15554","455 - Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi told us: Uthman ibn al-Haytham told us: Ibn Jurayj told us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr told me: from his father, from Abu al-Baddah ibn Asim ibn Adi, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the camel herders to stone on the day of sacrifice, then leave a day and a night, then stone thereafter."
"15555","456 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari told us: Muhammad ibn Sahl told us: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari told us: from Ibn Jurayj, from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, from Abu al-Baddah, from Asim ibn Adi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the camel herders, taking turns, to stone on the day of sacrifice, then to leave."
"15556","457 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi told us: Muhammad ibn Aidh told us: al-Walid ibn Muslim told us: from Abdullah ibn Murshid, from Abu al-Baddah ibn Asim ibn Adi, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah on Monday, with twelve nights passed from Rabi al-Awwal, and he stayed in Madinah ten years."
"15557","458 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani told us: Ismail ibn Mujammi told us: from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from his father who said: Abu al-Baddah ibn Asim ibn Adi al-Ansari told me, from his father, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked us shortly after he arrived, and said: Where is the confinement of the flood? We said: We do not know. Then a man from Banu Sulaym passed by me, and I said: From where have you come? He said: From the confinement of the flood. So I called for my sandals and went down to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, you asked us about the confinement of the flood and we said we had no knowledge of it, and this man passed by me and I asked him and he claimed his family is there. So the Messenger of Allah asked him: Where is your family? He said: At the confinement of the flood. He said: Take your family out of it, for a fire is about to emerge from it that will light up the necks of camels at Busra."
"15558","459 - Musa ibn Harun told us: Umar ibn Zurarah al-Hadathi told us: Isa ibn Yunus told us: from Said ibn Umar al-Baghawi, from Asim ibn Abi al-Baddah ibn Asim ibn Adi, from his father, from his grandfather Asim ibn Adi who said: My brother and I bought one hundred shares from the shares of Khaybar, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O Asim, two attacking wolves that find sheep whose owner neglected them are not more corrupting to them than a man's love of wealth and honor is to his religion."
"15559","460 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani told us: Said ibn Sulayman told us: from Khalid ibn Abdullah, from Husayn, from al-Shabi, from Asim ibn Adi, that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when this verse was revealed: Then they do not bring four witnesses, I said: O Messenger of Allah, until they bring four witnesses, the treacherous one will have fulfilled his need. He said: He had not stood up until his cousin, his paternal uncle's son, came with his wife carrying a boy, and she was saying: He is from you, and he was saying: He is not from me. He said: Then the verse of mutual imprecation was revealed, and I am the first who spoke about it, and whoever is afflicted with it."
"15560","Asim ibn Thabit ibn Abi al-Aflah, and it is said Ibn al-Aflah al-Ansari, the protector of the hornets, a Badr veteran, killed in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 461 - al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman told us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi told us: Muhammad ibn Fulayh told us: from Musa ibn Uqbah, from al-Zuhri: Among the names of those from the Ansar who witnessed Badr: Asim ibn Thabit ibn Abi al-Aflah."
"15561","462 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil told us: Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi told us: My father told me: from Ibn Ishaq: Among the names of those from the Ansar who witnessed Badr: Asim ibn Thabit ibn Qays ibn al-Aflah ibn Ismah ibn Malik ibn Umayyah ibn Sasah ibn Zayd ibn Malik ibn Awf ibn Amr ibn Awf."
"15562","463 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari told us: from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, (Ha). And Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri told us: My father told me: Ibrahim ibn Sad told us: from al-Zuhri, from Umar ibn Asid ibn Jariyah al-Thaqafi, an ally of Banu Zuhrah, and he was among the companions of Abu Hurayrah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ten men as spies, and appointed over them Asim ibn Thabit al-Ansari, the grandfather of Asim ibn Amr. He mentioned it at length."
"15563","Asim ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi. 464 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib told us: Surayj ibn al-Numan al-Jawhari told us: Hashraj ibn Nubatah told us: from Hisham ibn Habib, from Qays ibn Asim, from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab sent to him seeking his help with some charity, but he refused to work for him, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: On the Day of Resurrection the ruler will be ordered and stood upon the bridge of Hell, and the bridge will be ordered and it will shake violently, and every bone of his will be displaced from its place, then Allah will order the bones and they will return to their place, then He will question him. If he was obedient to Allah, He will pull him out and give him two shares of reward, and if he was disobedient to Allah, the bridge will tilt with him and he will fall into Hell for seventy autumns."
"15564","Asim al-Laythi Abu Nasr. 465 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati told us: Musa ibn Ismail told us, (Ha). And Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Aburi al-Tustari told us: Uqbah ibn Sinan al-Dari told us, they said: Ghassan ibn Mudar told us: from Said ibn Yazid Abu Maslamah, from Nasr ibn Asim al-Laythi, from his father, who said: I entered the mosque of Madinah and the people were saying: We seek refuge in Allah from the anger of Allah and the anger of His Messenger. He said: I said: What is it? They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was preaching on his pulpit when a man stood and took his son by the hand and took him out of the mosque, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse the leader and the led; woe to this one one day, to this Ummah, from so-and-so with large buttocks."
"15565","Asim ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab. 466 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis told us: Said ibn Abi Maryam told us: Bakr ibn Mudar told us, (Ha). And Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani told us: My father told us: Bakr ibn Mudar told us, (Ha). And Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj told us: Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani told us: Bakr ibn Mudar told us: from Musa ibn Jubayr, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Asim ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divorced Hafsah bint Umar with one divorce, then took her back."
"15566","Asim al-Muzani. 467 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us: My father told me, (Ha). And Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati told us: Hamid ibn Yahya told us, they said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah told us: from Abd al-Malik ibn Nawfal ibn Musahiq: He heard Ibn Isam al-Muzani narrating from his father, and he had companionship, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send an army or an expedition, he would say to them: If you see a mosque or hear a caller to prayer, do not kill anyone. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us in an expedition and ordered us with that. We went traveling in the land of Tihamah, and a man driving women in litters caught up with us, so we presented Islam to him and said: Are you a Muslim? He said: What is Islam? So we informed him, and he did not know it. He said: If I do not do it, what will you do? We said: We will kill you. He said: Will you wait for me until I catch up with the litters? We said: Yes, and we will catch up with him. So he went out, and there was a woman in her litter, and he said: Accept Islam, Hubaysh, before life is cut off. She said: I accept Islam ten or nine times in succession, then he said: Go quickly. Then he came to us and said: Do as you wish. So we brought him near and struck his neck, and the other woman came down from her litter and knelt over him until she died."
"15567","Those named Ismah. Ismah ibn Malik al-Khatmi. 468 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri told us: Khalid ibn Abd al-Salam al-Sadafi told us: al-Fadl ibn al-Mukhtar told us: from Abdullah ibn Mawhab, from Ismah ibn Malik al-Khatmi, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Part of my body itched, so I put my hand in to scratch and my hand touched my private part. He said: That happens to me too."
"15568","469 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no reserved pasture in Islam, nor false bidding."
"15569","470 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited us at Quba, and when he wanted to return we brought him a Qahati donkey that cropped its steps, and he rode it. We said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a boy who will come with you to bring back the animal. He said: The owner of the animal is most entitled to its front. We said: O Messenger of Allah, ride and return it to us. So he went and returned it to us, trotting so it could not be kept pace with."
"15570","471 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Most of the hypocrites of my Ummah are its reciters."
"15571","472 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us in one of the lanes of Madinah and reached a rubbish heap of a people, and he said: O Hudhayfah, shield me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and urinated standing, then called for water and performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks and prayed."
"15572","473 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: A slave came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my master married me and wants to separate me and my wife. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit and said: O people, divorce is only in the hand of the one who took the leg."
"15573","474 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should sleep in a saffron-dyed garment, for it is attended."
"15574","475 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there were to be a prophet after me, it would be Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"15575","476 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The back of the believer is protected except by its right."
"15576","477 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: A man from Khuzah came, and Ali met him and said: What brought you? He said: I came to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to whom we should pay the charity of our wealth when Allah takes you. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: To Abu Bakr. Then when Allah takes Abu Bakr, to whom? He said: Umar. Then when Allah takes Umar, to whom? He said: To Uthman. He said: Then when Allah takes Uthman, to whom? He said: Look out for yourselves."
"15577","478 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: A man from the desert people came with camels of his, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met him and bought them from him. Then Ali met him and said: What brought you? He said: I came with camels and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought them from me. He said: Did he pay you? He said: No, but I sold them to him on credit. So Ali said: Go back and say to him: O Messenger of Allah, if something happens to you, who will settle my due? And see what he says to you, then come back to me and inform me. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, if something happens to you, who will settle for me? He said: Abu Bakr. So he informed Ali, and he said to him: Go back and ask him: If something happens to Abu Bakr, who will settle for me? So he asked him and he said: Umar. So he came and informed Ali, and he said to him: Go back and ask him: When Umar dies, who will settle for me? So he came and asked him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to you, when Umar dies, if you can die, then die."
"15578","479 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed Zuhr and sat in the mosque when a man came and entered to pray, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will no man give charity to this one and pray with him?"
"15579","480 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: A man announced his lost property in the mosque, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: May Allah not return your lost property to you. And he disliked saying it himself."
"15580","481 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays Jumuah, let him not pray anything after it until he speaks or leaves."
"15581","482 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his eye gouged out, and he said to him: Who struck you? He said: The one-eyed man of Banu so-and-so. So he sent for him and he came, and he said: Did you gouge this one's eye? He said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled blood money against him and said: Do not gouge his eye and leave him sightless."
"15582","483 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: A slave stole in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he pardoned him. Then he was brought a second time having stolen, and he pardoned him. Then he was brought a third time and he pardoned him. Then he was brought a fourth time having stolen and he pardoned him. Then he was brought a fifth time having stolen and he cut his hand. Then he was brought a sixth time and he cut his foot. Then he was brought a seventh time and he cut his hand. Then he was brought an eighth time and he cut his foot. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four for four."
"15583","484 - And with his chain, from Ismah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to begin recitation with All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds, and Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them."
"15584","485 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a spear he would walk with before him, and when he prayed he would fix it before him."
"15585","486 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: A camel belonging to an Ansari orphan ran away from us and we could not catch it, so we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He stood with us until we came to the wall in which the camel was. When the camel saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it came until it prostrated to him. We said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would order us to prostrate to you as is prostrated to kings. He said: That is not in my Ummah; if I were to do so, I would order women to prostrate to their husbands."
"15586","487 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: A group of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we pass through these markets and look at these fruits and desire them, and we have no coin to buy with; is there reward for us in that? He said: Is reward save in that?"
"15587","488 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gifts take away hearing and heart."
"15588","489 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lost property of the believer is the burning of the Fire, three times."
"15589","490 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: When the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who was under Uthman died, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Marry Uthman; if I had a third I would marry her to him, and I married him only by revelation from Allah, mighty and majestic."
"15590","491 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode a horse and it ran with him, then he returned to us and said: I found it like the sea."
"15591","492 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three at whom Allah will not look tomorrow: an old adulterer, a man who takes oaths as merchandise, swearing in every truth and falsehood, and a poor man, arrogant and conceited."
"15592","493 - And with his chain, from Ismah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) employed a man over charity, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, choose for me. He said: Sit in your house."
"15593","494 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib entered the mosque one day and greeted them, and he saw dislike in their faces, so he returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his house and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is it with me that when I enter the mosque I see dislike in the faces of people? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came until he entered the mosque and said: O people, you will not believe and will not be believers until you love Abbas."
"15594","495 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at a man walking in his sandals in the graveyards and said: O wearer of Sibtiyyah sandals, take off your sandals."
"15595","496 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved deed to Allah, mighty and majestic, is the rosary of speech, and the most hateful deeds to Allah is complaining. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the rosary of speech? He said: People conversing while a man glorifies Allah. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what is complaining? He said: People being in good, then the neighbor and companion asks them and they say: We are in evil, complaining."
"15596","497 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever apostatizes from his religion, kill him."
"15597","498 - And with his chain, from Ismah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the Quran were gathered in a leather skin, the Fire would not burn it."
"15598","499 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin told us: Ibrahim ibn Munqidh told us: Idris ibn Yahya told us: al-Fadl ibn al-Mukhtar told us: from Ubaydullah ibn Mawhab, from Ismah ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever endears himself to people with what they love while openly defying Allah will meet Allah Almighty while He is angry with him."
"15599","500 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin told us: Ibrahim ibn Munqidh told us: Idris ibn Yahya told us: al-Fadl ibn al-Mukhtar told us: from Abdullah ibn Mawhab, from Ismah ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has provided sea game for you."
"15600","Ismah ibn Qays al-Sulami. 501 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti told us: My father told us, (Ha). And Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Zakariyya al-Iyadi told us: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti told us: Ismail ibn Ayyash told us: from Safwan ibn Amr, from Azhar ibn Abdullah al-Harazi, from Ismah ibn Qays al-Sulami, a companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to seek refuge in Allah from the trial of the East. It was said to him: How about the trial of the West? He said: That is greater and greater."
